#: src/intro/why-rust.md:3
msgid ""
"Rust is not a better C++ in every respect, and this book does not pretend it"
" is. It makes one trade very clearly: you accept more rules at compile time,"
" and in exchange a whole class of bugs that C++ leaves to code review, "
"sanitizers and luck becomes impossible in safe code. Whether the trade is "
"worth it depends on what you are building. This chapter sets out the "
"benefits, the costs and the situations where each wins."
msgstr ""
"Rust 并不是在所有方面都比 C++ 更好，本书也不假装如此。它做了一个非常明确的取舍：你在编译期接受更多规则，换来的是，一整类在 C++ "
"里只能靠代码审查、sanitizer 和运气来防范的 bug，在安全的 Rust "
"代码中根本不可能出现。这个取舍值不值得，取决于你在做什么。本章列出它的好处、代价，以及各自占上风的场景。"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:10
msgid "What you gain over C++"
msgstr "相比 C++，你得到什么"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:12
msgid ""
"**Memory safety without a garbage collector.** Use-after-free, dangling "
"references, iterator invalidation, double frees and buffer overruns are "
"compile errors or checked panics in safe Rust, not undefined behavior "
"([Ownership](../foundations/ownership.md), "
"[Borrowing](../foundations/borrowing.md)). There is no GC and no runtime to "
"speak of, so the performance model is the one you know from C++: values on "
"the stack, explicit heap allocation, zero-cost abstractions, and no pauses."
msgstr ""
"**不需要垃圾回收的内存安全。** 在安全的 Rust 中，释放后使用、悬垂引用、迭代器失效、重复释放和缓冲区越界，要么是编译错误，要么是受检查的 "
"panic，而不是未定义行为（[所有权](../foundations/ownership.md)、[借用](../foundations/borrowing.md)）。没有"
" GC，也几乎没有运行时，所以性能模型和你在 C++ 中熟悉的一样：值放在栈上，堆分配是显式的，抽象是零成本的，也没有停顿。"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:19
msgid ""
"**Thread safety checked by the compiler.** Sharing data between threads "
"without synchronization does not compile. `Send` and `Sync` make \"this type"
" must stay on the render thread\" a rule the compiler enforces rather than a"
" comment ([Threads, locks and Send/Sync](../systems/concurrency.md))."
msgstr ""
"**由编译器检查的线程安全。** 不加同步就在线程之间共享数据，代码无法编译。`Send` 和 `Sync` "
"让\"这个类型只能留在渲染线程上\"成为编译器强制执行的规则，而不只是一句注释（[线程、锁与 "
"Send/Sync](../systems/concurrency.md)）。"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:23
msgid ""
"**`unsafe` is explicit and local.** When you need raw pointers, FFI or hand-"
"written SIMD, you still have them, inside `unsafe` blocks that mark exactly "
"which lines need careful review ([Unsafe Rust](../systems/unsafe.md))."
msgstr ""
"**`unsafe` 是显式的、局部的。** 需要裸指针、FFI 或手写 SIMD 时，这些能力仍然都在，只是放在 `unsafe` "
"块里，明确标出哪几行需要仔细审查（[Unsafe Rust](../systems/unsafe.md)）。"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:26
msgid ""
"**One toolchain.** Building, dependencies, tests, benchmarks, formatting, "
"linting and documentation are standard and the same in every project ([Tools"
" and the ecosystem](../systems/testing-and-tooling.md)). There is no CMake "
"dialect to learn per project."
msgstr ""
"**一套工具链。** "
"构建、依赖、测试、基准测试、格式化、静态检查和文档都是标准化的，每个项目都一样（[工具与生态](../systems/testing-and-"
"tooling.md)）。不需要为每个项目学一种 CMake 方言。"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:30
msgid ""
"**Package management that works.** Adding a library is one line, built from "
"source with your compiler and flags, with versions pinned in a lock file "
"([crates.io and the ecosystem](../systems/crates-io.md))."
msgstr ""
"**真正好用的包管理。** 添加一个库只需要一行，它会用你的编译器和编译选项从源代码构建，版本锁定在 lock 文件里（[crates.io "
"与生态](../systems/crates-io.md)）。"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:33
msgid ""
"**Errors and absence in the type system.** `Result` and `Option` replace "
"error codes, exceptions and null pointers, and the compiler makes you handle"
" them ([Error handling](../foundations/errors.md))."
msgstr ""
"**错误和\"值不存在\"都在类型系统里。** `Result` 和 `Option` "
"取代了错误码、异常和空指针，而且编译器要求你处理它们（[错误处理](../foundations/errors.md)）。"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:37
msgid "What it costs"
msgstr "代价是什么"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:39
msgid ""
"**The learning curve is real.** The borrow checker rejects some designs that"
" are correct, and some C++ habits, such as object graphs of mutual pointers "
"and long-lived mutable references into containers, have to be replaced with "
"other patterns (indices, handles, arenas). Expect a few weeks of friction "
"before it feels natural. Most of this book exists to shorten that period."
msgstr ""
"**学习曲线是真实存在的。** 借用检查器会拒绝一些其实正确的设计。有些 C++ "
"习惯，比如对象之间互相持有指针的对象图，以及长期持有指向容器内部的可变引用，需要换成其他模式（索引、句柄、arena）。在它变得自然之前，预计会有几周的磨合期。本书的大部分内容就是为了缩短这段时间。"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:45
msgid ""
"**Compile times.** A clean build of a large Rust project is comparable to a "
"large C++ project with heavy templates. Incremental builds and `cargo check`"
" help; the [Project organization](../foundations/project-organization.md) "
"chapter covers how to structure crates so builds stay fast."
msgstr ""
"**编译时间。** 大型 Rust 项目的完整构建时间，和大量使用模板的大型 C++ 项目相当。增量构建和 `cargo check` "
"会有帮助；[项目组织](../foundations/project-organization.md)一章讲了如何组织 crate，让构建保持快速。"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:49
msgid ""
"**A younger game and graphics ecosystem.** There is no Unreal or Unity. Rust"
" engines such as Bevy and Fyrox are capable but young, console SDKs and "
"platform middleware are C and C++ first, and most GPU compute (CUDA kernels,"
" vendor libraries) is still written in C++. You can call all of it through "
"FFI, but someone has to write and maintain the bindings."
msgstr ""
"**游戏和图形生态更年轻。** 没有 Unreal，也没有 Unity。Bevy 和 Fyrox 等 Rust 引擎能力不错，但还年轻；主机 SDK "
"和平台中间件优先支持 C 和 C++；大多数 GPU 计算（CUDA kernel、厂商的库）仍然用 C++ 编写。这些都可以通过 FFI "
"调用，但总得有人编写和维护绑定。"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:54
msgid ""
"**Interop with existing C++ has a cost.** Rust talks to C easily and to C++ "
"through a C layer or generated bindings. Templates, exceptions and C++ "
"classes do not cross the boundary directly ([FFI with C and "
"C++](../systems/ffi.md))."
msgstr ""
"**和现有 C++ 代码互操作是有成本的。** Rust 调用 C 很容易，调用 C++ 则要通过一层 C 接口或生成的绑定。模板、异常和 C++ "
"类都不能直接跨越这个边界（[与 C 和 C++ 的 FFI](../systems/ffi.md)）。"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:58
msgid ""
"**No stable ABI between Rust crates.** You cannot ship a closed-source Rust "
"library for other Rust code to link; you ship source, or a C ABI."
msgstr ""
"**Rust crate 之间没有稳定的 ABI。** 你不能发布一个闭源的 Rust 库给其他 Rust 代码链接；只能发布源代码，或者提供 C "
"ABI。"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:60
msgid ""
"**Smaller hiring pool.** Fewer engineers have shipped Rust in production "
"than C++, especially in games."
msgstr "**招聘范围更小。** 在生产环境中交付过 Rust 的工程师比 C++ 少，在游戏行业尤其如此。"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:63
msgid "Rust and AI-assisted development"
msgstr "Rust 与 AI 辅助开发"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:65
msgid ""
"More and more code is written with an AI assistant or by an agent, and "
"reviewed by a person. Rust's strictness, which feels like a cost when you "
"write every line yourself, becomes useful when you are reviewing code you "
"did not write:"
msgstr ""
"越来越多的代码由 AI 助手协助编写，或由 agent 生成，再由人来审查。Rust "
"的严格，在每一行都自己写的时候像是一种代价；但当你审查不是自己写的代码时，它就变得很有用："

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:70
msgid ""
"**The compiler checks what you would otherwise have to review.** Code "
"generated in C++ can compile cleanly and still contain a lifetime bug that "
"shows up weeks later as a crash. The same mistake in Rust is a compile "
"error, before anyone reads the code:"
msgstr ""
"**编译器替你检查本来需要人工审查的东西。** 用 C++ 生成的代码可能干净地通过编译，却仍然藏着一个生命周期 "
"bug，几周后才以崩溃的形式出现。同样的错误在 Rust 里是编译错误，在任何人读代码之前就被拦下了："

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:78
msgid "\"boss\""
msgstr ""

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:78
msgid "// may reallocate: `first` would dangle\n"
msgstr "// 可能重新分配内存：`first` 会变成悬垂引用\n"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:79
msgid "// error[E0502]: cannot borrow `*enemies` as mutable\n"
msgstr "// error[E0502]：不能以可变方式借用 `*enemies`\n"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:83
msgid ""
"**Error messages an agent can act on.** Rust's compiler errors name the "
"problem, point at the exact span and usually suggest a fix. An agent that "
"builds, reads the error and edits in a loop converges much faster than one "
"that has to interpret a page of template instantiation errors, or a crash at"
" run time."
msgstr ""
"**agent 能据此行动的错误信息。** Rust "
"的编译错误会指出问题是什么，标出确切的代码位置，通常还会给出修复建议。一个\"构建、读错误、修改\"循环工作的 "
"agent，比起要解读一整页模板实例化错误或运行时崩溃的 agent，收敛得快得多。"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:88
msgid ""
"**One way to build, test and lint.** `cargo build`, `cargo test`, `cargo "
"clippy` and `cargo fmt` work the same in every repository, so an agent does "
"not need project-specific instructions to verify its own work."
msgstr ""
"**统一的构建、测试和检查方式。** `cargo build`、`cargo test`、`cargo clippy` 和 `cargo fmt` "
"在每个仓库里都一样，所以 agent 不需要针对具体项目的说明，就能验证自己的工作。"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:91
msgid ""
"**Explicit contracts are easier to review.** Function signatures say who "
"owns what, which errors can occur and what may be absent. An exhaustive "
"`match` means a new enum variant cannot be silently ignored. A reviewer can "
"check intent from the signature instead of tracing the whole body."
msgstr ""
"**明确的契约更容易审查。** 函数签名说明了谁拥有什么、可能出现哪些错误、什么可能不存在。穷尽的 `match` "
"意味着新增的枚举变体不会被悄悄忽略。审查者可以从签名判断意图，而不必追踪整个函数体。"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:95
msgid ""
"**Rust is part of the AI stack itself.** Hugging Face's `tokenizers`, "
"inference frameworks such as `candle`, and many fast Python extensions "
"(built with PyO3, like Polars) are written in Rust. Systems work around "
"models, such as inference servers, data pipelines and tools that run next to"
" Python, is a common place for Rust today."
msgstr ""
"**Rust 本身就是 AI 技术栈的一部分。** Hugging Face 的 `tokenizers`、`candle` "
"等推理框架，以及许多高性能的 Python 扩展（用 PyO3 构建，比如 Polars）都是用 Rust "
"编写的。围绕模型的系统工作，比如推理服务、数据管线，以及和 Python 配合运行的工具，是如今 Rust 的常见用武之地。"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:101
msgid ""
"The honest caveat: models still produce Rust that does not compile, "
"especially around lifetimes and async code, and there is less Rust than C++ "
"or Python in their training data. The benefit is not that generated Rust is "
"correct the first time. It is that many of its mistakes are caught by the "
"compiler instead of by your users."
msgstr ""
"需要坦白的是：模型仍然会写出无法编译的 Rust，尤其是在生命周期和异步代码上；而且它们训练数据中的 Rust 也比 C++ 和 Python "
"少。好处并不在于生成的 Rust 一次就正确，而在于它的许多错误会被编译器发现，而不是被你的用户发现。"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:107
msgid "When to choose it"
msgstr "什么时候选择它"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:109
msgid "Situation"
msgstr "场景"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:109
msgid "Choice"
msgstr "选择"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:111
msgid ""
"A new tool, service or pipeline: asset processing, build tools, servers, "
"editors"
msgstr "新的工具、服务或管线：资源处理、构建工具、服务器、编辑器"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:111
msgid ""
"**Rust.** Safety and tooling pay off immediately, and there is no legacy "
"code to bind to"
msgstr "**Rust。** 安全性和工具链立刻见效，也没有需要绑定的遗留代码"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:112
msgid ""
"Code that parses untrusted input: network protocols, file formats, mods, "
"save files"
msgstr "解析不可信输入的代码：网络协议、文件格式、mod、存档"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:112
msgid "**Rust.** The classic source of security bugs in C++"
msgstr "**Rust。** 这是 C++ 安全漏洞的典型来源"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:113
msgid "Heavily multithreaded systems: job systems, streaming, networking"
msgstr "重度多线程的系统：任务系统、流式加载、网络"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:113
msgid "**Rust.** Data races are compile errors"
msgstr "**Rust。** 数据竞争是编译错误"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:114
msgid "A new subsystem inside an existing C++ engine"
msgstr "现有 C++ 引擎中的新子系统"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:114
msgid ""
"**Rust behind a C API** can work well for self-contained parts (a physics "
"step, an audio mixer, a parser). Budget for the FFI layer"
msgstr "对于相对独立的部分（物理步进、音频混音器、解析器），**用 C API 包装的 Rust** 可以很好地工作。要为 FFI 层留出预算"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:115
msgid "A large existing C++ engine and codebase"
msgstr "大型的现有 C++ 引擎和代码库"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:115
msgid ""
"**C++.** Rewriting is rarely worth it. Add Rust at the edges, if at all"
msgstr "**C++。** 重写很少值得。如果要用 Rust，就从边缘开始"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:116
msgid "A console-first title, or one built on Unreal or Unity"
msgstr "以主机平台为主的项目，或基于 Unreal 或 Unity 的项目"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:116
msgid "**C++ (or C#).** The platform tools and middleware assume them"
msgstr "**C++（或 C#）。** 平台工具和中间件都以它们为前提"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:117
msgid "CUDA kernels and GPU compute libraries"
msgstr "CUDA kernel 和 GPU 计算库"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:117
msgid ""
"**C++** for the kernels. Rust can drive them through FFI or use wgpu compute"
" for portable cases"
msgstr "kernel 用 **C++**。Rust 可以通过 FFI 驱动它们，可移植的场景也可以用 wgpu 计算"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:118
msgid "A tight deadline with a team that knows only C++"
msgstr "工期紧张，而团队只熟悉 C++"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:118
msgid "**C++.** Learn Rust on a tool or side project first"
msgstr "**C++。** 先在工具或业余项目上学习 Rust"

#: src/intro/why-rust.md:120
msgid ""
"A common path for engine teams is to start with tools and services, where "
"Rust's disadvantages matter least, and move closer to the runtime as "
"experience and bindings accumulate. The rest of this book follows the same "
"order: the language first, then tools and systems programming, then graphics"
" and engine code."
msgstr ""
"引擎团队常见的路径是：先从工具和服务开始，那里 Rust "
"的劣势影响最小，再随着经验和绑定的积累，逐步靠近运行时。本书的其余部分也按同样的顺序展开：先是语言本身，然后是工具和系统编程，最后是图形和引擎代码。"

#: src/intro/how-to-read.md:3
msgid ""
"Read Part I in order. Ownership, borrowing and lifetimes build on each "
"other, and most of Rust's surprises for a C++ programmer are in those three "
"chapters. Read Part II before you start a real project: it covers tests, "
"tooling, logging and dependencies. After that, Part III and Part IV can be "
"read in any order; each chapter links back to what it relies on."
msgstr ""
"请按顺序阅读第一部分。所有权、借用和生命周期这三章层层递进，Rust 给 C++ "
"程序员的大部分意外都集中在这里。开始一个真正的项目之前，请先读第二部分：它讲的是测试、工具、日志和依赖。之后，第三部分和第四部分可以按任意顺序阅读；每一章都会链接到它所依赖的内容。"

#: src/intro/how-to-read.md:9
msgid "Conventions"
msgstr "约定"

#: src/intro/how-to-read.md:11
msgid ""
"Side-by-side code shows the C++ you would write next to the Rust equivalent:"
msgstr "并排的代码会把你会写的 C++ 和对应的 Rust 放在一起："

