#: src/intro/syntax.md:119
msgid ""
"**`derive` is a built-in attribute whose arguments are macros.** Each name "
"in `#[derive(...)]` is a derive macro that generates an `impl` of the trait "
"with the same name. `#[derive(Clone)]` on `struct Vec2 { x: f32, y: f32 }` "
"writes roughly `impl Clone for Vec2 { fn clone(&self) -> Self { Vec2 { x: "
"self.x.clone(), y: self.y.clone() } } }`. The standard derives (`Debug`, "
"`Clone`, `Copy`, `PartialEq`, `Eq`, `PartialOrd`, `Ord`, `Hash`, `Default`) "
"are in the prelude, so they need no import. A crate's derive usually has the"
" same name as its trait, and one `use serde::Serialize;` imports both."
msgstr ""
"**`derive` 是一个内置属性，它的参数是宏。** `#[derive(...)]` 里的每个名字都是一个 derive 宏，它会为同名的 "
"trait 生成一个 `impl`。把 `#[derive(Clone)]` 加在 `struct Vec2 { x: f32, y: f32 }` "
"上，大致会生成 `impl Clone for Vec2 { fn clone(&self) -> Self { Vec2 { x: "
"self.x.clone(), y: self.y.clone() } } }`。标准的 "
"derive（`Debug`、`Clone`、`Copy`、`PartialEq`、`Eq`、`PartialOrd`、`Ord`、`Hash`、`Default`）都在"
" prelude 里，不需要导入。crate 提供的 derive 通常和它的 trait 同名，一句 `use serde::Serialize;` "
"会同时导入两者。"

#: src/intro/syntax.md:128
msgid ""
"**`repr` is built in** and controls memory layout: `#[repr(C)]` for "
"C-compatible structs, `#[repr(u8)]` for an enum's tag, `#[repr(align(64))]` "
"for alignment ([Memory layout and performance](../systems/memory-and-"
"performance.md))."
msgstr ""
"**`repr` 是内置的**，用来控制内存布局：`#[repr(C)]` 用于与 C 兼容的结构体，`#[repr(u8)]` "
"指定枚举标签的类型，`#[repr(align(64))]` 指定对齐（[内存布局与性能](../systems/memory-and-"
"performance.md)）。"

#: src/intro/syntax.md:132
msgid ""
"**Placement.** `#[attr]` applies to the item, field, statement or expression"
" that follows it. `#![attr]` applies to the item it is written inside, and "
"must come first there: at the top of `lib.rs` or `main.rs` it applies to the"
" whole crate."
msgstr ""
"**放置位置。** `#[attr]` 作用于紧随其后的条目、字段、语句或表达式。`#![attr]` 作用于它所在的条目，并且必须写在最前面：写在 "
"`lib.rs` 或 `main.rs` 顶部时，它作用于整个 crate。"

