#: src/intro/syntax.md:439
msgid ""
"**`&` is visible at the call site.** C++ hides pass-by-reference in the "
"callee's signature. In Rust, `update(&mut player)` tells the reader at the "
"call that `player` may change."
msgstr ""
"**`&` 在调用处可见。** C++ 把按引用传参藏在被调用函数的签名里。在 Rust 中，`update(&mut player)` "
"在调用处就告诉读者 `player` 可能会被修改；"

#: src/intro/syntax.md:442
msgid ""
"**There is no `->`** for member access. `.` works on values, references and "
"smart pointers alike."
msgstr "**没有用于成员访问的 `->`。** `.` 对值、引用和智能指针都一样适用；"

#: src/intro/syntax.md:444
msgid ""
"**`!` after a name is a macro**, not negation. Macros can take any syntax "
"inside their brackets, which is how `vec![0; 100]` and `println!(\"{x}\")` "
"work."
msgstr ""
"**名字后面的 `!` 表示宏**，而不是取反。宏的括号内可以接受任意语法，`vec![0; 100]` 和 `println!(\"{x}\")` "
"就是这样工作的；"

#: src/intro/syntax.md:446
msgid "**`?` is error propagation**, not a conditional."
msgstr "**`?` 是错误传播**，而不是条件运算；"

#: src/intro/syntax.md:447
msgid "**`'` starts a lifetime** unless it closes again one character later."
msgstr "**`'` 开始一个生命周期**，除非它在一个字符之后再次闭合；"

#: src/intro/syntax.md:448
msgid ""
"**`|` starts a closure** at the beginning of an expression, and means \"or\""
" in patterns and between two values."
msgstr "**`|` 在表达式开头时开始一个闭包**，在模式中以及两个值之间表示\"或\"；"

#: src/intro/syntax.md:450
msgid ""
"**`::<>` is only needed in expressions.** In a type position you write "
"`Vec<u32>`, as in C++."
msgstr "**`::<>` 只在表达式中需要。** 在类型位置上，你像 C++ 一样写 `Vec<u32>`。"

#: src/intro/syntax.md:456
msgid ""
"Your editor can fill in a lot of this for you. rust-analyzer shows inferred "
"types, parameter names and the lifetimes the compiler elided as inline "
"hints, and hovering a macro shows its expansion. While you learn, turn the "
"hints on."
msgstr ""
"你的编辑器可以替你补上很多信息。rust-analyzer "
"会以内联提示的形式显示推断出的类型、参数名以及编译器省略的生命周期，把鼠标悬停在宏上还能看到它的展开结果。学习期间，请打开这些提示。"

#: src/intro/syntax.md:464
msgid ""
"In the program at the top, remove the `?` from `parse_level` and read the "
"compiler error. What type does `parse` return?"
msgstr "在开头的程序中，去掉 `parse_level` 里的 `?`，阅读编译器错误。`parse` 返回的是什么类型？"

#: src/intro/syntax.md:466
msgid ""
"Change `0..scores.len()` to `0..=scores.len()`. What happens when you run "
"it, and why does Rust stop instead of reading past the end?"
msgstr ""
"把 `0..scores.len()` 改为 `0..=scores.len()`。运行时会发生什么？为什么 Rust 会停下来，而不是读到末尾之外？"

#: src/intro/syntax.md:468
msgid ""
"Write `let n = \"42\".parse().unwrap();` without a type anywhere. Fix the "
"error twice: once with a type on `n`, once with the turbofish."
msgstr ""
"写出 `let n = \"42\".parse().unwrap();`，不在任何地方标注类型。用两种方式修复这个错误：一次在 `n` "
"上标注类型，一次使用 turbofish。"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:3
msgid ""
"In C++, the language standard says nothing about how code is built. Every "
"project chooses a build system, a package manager, a directory layout and a "
"way to find headers and libraries, and connecting two projects means "
"reconciling their choices. Rust settled all of this from the start. One "
"tool, Cargo, builds every Rust project, and every library is published the "
"same way. This is the biggest day-to-day productivity difference you will "
"notice."
msgstr ""
"在 C++ "
"中，语言标准对代码如何构建只字未提。每个项目都要自己选择构建系统、包管理器、目录结构以及查找头文件和库的方式；要把两个项目连接起来，就得协调双方的选择。Rust"
" 从一开始就把这些都定了下来：一个工具 Cargo 构建所有 Rust 项目，所有库都以同样的方式发布。这是你在日常工作中会感受到的最大的效率差别。"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:12
msgid "crates, the unit of compilation, and why there are no headers,"
msgstr "crate：编译的基本单位，以及为什么没有头文件；"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:13
msgid "`Cargo.toml` compared with `CMakeLists.txt`,"
msgstr "`Cargo.toml` 与 `CMakeLists.txt` 的对比；"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:14
msgid "dependencies, versions and the lock file,"
msgstr "依赖、版本与锁文件；"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:15
msgid "features, the replacement for `#ifdef` and CMake options,"
msgstr "feature：`#ifdef` 和 CMake 选项的替代品；"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:16
msgid "build profiles and optimization settings,"
msgstr "构建配置（profile）与优化设置；"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:17
msgid "what gets linked, and how,"
msgstr "最终链接了什么，以及如何链接；"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:18
msgid "workspaces for large codebases."
msgstr "用于大型代码库的工作区（workspace）。"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:20
msgid "Crates: the unit of compilation"
msgstr "crate：编译的基本单位"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:22
msgid ""
"In C++ the compiler sees one **translation unit** at a time: a `.cpp` file "
"with all its headers pasted in. The linker stitches the object files "
"together afterwards, and headers exist so each translation unit can know the"
" declarations of the others."
msgstr ""
"在 C++ 中，编译器一次只看到一个**翻译单元**：一个 `.cpp` "
"文件加上粘贴进来的所有头文件。之后由链接器把目标文件拼接起来；头文件的存在，是为了让每个翻译单元知道其他翻译单元里的声明。"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:27
msgid ""
"In Rust the compiler sees a whole **crate** at a time. A crate is a tree of "
"modules (source files) compiled together into one library or executable. "
"Since the compiler sees every file of the crate at once, there is nothing to"
" declare in advance:"
msgstr ""
"在 Rust 中，编译器一次看到整个 **crate**。crate 是一棵模块（源文件）树，被一起编译成一个库或可执行文件。由于编译器能同时看到 "
"crate 的每个文件，就不需要任何提前声明："

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:32
msgid "no header files and no forward declarations,"
msgstr "没有头文件，也没有前置声明；"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:33
msgid "no include guards or `#pragma once`,"
msgstr "没有 include 守卫，也没有 `#pragma once`；"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:34
msgid "functions and types can be used before they are defined, in any order,"
msgstr "函数和类型可以在定义之前使用，顺序随意；"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:35
msgid ""
"no One Definition Rule to violate, because each item is defined in exactly "
"one place."
msgstr "不存在会被违反的单一定义规则（ODR），因为每个条目只在一个地方定义。"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:38
msgid ""
"When crate `game` depends on crate `math`, the compiler reads `math`'s "
"compiled metadata (an `.rlib` file), which contains its public API, generic "
"function bodies and inlinable code. That metadata plays the role of headers,"
" but it is generated by the compiler, so it can never disagree with the "
"implementation."
msgstr ""
"当 crate `game` 依赖 crate `math` 时，编译器读取 `math` 编译后的元数据（一个 `.rlib` "
"文件），其中包含它的公开 API、泛型函数体和可内联的代码。这些元数据扮演了头文件的角色，但它由编译器生成，所以永远不会与实现不一致。"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:46
msgid "Translation unit (`.cpp` + headers)"
msgstr "翻译单元（`.cpp` + 头文件）"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:46
msgid "Crate (a tree of `.rs` modules)"
msgstr "crate（由 `.rs` 模块组成的树）"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:47
msgid "Header file"
msgstr "头文件"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:47
msgid "Nothing; the compiler reads dependency metadata"
msgstr "不需要；编译器读取依赖的元数据"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:48
msgid "Static library `.a`/`.lib`"
msgstr "静态库 `.a`/`.lib`"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:48
msgid "Library crate (`.rlib`)"
msgstr "库 crate（`.rlib`）"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:49
msgid "Executable target"
msgstr "可执行目标"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:49
msgid "Binary crate"
msgstr "二进制 crate"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:50
msgid "CMake project"
msgstr "CMake 项目"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:50
msgid "Cargo package"
msgstr "Cargo 包（package）"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:51
msgid "vcpkg / Conan package"
msgstr "vcpkg / Conan 包"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:51
msgid "Crate on [crates.io](https://crates.io)"
msgstr "[crates.io](https://crates.io) 上的 crate"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:53
msgid ""
"A **package** is a directory with a `Cargo.toml`. It contains at most one "
"library crate (`src/lib.rs`) and any number of binary crates (`src/main.rs`,"
" `src/bin/*.rs`), plus tests, examples and benchmarks."
msgstr ""
"**包**（package）是一个带有 `Cargo.toml` 的目录。它最多包含一个库 crate（`src/lib.rs`）和任意多个二进制 "
"crate（`src/main.rs`、`src/bin/*.rs`），外加测试、示例和基准测试。"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:57 src/foundations/cargo.md:86
msgid "Cargo.toml"
msgstr "Cargo.toml"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:62
msgid "CMakeLists.txt"
msgstr "CMakeLists.txt"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:64
msgid ""
"```cmake\n"
"cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.20)\n"
"project(viewer VERSION 0.1.0 LANGUAGES CXX)\n"
"set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 17)\n"
"\n"
"find_package(glfw3 3.3 REQUIRED)\n"
"find_package(glm REQUIRED)\n"
"\n"
"option(VIEWER_HOT_RELOAD \"Hot reload\" OFF)\n"
"\n"
"add_executable(viewer src/main.cpp\n"
"                      src/renderer.cpp)\n"
"target_link_libraries(viewer glfw glm::glm)\n"
"if(VIEWER_HOT_RELOAD)\n"
"  target_compile_definitions(viewer\n"
"    PRIVATE HOT_RELOAD=1)\n"
"endif()\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:88
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[package]\n"
"name = \"viewer\"\n"
"version = \"0.1.0\"\n"
"edition = \"2024\"\n"
"\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"winit = \"0.30\"\n"
"glam = \"0.30\"\n"
"\n"
"[features]\n"
"hot-reload = []\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:105
msgid ""
"There is no list of source files: Cargo finds `src/main.rs` and the compiler"
" follows `mod` declarations from there. The `edition` selects a language "
"edition (2015, 2018, 2021, 2024), similar to `-std=c++17`, except that "
"crates of different editions link together freely. An edition can change "
"syntax and defaults, but never the ABI or the standard library."
msgstr ""
"这里没有源文件列表：Cargo 会找到 `src/main.rs`，编译器再沿着 `mod` 声明找到其余文件。`edition` "
"选择语言版本（2015、2018、2021、2024），类似于 `-std=c++17`，不同的是不同版本的 crate "
"可以自由地链接在一起。版本可以改变语法和默认行为，但绝不会改变 ABI 或标准库。"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:111
msgid "Dependencies and versions"
msgstr "依赖与版本"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:113
msgid ""
"Dependencies come from [crates.io](https://crates.io) by default, but can "
"also come from Git or a local path:"
msgstr "依赖默认来自 [crates.io](https://crates.io)，也可以来自 Git 或本地路径："

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:116
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"glam = \"0.30\"                                 # crates.io, semver-compatible with 0.30.x\n"
"serde = { version = \"1\", features = [\"derive\"] }\n"
"ash = { version = \"0.38\", default-features = false, features = [\"loaded\"] }\n"
"my-math = { path = \"../my-math\" }             # a local crate\n"
"imgui-backend = { git = \"https://github.com/example/imgui-backend\", rev = \"4f2a1c9\" }\n"
"\n"
"[dev-dependencies]   # only for tests, examples and benchmarks\n"
"criterion = \"0.5\"\n"
"\n"
"[build-dependencies] # only for build.rs\n"
"cc = \"1\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:131
msgid ""
"Version requirements follow [semantic versioning](https://semver.org): "
"`\"0.30\"` means \"any 0.30.x\", and `\"1.4\"` means \"1.4.0 or newer, but "
"below 2.0\". The first build resolves exact versions and records them in "
"`Cargo.lock`. Commit `Cargo.lock` for applications so every build uses "
"identical dependencies; `cargo update` moves to newer compatible versions "
"deliberately."
msgstr ""
"版本要求遵循[语义化版本](https://semver.org)：`\"0.30\"` 表示“任意 0.30.x”，`\"1.4\"` "
"表示“1.4.0 或更新，但低于 2.0”。第一次构建会解析出确切的版本并记录在 `Cargo.lock` 中。对于应用程序，请提交 "
"`Cargo.lock`，让每次构建都使用完全相同的依赖；用 `cargo update` 有意识地升级到兼容的新版本。"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:137
msgid ""
"How Cargo resolves versions and features, how to choose and vet crates, and "
"how to publish your own are covered in [crates.io and the "
"ecosystem](../systems/crates-io.md)."
msgstr ""
"Cargo 如何解析版本和 feature、如何挑选和审查 crate、如何发布自己的 crate，见 [crates.io "
"与生态](../systems/crates-io.md)。"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:141
msgid ""
"Cargo downloads, builds and links dependencies from source with _your_ "
"compiler and _your_ flags. There are no prebuilt binaries to mismatch: no "
"\"this library was built with a different `_ITERATOR_DEBUG_LEVEL`\", no "
"runtime library conflicts, no missing `.lib` for your compiler version."
msgstr ""
"Cargo "
"用<em>你的</em>编译器和<em>你的</em>编译选项从源码下载、构建并链接依赖。不存在不匹配的预编译二进制：不会有“这个库是用不同的 "
"`_ITERATOR_DEBUG_LEVEL` 构建的”，不会有运行时库冲突，也不会缺少对应你编译器版本的 `.lib`。"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:149
msgid ""
"If two of your dependencies need incompatible versions of a crate (say "
"`rand` 0.8 and `rand` 0.9), Cargo builds and links _both_. Symbols are "
"mangled with a hash of the crate's identity, so there is no clash. Types "
"from the two versions are distinct types, so you cannot accidentally pass "
"one to the other. In C++ the same situation is an ODR violation that the "
"linker may or may not catch."
msgstr ""
"如果你的两个依赖需要某个 crate 的不兼容版本（比如 `rand` 0.8 和 `rand` 0.9），Cargo "
"会把<em>两个版本</em>都构建并链接进来。符号名经过修饰，带有 crate "
"身份的哈希值，所以不会冲突。两个版本中的类型是不同的类型，你不会意外地把一个传给另一个。在 C++ 中，同样的情况就是违反 "
"ODR，链接器可能发现也可能发现不了。"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:158
msgid "Features: conditional compilation"
msgstr "feature：条件编译"

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:160
msgid ""
"**Features** are named, additive switches declared by a crate, used where "
"C++ uses preprocessor definitions and CMake options:"
msgstr "**feature** 是 crate 声明的、具名的、可叠加的开关，用于 C++ 中使用预处理器定义和 CMake 选项的场合："

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:163
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[features]\n"
"default = [\"png\"]\n"
"png = [\"dep:png\"]          # enabling \"png\" pulls in the optional dependency\n"
"hot-reload = []\n"
"vulkan = [\"dep:ash\"]\n"
"\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"png = { version = \"0.17\", optional = true }\n"
"ash = { version = \"0.38\", optional = true }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/foundations/cargo.md:175
msgid ""
"In code, `#[cfg(...)]` includes or removes an item, like `#if` but on whole "
"syntax items rather than text:"
msgstr "在代码中，`#[cfg(...)]` 会保留或移除一个条目，类似 `#if`，但作用于完整的语法条目而不是文本："

