#: src/foundations/values-and-types.md:3
msgid ""
"Rust's basic types look like C's, and they compile to the same machine "
"representation. The differences are in the rules around them: no implicit "
"conversions, defined overflow behavior, immutability by default, and a "
"compiler that is free to reorder struct fields unless you ask it not to. "
"This chapter walks through the types you will use in every program and how "
"they are laid out in memory."
msgstr ""
"Rust 的基本类型看起来和 C "
"的一样，编译后的机器表示也相同。区别在于围绕它们的规则：没有隐式转换，溢出行为有明确定义，默认不可变，而且除非你明确要求，编译器可以自由地重排结构体字段。本章介绍每个程序都会用到的类型，以及它们在内存中的布局。"

