#: src/foundations/values-and-types.md:24
msgid ""
"`let` is the only way to declare a local variable, and the type is inferred "
"unless you write it. Variables are immutable unless declared `mut`. That "
"reverses C++'s default, where you add `const` to opt out of mutability. In "
"practice most locals in Rust code are immutable, and `mut` flags the few "
"that change."
msgstr ""
"`let` 是声明局部变量的唯一方式，除非你写出类型，否则类型由编译器推断。变量默认不可变，除非声明为 `mut`。这与 C++ 的默认相反：在 C++"
" 中你要加上 `const` 才能放弃可变性。实践中，Rust 代码里的大多数局部变量都是不可变的，`mut` 标出了少数会改变的那些。"

