#: src/foundations/values-and-types.md:243
msgid "Things that are different from C++ classes:"
msgstr "与 C++ 类的不同之处："

#: src/foundations/values-and-types.md:245
msgid ""
"**No constructors.** A struct literal must set every field, so there is no "
"such thing as an uninitialized member. By convention a function called `new`"
" builds the value, and `Default` (`#[derive(Default)]`) provides a zero-ish "
"default."
msgstr ""
"**没有构造函数。** 结构体字面量必须为每个字段赋值，所以不存在未初始化的成员。按惯例，名为 `new` "
"的函数负责构造值，`Default`（`#[derive(Default)]`）提供一个近似“零值”的默认值。"

#: src/foundations/values-and-types.md:249
msgid ""
"**No inheritance**, no `virtual`, no `protected`. Behavior is shared through"
" traits ([Traits and generics](traits-and-generics.md))."
msgstr ""
"**没有继承**，没有 `virtual`，没有 `protected`。行为通过 trait 共享（参见 [Trait 与泛型](traits-"
"and-generics.md)）。"

#: src/foundations/values-and-types.md:251
msgid ""
"**Methods live in `impl` blocks**, separate from the data. A type can have "
"several `impl` blocks, even in different files of the same crate."
msgstr "**方法放在 `impl` 块中**，与数据分开。一个类型可以有多个 `impl` 块，甚至可以分布在同一 crate 的不同文件中。"

#: src/foundations/values-and-types.md:253
msgid ""
"**`#[derive(...)]`** generates common trait implementations: `Debug` "
"(printing), `Clone`, `Copy`, `PartialEq`, `Hash`, `Default`, and more. It is"
" the replacement for writing boilerplate operators by hand."
msgstr ""
"**`#[derive(...)]`** 会生成常用 trait "
"的实现：`Debug`（打印）、`Clone`、`Copy`、`PartialEq`、`Hash`、`Default` "
"等等。它取代了手写样板运算符的做法。"

#: src/foundations/values-and-types.md:257
msgid ""
"**Newtypes** like `EntityId(u32)` cost nothing at run time, and the compiler"
" will refuse to pass an `EntityId` where a `TextureId(u32)` is expected. Use"
" them generously for IDs, handles and units."
msgstr ""
"像 `EntityId(u32)` 这样的 **newtype** 在运行时没有任何开销，而编译器会拒绝在需要 `TextureId(u32)` "
"的地方传入 `EntityId`。对 ID、句柄和单位，请大方地使用它们。"

#: src/foundations/values-and-types.md:261
#: src/foundations/enums-and-match.md:224
msgid "Memory layout"
msgstr "内存布局"

#: src/foundations/values-and-types.md:263
msgid ""
"Rust gives you exactly the layout control you have in C, but the **default**"
" is different:"
msgstr "Rust 给你的布局控制能力和 C 完全一样，但**默认值**不同："

#: src/foundations/values-and-types.md:266
msgid ""
"Without an attribute (`repr(Rust)`), the compiler may **reorder fields** to "
"minimize padding. Field order in the source does not determine order in "
"memory, and the layout is not stable between compiler versions."
msgstr ""
"不加属性时（`repr(Rust)`），编译器可以**重排字段**以减少填充。源码中的字段顺序并不决定内存中的顺序，而且布局在不同编译器版本之间并不稳定。"

#: src/foundations/values-and-types.md:269
msgid ""
"`#[repr(C)]` lays fields out in declaration order with C's padding rules, "
"exactly like the equivalent C struct. Use it for anything that crosses a "
"boundary: GPU buffers, files, network packets, FFI."
msgstr ""
