msgid "Local variables are dropped in reverse order of declaration, like C++."
msgstr "局部变量按声明的相反顺序丢弃，和 C++ 一样。"

#: src/foundations/ownership.md:206
msgid ""
"Struct fields are dropped in **declaration order**, which is the opposite of"
" C++ (members are destroyed in reverse). This rarely matters, but it does "
"when one field must outlive another, for example a Vulkan device and the "
"objects created from it. Put the dependent objects first, or wrap the order-"
"sensitive part in an explicit `Drop` for the parent struct."
msgstr ""
"结构体字段按**声明顺序**丢弃，这与 C++ 相反（C++ 的成员按逆序析构）。这一点很少有影响，但当一个字段必须比另一个活得更久时就很重要，例如 "
"Vulkan 设备和由它创建的对象。请把依赖它的对象放在前面，或者为父结构体显式实现 `Drop`，把对顺序敏感的部分包起来。"

#: src/foundations/ownership.md:211
msgid ""
"`drop(x)` is not special. It is an ordinary function that takes its argument"
" by value and does nothing, so the value is dropped when it returns."
msgstr "`drop(x)` 并不特殊。它只是一个按值接收参数、什么也不做的普通函数，所以值在它返回时被丢弃。"

#: src/foundations/ownership.md:217
msgid "What if a value is moved on only one branch?"
msgstr "如果一个值只在某个分支上被移动了呢？"

#: src/foundations/ownership.md:224
msgid "// is `v` dropped here?\n"
msgstr "// `v` 在这里会被丢弃吗？\n"

#: src/foundations/ownership.md:229
msgid ""
"The compiler adds a hidden boolean \"drop flag\" on the stack, sets it when "
"`v` is moved, and checks it at the end of scope. This is the only runtime "
"cost of ownership tracking, and it only appears when moves are conditional."
msgstr ""
"编译器会在栈上添加一个隐藏的布尔“丢弃标志”，在 `v` "
"被移动时设置它，并在作用域结束时检查它。这是所有权追踪唯一的运行时开销，而且只在有条件的移动中才会出现。"

