"`std::mem::forget`，并想想它为什么按值接收 `self`。"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:3
msgid ""
"Moving ownership every time a function needs to look at a value would be "
"unworkable. Most of the time you want what C++ gives you with `const T&` and"
" `T&`: access without ownership. Rust calls this **borrowing**, and its "
"references look like C++ references with one big addition: the compiler "
"checks that a reference can never outlive what it points to, and that nobody"
" modifies data while someone else is reading it."
msgstr ""
"每当函数需要查看一个值时就转移所有权，这是行不通的。大多数时候，你想要的是 C++ 中 `const T&` 和 `T&` "
"提供的东西：不拥有、只访问。Rust 称之为**借用**，它的引用看起来很像 C++ "
"的引用，只是多了一项重要保证：编译器会检查引用绝不会比它指向的东西活得更久，并且在有人读取数据时没有人能修改它。"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:12
msgid "the two kinds of reference and the one rule that governs them,"
msgstr "两种引用，以及支配它们的唯一规则；"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:13
msgid "why that rule rules out iterator and reference invalidation,"
msgstr "为什么这条规则排除了迭代器失效和引用失效；"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:14
msgid "how long a borrow lasts,"
msgstr "一次借用持续多久；"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:15
msgid "slices, the safe `std::span`,"
msgstr "切片：安全的 `std::span`；"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:16
msgid "what the rule buys the optimizer,"
msgstr "这条规则给优化器带来了什么；"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:17
msgid ""
"the borrow-checker fights you will have in engine code, and their fixes."
msgstr "你在引擎代码中会遇到的借用检查器难题，以及解决办法。"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:19
msgid "Two kinds of reference"
msgstr "两种引用"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:32
msgid "// nothing at the call site says it mutates\n"
msgstr "// 调用处看不出它会修改参数\n"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:51
msgid "// mutation is visible here\n"
msgstr "// 修改在这里一目了然\n"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:52
msgid "\"{a} {samples:?}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:59
msgid ""
"`&T` is a **shared reference**: read-only access, like `const T&`. You can "
"have as many as you like at the same time."
msgstr "`&T` 是**共享引用**：只读访问，类似 `const T&`。同一时间你可以拥有任意多个。"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:61
msgid ""
"`&mut T` is a **mutable reference**: read-write access, like `T&`. While it "
"exists, it is the _only_ way to reach the value."
msgstr "`&mut T` 是**可变引用**：读写访问，类似 `T&`。在它存在期间，它是访问该值的<em>唯一</em>途径。"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:64
msgid ""
"Both are plain pointers at run time, never null, and always point to a "
"valid, initialized value. Unlike C++ references they are first-class values:"
" you can reassign a `let` binding holding a reference, store references in "
"structs, and put them in containers."
msgstr ""
"两者在运行时都是普通指针，永远不为空，并且总是指向一个有效的、已初始化的值。与 C++ 引用不同，它们是一等值：你可以给持有引用的 `let` "
"绑定重新赋值，把引用存进结构体，放进容器。"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:69
msgid ""
"You also borrow explicitly at the call site: `average(&samples)`, "
"`normalize(&mut samples)`. Reading a call tells you whether it can modify "
"its argument, which C++ hides behind the function signature."
msgstr ""
"借用也要在调用处显式写出：`average(&samples)`、`normalize(&mut "
"samples)`。读一个函数调用就能知道它会不会修改参数，而 C++ 把这一点藏在了函数签名里。"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:73
msgid "The rule: shared XOR mutable"
msgstr "规则：共享与可变互斥"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:75
msgid ""
"At any point in the program, a value can have **either** any number of `&T` "
"**or** exactly one `&mut T`, never both. Step through it:"
msgstr "在程序的任意时刻，一个值**要么**有任意数量的 `&T`，**要么**恰好有一个 `&mut T`，绝不会同时存在。逐步执行看看："

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:80
msgid ""
"While a shared borrow is in use, the owner is also frozen against writes: "
"`scores` itself cannot be modified until `a` and `b` are done. While a "
"mutable borrow is in use, the owner cannot even be _read_ except through it."
msgstr ""
"当共享借用正在使用时，所有者本身也被冻结，不能写入：在 `a` 和 `b` 用完之前，`scores` "
"本身不能被修改。当可变借用正在使用时，除了通过它，所有者甚至连<em>读</em>都不行。"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:84
msgid ""
"This is a reader-writer lock, enforced at compile time, with zero runtime "
"cost."
msgstr "这是一把读写锁，在编译期强制执行，运行时零开销。"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:86
msgid "The bug this rule removes"
msgstr "这条规则消除的 bug"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:88
msgid ""
"Every C++ engineer has hit this, usually with `std::vector<Entity>` and a "
"cached `Entity*` or iterator. Compare the two tabs:"
msgstr ""
"每个 C++ 工程师都遇到过这种情况，通常是 `std::vector<Entity>` 加上一个缓存的 `Entity*` 或迭代器。比较两个标签页："

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:93
msgid ""
"The C++ program is undefined behavior that usually _appears_ to work. The "
"Rust program does not compile, and the error points at all three lines "
"involved: where the borrow starts, where the conflicting mutation is, and "
"where the borrow is used later."
msgstr ""
"C++ 程序是未定义行为，而且通常<em>看起来</em>能正常工作。Rust "
"程序无法编译，错误信息会指出涉及的全部三行：借用从哪里开始、冲突的修改在哪里，以及借用在哪里被再次使用。"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:98
msgid ""
"The same rule covers modifying a container while iterating over it, holding "
"a `string_view` into a `std::string` that gets reassigned, and a `std::span`"
" over a vector that grows. These are all the same mistake: a reader holds a "
"pointer into memory that a writer is about to move or free."
msgstr ""
"同一条规则也覆盖了：在遍历容器时修改它；持有指向某个 `std::string` 的 `string_view`，而该字符串被重新赋值；在一个会增长的 "
"vector 上持有 `std::span`。这些都是同一个错误：读者持有一个指针，指向写者即将移动或释放的内存。"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:103
msgid "How long does a borrow last?"
msgstr "一次借用持续多久？"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:105
msgid ""
"A borrow is alive from where it is created to its **last use**, not to the "
"end of the enclosing block. The compiler computes this (\"non-lexical "
"lifetimes\"), and most of the time you never think about it. When you do get"
" an error, picture the live range of each reference. Hover the bars below to"
" see which lines each borrow covers, and switch between the rejected program"
" and two fixes:"
msgstr ""
"借用从创建处一直存活到它的**最后一次使用**，而不是到所在代码块的结尾。编译器会计算这一点（“非词法生命周期”），大多数时候你完全不用考虑。当你真的遇到错误时，请想象每个引用的存活范围。把鼠标悬停在下面的条带上，可以看到每次借用覆盖了哪些行；还可以在被拒绝的程序和两种修复方案之间切换："

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:114
msgid "Borrowing in methods"
msgstr "方法中的借用"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:116
msgid ""
"Methods choose how they access `self`, which is how the standard library "
"encodes \"this method mutates\" or \"this method consumes\":"
msgstr "方法自己选择如何访问 `self`，标准库就是这样表达“这个方法会修改”或“这个方法会消耗”的："

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:125
msgid "// like a const member function\n"
msgstr "// 类似 const 成员函数\n"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:128
msgid "// non-const member function\n"
msgstr "// 非 const 成员函数\n"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:135
msgid "// consumes the mesh\n"
msgstr "// 消耗这个 mesh\n"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:142
msgid "// auto-borrows: (&mut m).translate(...)\n"
msgstr "// 自动借用：(&mut m).translate(...)\n"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:144
msgid "// `m` is moved; it cannot be used after this\n"
msgstr "// `m` 被移动了；此后不能再使用\n"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:145
msgid "\"{raw:?}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:149
msgid ""
"The `.` operator borrows and dereferences automatically, so you write "
"`m.translate(...)` rather than `(&mut m).translate(...)`. Method calls are "
"one of the very few places where Rust inserts a borrow for you."
msgstr ""
"`.` 运算符会自动借用和解引用，所以你写 `m.translate(...)` 而不是 `(&mut m).translate(...)`。方法调用是"
" Rust 为你自动插入借用的极少数地方之一。"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:153
msgid "Slices: the safe span"
msgstr "切片：安全的 span"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:155
msgid ""
"A **slice** `&[T]` is a pointer plus a length, a borrowed view of contiguous"
" elements. It is `std::span<const T>`, and `&mut [T]` is `std::span<T>`, "
"except that the borrow checker guarantees the underlying storage outlives "
"the view and does not reallocate under it. `&str` is the same for UTF-8 "
"text, the safe `std::string_view`."
msgstr ""
"**切片** `&[T]` 是一个指针加一个长度，是对连续元素的借用视图。它就是 `std::span<const T>`，而 `&mut [T]` 是"
" `std::span<T>`，区别在于借用检查器保证底层存储比视图活得更久，并且不会在它底下重新分配。`&str` 是 UTF-8 "
"文本的同类物，即安全的 `std::string_view`。"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:161
msgid ""
"Write functions that take slices rather than `&Vec<T>`. They then accept "
"vectors, arrays, and sub-ranges:"
msgstr "编写接收切片而不是 `&Vec<T>` 的函数。这样它们就能接受 vector、数组和子区间："

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:172
msgid "// &Vec<f32> coerces to &[f32]\n"
msgstr "// &Vec<f32> 自动转换为 &[f32]\n"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:173
msgid "// so does &[f32; 2]\n"
msgstr "// &[f32; 2] 也一样\n"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:174
msgid "// a sub-range: bounds-checked once\n"
msgstr "// 子区间：只做一次边界检查\n"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:178
msgid ""
"Indexing a slice is bounds-checked. An out-of-range index panics instead of "
"reading past the end. In hot loops, iterating (`for x in xs`) avoids the "
"checks entirely, and the [iterators chapter](closures-and-iterators.md) "
"shows how to confirm that in the assembly."
msgstr ""
"对切片的索引会做边界检查。越界的索引会 panic，而不是读到末尾之外。在热点循环中，用迭代（`for x in "
"xs`）可以完全避免这些检查，[迭代器一章](closures-and-iterators.md)介绍了如何在汇编中确认这一点。"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:183
msgid "What the rule buys the optimizer"
msgstr "这条规则给优化器带来了什么"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:185
msgid ""
"Because a `&mut T` is guaranteed to be the only path to its target, the "
"compiler can assume it does not alias anything else. In C++ terms, every "
"`&mut` is `__restrict`, and the compiler checks it for you."
msgstr ""
"由于 `&mut T` 保证是通往其目标的唯一途径，编译器可以假定它不与任何其他东西重叠（alias）。用 C++ 的话说，每个 `&mut` 都是 "
"`__restrict`，而且由编译器替你检查。"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:197
msgid ""
"// must reload b: a and b\n"
"              // might be the same int\n"
msgstr ""
"// 必须重新加载 b：a 和 b\n"
"              // 可能是同一个 int\n"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:210
msgid ""
"// b cannot alias a: the\n"
"              // compiler folds this to\n"
"              // *a += 2 * *b\n"
msgstr ""
"// b 不可能与 a 重叠：\n"
"              // 编译器把这里合并成\n"
"              // *a += 2 * *b\n"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:220
msgid ""
"Open the Rust version in the Playground (link under the example), choose "
"**Show Assembly** in release mode, and compare with the C++ version in "
"Compiler Explorer. The Rust version loads `b` once. In SIMD-heavy code such "
"as skinning, particle updates or audio mixing, this is the difference "
"between vectorizing and not, without sprinkling `__restrict` around and "
"hoping it is true."
msgstr ""
"在 Playground 中打开 Rust 版本（示例下方的链接），在 release 模式下选择 **Show Assembly**，再和 "
"Compiler Explorer 中的 C++ 版本比较。Rust 版本只加载一次 `b`。在蒙皮、粒子更新或音频混音这类大量使用 SIMD "
"的代码中，这就是能否向量化的区别，而且不需要到处撒 `__restrict` 并祈祷它成立。"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:226
msgid "Fights you will have, and the fixes"
msgstr "你会遇到的难题，以及解决办法"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:228
msgid ""
"The borrow checker reasons about whole values, plus individual fields of a "
"struct when it can see them directly. Most surprises in engine code come "
"from that boundary."
msgstr "借用检查器以整个值为单位进行推理，当它能直接看到结构体的各个字段时，也会以字段为单位推理。引擎代码中的大多数意外都源于这个边界。"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:232
msgid "Two mutable elements of one array"
msgstr "同一个数组中的两个可变元素"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:238
msgid "// error: `bodies` already borrowed mutably\n"
msgstr "// 错误：`bodies` 已经被可变借用\n"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:243
msgid ""
"The checker does not know that indices 0 and 1 differ. The standard library "
"does the reasoning for you with `split_at_mut`, which hands out two non-"
"overlapping `&mut` slices:"
msgstr ""
"检查器不知道索引 0 和 1 是不同的。标准库通过 `split_at_mut` 替你完成推理，它会交给你两个互不重叠的 `&mut` 切片："

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:251
msgid "// bodies[0], bodies[1]\n"
msgstr "// bodies[0]、bodies[1]\n"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:253
msgid "// Or, for any two distinct indices (Rust 1.86+):\n"
msgstr "// 或者，对任意两个不同的索引（Rust 1.86+）：\n"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:257
msgid "\"{bodies:?}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:261
msgid "Borrowing two fields through a method"
msgstr "通过方法借用两个字段"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:263
msgid ""
"Borrowing two different fields directly is fine. Borrowing them through "
"methods is not, because a method signature `&mut self` claims the whole "
"struct:"
msgstr "直接借用两个不同的字段没有问题。通过方法借用就不行了，因为方法签名中的 `&mut self` 声明占用了整个结构体："

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:274
msgid "// Fine: two disjoint fields, borrowed directly.\n"
msgstr "// 没问题：两个不相交的字段，直接借用。\n"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:280
msgid ""
"// Would NOT compile: each call borrows all of `self`.\n"
"        // let t = self.transforms_mut();\n"
"        // let v = self.velocities();\n"
msgstr ""
"// 无法编译：每次调用都借用了整个 `self`。\n"
"        // let t = self.transforms_mut();\n"
"        // let v = self.velocities();\n"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:293
msgid ""
"The fixes, in order of preference: access the fields directly inside the "
"`impl`; write one method that returns both borrows at once (`fn "
"parts_mut(&mut self) -> (&mut A, &B)`); or split the struct so the parts "
"that change together live together. The last one is the road to an ECS, "
"which has [its own chapter](../engine/ecs.md)."
msgstr ""
"修复方法按推荐顺序排列：在 `impl` 内部直接访问字段；写一个同时返回两个借用的方法（`fn parts_mut(&mut self) -> "
"(&mut A, &B)`）；或者拆分结构体，让一起变化的部分放在一起。最后一种通向 ECS，它有[专门的一章](../engine/ecs.md)。"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:299
msgid "Long-lived pointers between objects"
msgstr "对象之间长期存在的指针"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:301
msgid ""
"Storing `&Enemy` inside `Missile` to remember its target works for a few "
"lines of code and then fails, because the borrow would freeze the whole "
"enemy list for as long as the missile exists. References are for _temporary_"
" access. For long-lived relationships between objects, use [handles into an "
"arena](../engine/handles-and-arenas.md), or shared ownership with "
"[`Rc`/`Arc`](smart-pointers.md)."
msgstr ""
"在 `Missile` 中存一个 `&Enemy` "
"来记住它的目标，在几行代码里能行，之后就会失败，因为这个借用会在导弹存在的整个期间冻结整个敌人列表。引用是用于<em>临时</em>访问的。对象之间长期存在的关系，请使用[指向"
" arena 的句柄](../engine/handles-and-arenas.md)，或使用 [`Rc`/`Arc`](smart-"
"pointers.md) 共享所有权。"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:311
msgid ""
"In C++ it is normal to keep a raw pointer to \"the thing I'm working with\" "
"as a member. In Rust, a struct that holds a reference needs a lifetime "
"parameter and borrows its target for its whole life. That is occasionally "
"right (parsers, views, iterators), but for game objects it almost never is. "
"If you find yourself adding `<'a>` to a struct to make the borrow checker "
"happy, step back and ask who should own the data."
msgstr ""
"在 C++ 中，把“我正在处理的那个东西”的裸指针作为成员保存是很常见的。在 Rust "
"中，持有引用的结构体需要一个生命周期参数，并在它整个生命期间借用目标。这偶尔是对的（解析器、视图、迭代器），但对游戏对象而言几乎从来都不对。如果你发现自己为了让借用检查器满意而给结构体加上"
" `<'a>`，请退一步，问问数据应该归谁所有。"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:320
msgid "No null, no dangling"
msgstr "没有空引用，没有悬垂引用"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:322
msgid "Two guarantees fall out of everything above:"
msgstr "从以上所有内容可以得出两个保证："

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:324
msgid ""
"References are never null. \"Maybe a reference\" is `Option<&T>`, which the "
"compiler stores as a plain nullable pointer, so it costs nothing, and "
"`match`/`if let` forces you to handle the `None` case."
msgstr ""
"引用永远不为空。“可能有引用”写作 `Option<&T>`，编译器会把它存成一个普通的可空指针，所以没有任何开销，而 `match`/`if let`"
" 会强迫你处理 `None` 的情况。"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:327
msgid ""
"References never dangle. Returning a reference to a local is rejected, and "
"so is keeping one past the lifetime of its owner. The [next "
"chapter](lifetimes.md) explains how the compiler proves this across function"
" boundaries."
msgstr ""
"引用永远不会悬垂。返回指向局部变量的引用会被拒绝，在所有者的生命期结束后继续持有引用也会被拒绝。[下一章](lifetimes.md)解释了编译器如何跨函数边界证明这一点。"

