#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:346
msgid ""
"In the `invalidation` example above, make the Rust version compile in three "
"different ways. Which one corresponds to what you would do in C++?"
msgstr "在上面的 `invalidation` 示例中，用三种不同的方法让 Rust 版本通过编译。哪一种对应你在 C++ 中的做法？"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:348
msgid ""
"Write `fn largest<'a>(a: &'a [f32], b: &'a [f32]) -> &'a [f32]` that returns"
" the slice with the larger sum. Then try removing the `'a` annotations and "
"read the error. (The [lifetimes chapter](lifetimes.md) explains it.)"
msgstr ""
"编写 `fn largest<'a>(a: &'a [f32], b: &'a [f32]) -> &'a "
"[f32]`，返回和较大的那个切片。然后试着去掉 `'a` 标注，阅读错误信息。（[生命周期一章](lifetimes.md)会解释它。）"

#: src/foundations/borrowing.md:351
msgid ""
"Implement `fn swap_ends(xs: &mut [i32])` that swaps the first and last "
"element, using `split_at_mut` rather than `xs.swap`. Handle empty slices."
msgstr ""
"实现 `fn swap_ends(xs: &mut [i32])`，交换第一个和最后一个元素，要求使用 `split_at_mut` 而不是 "
"`xs.swap`。处理空切片的情况。"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:3
msgid ""
"The previous chapter showed that the compiler tracks how long each borrow is"
" used. This chapter is about the other half of the proof: making sure the "
"_owner_ lives at least that long. In C++ this is the dangling pointer "
"problem: returning a pointer to a local, keeping a `string_view` to a "
"temporary, storing a reference to an object that gets destroyed. Rust rules "
"all of these out at compile time, and **lifetimes** are the notation for how"
" it does so across function boundaries."
msgstr ""
"上一章介绍了编译器如何追踪每次借用被使用多久。本章讲的是证明的另一半：确保<em>所有者</em>至少活得那么久。在 C++ "
"中，这就是悬垂指针问题：返回指向局部变量的指针、持有指向临时对象的 `string_view`、保存一个对象的引用而该对象随后被销毁。Rust "
"在编译期排除了所有这些情况，而**生命周期**就是它跨越函数边界做到这一点所用的记法。"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:11
msgid ""
"The most important fact first: **lifetimes do not exist at run time.** They "
"do not change what code is generated, they do not extend how long anything "
"lives, and they cost nothing. A lifetime annotation is a statement to the "
"compiler about which references are related, so it can check your program."
msgstr ""
"先说最重要的一点：**生命周期在运行时并不存在。** "
"它不会改变生成的代码，不会延长任何东西的寿命，也没有任何开销。生命周期标注是你向编译器做出的陈述，说明哪些引用彼此相关，以便它检查你的程序。"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:18
msgid "what a lifetime is, and watching a borrow outlive its owner,"
msgstr "生命周期是什么，以及观察一次借用比所有者活得更久；"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:19
msgid ""
"lifetime annotations on functions, and the elision rules that make most of "
"them unnecessary,"
msgstr "函数上的生命周期标注，以及让大多数标注变得不必要的省略规则；"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:21
msgid "structs that hold references,"
msgstr "持有引用的结构体；"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:22
msgid "`'static`,"
msgstr ""

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:23
msgid "reading the common error messages."
msgstr "读懂常见的错误信息。"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:25
msgid "A borrow must not outlive its owner"
msgstr "借用不能比所有者活得更久"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:27
msgid ""
"Step through this program. It is the Rust version of returning a pointer to "
"a local variable."
msgstr "逐步执行这个程序。它是“返回指向局部变量的指针”的 Rust 版本。"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:32
msgid ""
"The compiler gives every reference a **lifetime**: the region of code where "
"it must remain valid. Here, `r` is used on the last line, so the borrow `&s`"
" must be valid until then. But `s` is dropped at the inner closing brace. "
"The lifetime of the borrow is longer than the life of the value it points "
"to, so the program is rejected with error E0597, \"`s` does not live long "
"enough\"."
msgstr ""
"编译器给每个引用一个**生命周期**：它必须保持有效的那段代码区域。这里 `r` 在最后一行被使用，所以借用 `&s` 必须一直有效到那里。但 `s` "
"在内层的右花括号处就被丢弃了。借用的生命周期比它指向的值的寿命更长，所以程序被拒绝，报错 E0597：“`s` does not live long "
"enough”（`s` 活得不够久）。"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:38
msgid "Lifetimes in function signatures"
msgstr "函数签名中的生命周期"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:40
msgid ""
"Inside one function the compiler can see everything and needs no help. "
"Across function calls it only sees signatures. Consider:"
msgstr "在一个函数内部，编译器能看到一切，不需要帮助。跨函数调用时，它只能看到签名。考虑："

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:44
msgid "// error[E0106]: missing lifetime specifier\n"
msgstr "// error[E0106]: 缺少生命周期说明符\n"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:50
msgid ""
"The caller needs to know: the returned reference points into _which_ "
"argument? It decides how long the caller must keep each argument alive. You "
"answer with a **lifetime parameter**:"
msgstr "调用者需要知道：返回的引用指向<em>哪个</em>参数？这决定了调用者必须让每个参数存活多久。你用一个**生命周期参数**来回答："

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:60
msgid "\"Vulkan\""
msgstr ""

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:63 src/engine/opengl.md:46
msgid "\"GL\""
msgstr ""

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:65
msgid "\"{result}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:65
msgid "// fine: both strings are alive here\n"
msgstr "// 没问题：两个字符串在这里都还活着\n"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:67
msgid "// println!(\"{result}\");    // error: `other` does not live long enough\n"
msgstr "// println!(\"{result}\");    // 错误：`other` 活得不够久\n"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:71
msgid ""
"Read `<'a>` like a template parameter, but for regions of code instead of "
"types. The signature says: \"there is some region `'a` during which both `a`"
" and `b` are valid, and the result is valid for that same region.\" At the "
"call site the compiler picks the largest region that satisfies both "
"arguments, which is the scope of `other`, and then checks every use of "
"`result` against it. Uncomment the last line to see the error."
msgstr ""
"把 `<'a>` 当作模板参数来读，只不过它代表的是代码区域而不是类型。这个签名的意思是：“存在某个区域 `'a`，在这段区域内 `a` 和 `b` "
"都有效，而结果在同一区域内也有效。”在调用处，编译器选出同时满足两个参数的最大区域，也就是 `other` 的作用域，然后用它检查 `result` "
"的每一次使用。取消最后一行的注释就能看到错误。"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:78
msgid ""
