#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:122
msgid ""
"You need explicit lifetimes only when the rules are ambiguous: several input"
" references and a returned reference (like `longest`), or structs that hold "
"references."
msgstr "只有当规则存在歧义时才需要显式写出生命周期：有多个输入引用并返回一个引用（比如 `longest`），或者结构体持有引用。"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:129
msgid ""
"Lifetimes are checked by the **borrow checker**, which runs on MIR, a "
"simplified control-flow graph of each function. It computes, for every "
"reference, the set of program points where it is live, and checks that the "
"borrowed value is not moved, dropped or mutated in a conflicting way at any "
"of them. Then the lifetimes are erased. The machine code is identical to "
"what you would get from the same program with raw pointers."
msgstr ""
"生命周期由**借用检查器**检查，它运行在 MIR 上，MIR "
"是每个函数的简化控制流图。它为每个引用计算出它存活的程序点集合，并检查被借用的值在这些程序点上都没有以冲突的方式被移动、丢弃或修改。然后生命周期就被擦除了。生成的机器码与用裸指针写的同一程序完全相同。"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:138
msgid "Structs that hold references"
msgstr "持有引用的结构体"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:140
msgid ""
"A struct can hold references if it declares the lifetime they borrow for. "
"The annotation says \"a value of this type cannot outlive the data it "
"borrows\":"
msgstr "结构体如果声明了所借用数据的生命周期，就可以持有引用。这个标注的意思是“这个类型的值不能比它借用的数据活得更久”："

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:144
msgid "/// A zero-copy tokenizer over a shader source string.\n"
msgstr "/// 一个作用于着色器源码字符串的零拷贝分词器。\n"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:156
msgid "// tokens borrow from the source, not from the tokenizer\n"
msgstr "// 词法单元借用自源字符串，而不是分词器\n"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:163
msgid "';'"
msgstr ""

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:171
msgid "\"uniform mat4 mvp; in vec3 pos;\""
msgstr ""

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:173
msgid "\"{tokens:?}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:174
msgid "// drop(source); // error: `tokens` still borrows from `source`\n"
msgstr "// drop(source); // 错误：`tokens` 仍在借用 `source`\n"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:178
msgid ""
"This is the safe version of the C++ \"view\" types: `std::string_view`, "
"`std::span`, iterators. A `Tokens` cannot outlive `source`, and neither can "
"the tokens it produced. Note the `Item = &'src str`: the tokens borrow from "
"the original string, not from the tokenizer, so the tokenizer can be dropped"
" while the tokens are still in use."
msgstr ""
"这是 C++ 中“视图”类型的安全版本：`std::string_view`、`std::span`、迭代器。`Tokens` 不能比 `source`"
" 活得更久，它产生的词法单元也不能。注意 `Item = &'src "
"str`：词法单元借用的是原始字符串而不是分词器，所以在词法单元仍在使用时，分词器可以被丢弃。"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:184
msgid ""
"Use reference-holding structs for short-lived views, parsers and iterators. "
"For long-lived objects like game entities, store owned data or handles "
"([Handles and arenas](../engine/handles-and-arenas.md)). A lifetime "
"parameter spreads to every type that contains it, which is a good signal "
"that you are borrowing for too long."
msgstr ""
"持有引用的结构体适用于短期的视图、解析器和迭代器。对于游戏实体这类长期存在的对象，请保存拥有所有权的数据或句柄（[句柄与 "
"arena](../engine/handles-and-"
"arenas.md)）。生命周期参数会扩散到包含它的每个类型，这是一个明显的信号，说明你借用得太久了。"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:192
msgid ""
"`'static` is the lifetime of the whole program. Two different things carry "
"it:"
msgstr "`'static` 是整个程序的生命周期。有两种不同的东西带有它："

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:194
msgid ""
"**References** `&'static T` point to data that lives forever: string "
"literals (stored in the binary), `static` items, and leaked allocations "
"(`Box::leak`)."
msgstr ""
"**引用** `&'static T` 指向永远存活的数据：字符串字面量（存储在二进制文件中）、`static` "
"条目，以及被泄漏的分配（`Box::leak`）。"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:197
msgid ""
"**Type bounds** `T: 'static` mean \"`T` contains no non-static references\":"
" it owns all its data. `String`, `Vec<u8>` and `i32` all satisfy `T: "
"'static`. It does **not** mean the value lives forever."
msgstr ""
"**类型约束** `T: 'static` 的意思是“`T` 不包含非 static "
"的引用”：它拥有自己的全部数据。`String`、`Vec<u8>` 和 `i32` 都满足 `T: "
"'static`。它**并不**意味着这个值永远存活。"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:201
msgid ""
"The second meaning is common in APIs. `std::thread::spawn` requires `F: "
"'static` because the new thread may outlive the caller, so the closure must "
"not borrow the caller's locals:"
msgstr ""
"第二种含义在 API 中很常见。`std::thread::spawn` 要求 `F: "
"'static`，因为新线程可能比调用者活得更久，所以闭包不能借用调用者的局部变量："

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:209 src/foundations/errors.md:261
msgid "\"e1m1\""
msgstr ""

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:211
msgid ""
"// `move` transfers ownership of `level_name` into the thread,\n"
"        // making the closure 'static.\n"
msgstr ""
"// `move` 把 `level_name` 的所有权转移到线程中，\n"
"        // 使闭包成为 'static。\n"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:213
msgid "\"loaded {level_name}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:219
msgid ""
"Remove `move` and you get an error explaining that the closure may outlive "
"the function that borrows `level_name`. The [concurrency "
"chapter](../systems/concurrency.md) shows scoped threads, which _can_ "
"borrow."
msgstr ""
"去掉 `move`，你会得到一个错误，解释说这个闭包可能比借用 `level_name` "
"的函数活得更久。[并发一章](../systems/concurrency.md)介绍了作用域线程，它们<em>可以</em>借用。"

#: src/foundations/lifetimes.md:226
msgid ""
"When the compiler says a value \"does not live long enough\", the C++ reflex"
" is to make it live longer: allocate it on the heap, make it static. Usually"
" the better fix is to make the _borrow_ shorter (use the reference earlier, "
"copy the small value you need, or return owned data such as `String` instead"
" of `&str`). Returning owned data costs an allocation, and in exchange "
"removes a lifetime from every caller."
msgstr ""
"当编译器说一个值“活得不够久”时，C++ "
"的条件反射是让它活得更久：把它分配到堆上、把它变成静态的。通常更好的修复是让<em>借用</em>更短（更早地使用引用、复制你需要的那个小值，或者返回 "
"`String` 这样拥有所有权的数据而不是 `&str`）。返回拥有所有权的数据要付出一次分配的代价，换来的是每个调用者都少了一个生命周期。"

