#: src/foundations/enums-and-match.md:3
msgid ""
"If you take one feature from Rust back to C++, it will be this one. A Rust "
"`enum` is a **tagged union**: a type that is exactly one of several "
"variants, each of which can carry its own data. You have written this by "
"hand in C (a `struct` with a `kind` field and a `union`), and C++17 gave you"
" `std::variant` and `std::visit`. Rust makes it a core language feature, and"
" pairs it with `match`, a `switch` that checks you handled every case."
msgstr ""
"如果你只把 Rust 的一个特性带回 C++，那就是这一个。Rust 的 `enum` 是一个**带标签的联合体**（tagged "
"union）：它的值恰好是若干变体中的一个，每个变体都可以携带自己的数据。你在 C 里手写过这种东西（一个带 `kind` 字段和 `union` 的 "
"`struct`），C++17 则给了你 `std::variant` 和 `std::visit`。Rust 把它做成了语言的核心特性，并配上了 "
"`match`：一个会检查你是否处理了每种情况的 `switch`。"

