#: src/foundations/enums-and-match.md:108
msgid ""
"A `match` must cover every possible value. Delete the `Light::Ambient(_)` "
"arm above and run it: the compiler rejects the program and names the missing"
" variant. This is the feature that makes enums so useful in a large "
"codebase. When you add a variant, the compiler lists every `match` that "
"needs updating. C++ compilers can warn about missing `case` labels in a "
"`switch` over an enum, but only for plain enums, only as a warning, and "
"never for `std::variant`."
msgstr ""
