#: src/foundations/errors.md:3
msgid ""
"C++ has too many ways to report an error: exceptions, error codes, `errno`, "
"`HRESULT`, `VkResult`, `std::error_code`, `std::expected`, `bool` plus an "
"out parameter, and `assert`. Engines usually ban exceptions and end up with "
"a mix of the rest. Rust has two mechanisms with a clear division of labor:"
msgstr ""
"C++ "
"报告错误的方式太多了：异常、错误码、`errno`、`HRESULT`、`VkResult`、`std::error_code`、`std::expected`、`bool`"
" 加输出参数，还有 `assert`。引擎通常禁用异常，最后混用剩下的那些。Rust 只有两种机制，分工明确："

#: src/foundations/errors.md:8
msgid ""
"**`Result<T, E>`** for errors a caller can reasonably handle: a missing "
"file, a malformed asset, a device that failed to initialize. It is an "
"ordinary return value, as cheap as an error code."
msgstr ""
"**`Result<T, E>`** 用于调用者可以合理处理的错误：文件缺失、资源格式错误、设备初始化失败。它是一个普通的返回值，和错误码一样廉价。"

#: src/foundations/errors.md:11
msgid ""
"**`panic!`** for bugs: a broken invariant, an out-of-bounds index, an "
"`unwrap()` on something that was supposed to be there. It is like a failed "
"`assert` that stays on in release builds."
msgstr ""
"**`panic!`** 用于 bug：被破坏的不变量、越界的索引、对本应存在的东西调用 `unwrap()`。它就像一个在发布构建中依然开启的失败 "
"`assert`。"

#: src/foundations/errors.md:15
