#: src/foundations/errors.md:50
msgid "How `Ok(...)` and `Err(...)` work"
msgstr "`Ok(...)` 和 `Err(...)` 是怎么工作的"

#: src/foundations/errors.md:52
msgid ""
"Nothing here is special syntax. `Ok` and `Err` are the two **variants** of "
"the `Result` enum ([Enums and pattern matching](enums-and-match.md)), and "
"the same name plays three roles depending on where it appears:"
msgstr ""
"这里没有任何特殊语法。`Ok` 和 `Err` 是 `Result` 枚举的两个**变体**（[枚举与模式匹配](enums-and-"
"match.md)），同一个名字根据出现的位置扮演三种角色："

#: src/foundations/errors.md:56
msgid ""
"**As an expression, it builds a value.** A variant that carries data can be "
"called like a function: `Ok(42)` is a `Result<i32, _>` meaning \"success, "
"holding 42\", and `Err(e)` means \"failure, holding `e`\". That is why a "
"fallible function ends with `Ok(value)`: it returns the success case."
msgstr ""
"**在表达式中，它构造一个值。** 携带数据的变体可以像函数一样调用：`Ok(42)` 是一个 `Result<i32, _>`，表示\"成功，值为 "
"42\"；`Err(e)` 表示\"失败，错误为 `e`\"。这就是可能失败的函数以 `Ok(value)` 结尾的原因：它返回的是成功的情况；"

#: src/foundations/errors.md:60
msgid ""
"**In a pattern, it takes the value apart.** In `match`, `if let` or `let ..."
" else`, `Ok(src)` means \"if this is the success case, bind what is inside "
"to `src`\". The compiler checks that every variant is handled, so forgetting"
" the `Err` arm is a compile error."
msgstr ""
"**在模式中，它把值拆开。** 在 `match`、`if let` 或 `let ... else` 中，`Ok(src)` "
"的意思是\"如果这是成功的情况，就把里面的值绑定到 `src`\"。编译器会检查每个变体都被处理了，所以漏掉 `Err` 分支是编译错误；"

#: src/foundations/errors.md:64
msgid ""
"**It needs no prefix.** The full names are `Result::Ok` and `Result::Err`, "
"but the standard prelude imports `Ok`, `Err`, `Some` and `None` into every "
"file, so you write them bare."
msgstr ""
"**它不需要前缀。** 完整的名字是 `Result::Ok` 和 `Result::Err`，但标准 prelude 会把 "
"`Ok`、`Err`、`Some` 和 `None` 导入每个文件，所以你可以直接写。"

#: src/foundations/errors.md:68
msgid ""
