#: src/foundations/traits-and-generics.md:3
msgid ""
"C++ gives you two separate tools for polymorphism: virtual functions for "
"run-time dispatch and templates for compile-time dispatch, with concepts "
"(C++20) bolted on to constrain templates. Rust has one concept that serves "
"both purposes: the **trait**. A trait is a set of methods a type can "
"implement. Used as a constraint on a generic, it is a concept and the call "
"is resolved at compile time. Used behind a pointer as `dyn Trait`, it is an "
"interface with a vtable."
msgstr ""
"C++ 为多态提供了两种独立的工具：用于运行时分派的虚函数和用于编译期分派的模板，此外还加上了用于约束模板的 concept（C++20）。Rust "
"只有一个概念，同时服务于这两种目的：**trait**。trait 是一个类型可以实现的一组方法。用作泛型的约束时，它就是 "
"concept，调用在编译期解析；放在指针后面写成 `dyn Trait` 时，它就是一个带虚表的接口。"

