#: src/foundations/traits-and-generics.md:238
msgid ""
"Rust code defaults to generics, as modern C++ defaults to templates in "
"libraries. Reach for `dyn` when you need a heterogeneous collection, a "
"plugin boundary, or to stop generic code from spreading through a large "
"codebase."
msgstr ""
"Rust 代码默认使用泛型，就像现代 C++ 的库默认使用模板一样。当你需要异构集合、插件边界，或者想阻止泛型代码在大型代码库中蔓延时，再使用 "
"`dyn`。"

#: src/foundations/traits-and-generics.md:245
msgid ""
"The classic OOP engine has `class GameObject { virtual void update(); }` and"
" a `std::vector<GameObject*>`. The direct translation, `Vec<Box<dyn "
"GameObject>>`, works and is sometimes right (a few dozen heterogeneous "
"systems, editor panels, a render-graph's passes). For thousands of entities "
"it has the same cache problems as in C++, plus it fights the borrow checker "
"as soon as objects need to touch each other. Most Rust engines use enums for"
" closed sets of variants ([Enums](enums-and-match.md)) and an ECS for game "
"objects ([ECS chapter](../engine/ecs.md))."
msgstr ""
"经典的面向对象引擎有 `class GameObject { virtual void update(); }` 和一个 "
"`std::vector<GameObject*>`。直接翻译成 `Vec<Box<dyn GameObject>>` "
"是可行的，有时也是对的（几十个异构的系统、编辑器面板、渲染图中的各个 pass）。但对成千上万个实体来说，它有和 C++ "
"中一样的缓存问题，而且一旦对象之间需要互相访问，就会和借用检查器冲突。大多数 Rust 引擎用枚举表示封闭的变体集合（[枚举](enums-and-"
"match.md)），用 ECS 表示游戏对象（[ECS 一章](../engine/ecs.md)）。"

