#: src/foundations/traits-and-generics.md:296
msgid ""
"The standard library's `Iterator` trait has an associated type `Item`, which"
" is why you write `impl Iterator<Item = u32>`."
msgstr ""
"标准库的 `Iterator` trait 有一个关联类型 `Item`，所以你会写 `impl Iterator<Item = u32>`。"

#: src/foundations/traits-and-generics.md:299
msgid "Composition instead of inheritance"
msgstr "用组合代替继承"

#: src/foundations/traits-and-generics.md:301
msgid "Rust has no struct inheritance. What it offers instead:"
msgstr "Rust 没有结构体继承。它提供的替代方案是："

#: src/foundations/traits-and-generics.md:303
msgid ""
"**Composition:** a struct contains other structs as fields, and forwards "
"methods explicitly where needed."
msgstr "**组合：** 结构体把其他结构体作为字段，在需要时显式转发方法。"

#: src/foundations/traits-and-generics.md:305
msgid "**Default methods** on traits provide shared behavior."
msgstr "trait 上的**默认方法**提供共享的行为。"

#: src/foundations/traits-and-generics.md:306
msgid ""
"**Supertraits:** `trait Drawable: Shape` means every `Drawable` is also a "
"`Shape`, so code with a `Drawable` can call `area()`. This is interface "
"inheritance, not data inheritance."
msgstr ""
"**父 trait（supertrait）：** `trait Drawable: Shape` 表示每个 `Drawable` 也都是 "
"`Shape`，所以持有 `Drawable` 的代码可以调用 `area()`。这是接口继承，而不是数据继承。"

#: src/foundations/traits-and-generics.md:309
msgid ""
"**Blanket implementations:** implement a trait for every type that satisfies"
" some bound, e.g. `impl<T: Shape> Describe for T { ... }`."
msgstr ""
"**通用实现（blanket implementation）：** 为满足某个约束的所有类型实现一个 trait，例如 `impl<T: Shape> "
"Describe for T { ... }`。"

#: src/foundations/traits-and-generics.md:320
msgid "// Every Shape gets Describe for free.\n"
msgstr "// 每个 Shape 都免费获得 Describe。\n"

#: src/foundations/traits-and-generics.md:324
msgid "\"a shape with area {:.2}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/foundations/traits-and-generics.md:341
msgid ""
"Do not try to emulate a class hierarchy with traits and `Deref`. If you "
"catch yourself designing `trait Entity`, `trait Actor: Entity`, `trait Pawn:"
" Actor`, step back. Ask which _behaviors_ you need to abstract over (update,"
" render, serialize), make those small traits, and let concrete types compose"
" data."
msgstr ""
"不要试图用 trait 和 `Deref` 模拟类层次结构。如果你发现自己在设计 `trait Entity`、`trait Actor: "
"Entity`、`trait Pawn: Actor`，请退一步。问问自己需要抽象的是哪些<em>行为</em>（更新、渲染、序列化），把它们做成小的 "
"trait，然后让具体类型去组合数据。"

#: src/foundations/traits-and-generics.md:348
msgid "The orphan rule"
msgstr "孤儿规则"

#: src/foundations/traits-and-generics.md:350
msgid ""
"You may write `impl Trait for Type` only if your crate defines the trait or "
"the type (or both). You cannot implement `std::fmt::Display` for `Vec<u8>`, "
"because neither is yours. This **coherence** rule guarantees there is at "
"most one implementation of a trait for a type in the whole program, so "
"adding a dependency can never make two implementations clash, the way two "
"libraries' `operator<<` overloads or template specializations can in C++."
msgstr ""
"只有当你的 crate 定义了 trait 或类型（或两者都定义了）时，你才能编写 `impl Trait for Type`。你不能为 "
"`Vec<u8>` 实现 "
"`std::fmt::Display`，因为两者都不是你的。这条**一致性**（coherence）规则保证在整个程序中，一个类型对一个 trait "
"最多只有一个实现，所以添加一个依赖永远不会造成两个实现冲突；而在 C++ 中，两个库的 `operator<<` 重载或模板特化就可能冲突。"

#: src/foundations/traits-and-generics.md:357
msgid ""
"The usual workaround is a newtype: `struct Bytes(Vec<u8>);` is your type, so"
" you may implement anything for it."
msgstr "常见的变通办法是 newtype：`struct Bytes(Vec<u8>);` 是你自己的类型，所以你可以为它实现任何东西。"

