#: src/foundations/operators-and-conversions.md:103
msgid ""
"What you can overload: `+ - * / %`, the bitwise operators `& | ^ ! << >>`, "
"unary `-`, their compound-assignment forms (`+=` and so on), indexing `[]`, "
"and dereference `*` (through `Deref`, below). Comparisons come from "
"`PartialEq` and `PartialOrd`."
msgstr ""
"可以重载的有：`+ - * / %`、位运算符 `& | ^ ! << >>`、一元 `-`、它们的复合赋值形式（`+=` 等）、索引 "
"`[]`，以及解引用 `*`（通过下文的 `Deref`）。比较运算来自 `PartialEq` 和 `PartialOrd`。"

#: src/foundations/operators-and-conversions.md:108
msgid ""
"What you cannot overload: `&&`, `||`, assignment `=`, the comma, `->`, "
"`new`, function call `()` on your own types (closures fill that role), and "
"conversion operators. There is no operator to overload for a copy, either: "
"`Copy` types are always copied bit for bit."
msgstr ""
"不能重载的有：`&&`、`||`、赋值 `=`、逗号、`->`、`new`、对自定义类型的函数调用 "
"`()`（由闭包承担这个角色），以及转换运算符。复制也没有可重载的运算符：`Copy` 类型总是逐位复制。"

#: src/foundations/operators-and-conversions.md:116
msgid ""
"`Add` takes `self` by value. For small `Copy` types like `Vec3` that is "
"ideal, since they are passed in registers. For large types (a 4x4 matrix is "
"64 bytes) it is common to also implement `Add<&Mat4> for &Mat4` so `&a + &b`"
" avoids copies, though in practice the optimizer usually removes them either"
" way. Check the assembly before you complicate the API."
msgstr ""
"`Add` 按值接收 `self`。对于 `Vec3` 这样的小型 `Copy` 类型来说这很理想，因为它们通过寄存器传递。对于大类型（4x4 矩阵有 "
"64 字节），常见做法是再实现 `Add<&Mat4> for &Mat4`，让 `&a + &b` "
"避免复制，不过实践中优化器通常两种情况下都能消除复制。在把 API 搞复杂之前，先看看汇编。"

#: src/foundations/operators-and-conversions.md:124
msgid "Copy and Clone"
msgstr "Copy 与 Clone"

#: src/foundations/operators-and-conversions.md:126
msgid "[Ownership](ownership.md) introduced these; here are the details:"
msgstr "[所有权](ownership.md)一章介绍过它们，下面是细节："

#: src/foundations/operators-and-conversions.md:128
msgid ""
"`Clone` is an explicit, possibly expensive duplicate: `let b = a.clone();`. "
"You can implement it by hand or derive it, which clones each field."
msgstr ""
"`Clone` 是显式的、可能很昂贵的复制：`let b = a.clone();`。你可以手动实现它，也可以派生它，派生的实现会克隆每个字段。"

#: src/foundations/operators-and-conversions.md:130
msgid ""
"`Copy` is a marker that says \"duplicating my bytes is a valid copy\". It "
"changes assignment and argument passing from a move to a copy. `Copy` "
"requires `Clone`, and you cannot customize it: a `Copy` type's clone must be"
" a plain bitwise copy."
msgstr ""
"`Copy` 是一个标记，表示“复制我的字节就是有效的拷贝”。它把赋值和传参从移动变成复制。`Copy` 要求实现 "
"`Clone`，而且不能自定义：`Copy` 类型的 clone 必须是普通的逐位复制。"

#: src/foundations/operators-and-conversions.md:134
msgid ""
"A type can be `Copy` only if all its fields are `Copy`, and it does not "
"implement `Drop`."
msgstr "只有当一个类型的所有字段都是 `Copy`，且它没有实现 `Drop` 时，它才能是 `Copy`。"

#: src/foundations/operators-and-conversions.md:137
msgid ""
"So a Rust `Copy` type is what C++ calls _trivially copyable_, and there is "
"no way to write a type with an expensive implicit copy, like `std::string`. "
"The copy-constructor bugs (slicing, accidental deep copies in a range-for, "
"copying a `std::vector` into a lambda) do not have a Rust counterpart."
msgstr ""
"所以 Rust 的 `Copy` 类型就是 C++ 所说的<em>可平凡复制</em>类型，你无法写出像 `std::string` "
"那样带有昂贵隐式拷贝的类型。拷贝构造函数带来的 bug（对象切片、range-for 中意外的深拷贝、把 `std::vector` 拷贝进 "
"lambda）在 Rust 中都没有对应物。"

