#: src/foundations/collections.md:215
msgid ""
"Why no `s[i]`? Because in UTF-8 a character is one to four bytes, so \"the "
"i-th character\" is an O(n) scan and \"the i-th byte\" may be half a "
"character. Rust makes you say which you mean: `s.as_bytes()[i]` for bytes, "
"`s.chars()` for Unicode scalar values. For ASCII-only data (like many file "
"formats), work on `&[u8]` and byte literals `b\"...\"`."
msgstr ""
"为什么没有 `s[i]`？因为在 UTF-8 中一个字符占一到四个字节，所以“第 i 个字符”需要 O(n) 的扫描，而“第 i "
"个字节”可能只是半个字符。Rust 要你说清楚你指的是什么：字节用 `s.as_bytes()[i]`，Unicode 标量值用 "
"`s.chars()`。对于只含 ASCII 的数据（比如很多文件格式），直接操作 `&[u8]` 和字节字面量 `b\"...\"`。"

#: src/foundations/collections.md:221
msgid ""
"Take `&str` in function parameters, not `&String`: a `&String` coerces to "
"`&str` automatically, and literals are already `&str`."
msgstr "函数参数请接收 `&str` 而不是 `&String`：`&String` 会自动转换为 `&str`，而字面量本来就是 `&str`。"

#: src/foundations/collections.md:227
msgid ""
"`String` is literally a `Vec<u8>` with a UTF-8 guarantee: pointer, capacity,"
" length, 24 bytes. There is **no small-string optimization**, so every non-"
"empty `String` allocates. If you build many tiny strings (entity names, "
"debug labels), consider interning them into IDs, or crates like `smol_str` "
"or `compact_str`."
msgstr ""
"`String` 实际上就是一个带有 UTF-8 保证的 `Vec<u8>`：指针、容量、长度，共 24 "
"字节。它**没有小字符串优化**，所以每个非空的 `String` "
"都会分配内存。如果你要创建大量很小的字符串（实体名称、调试标签），可以考虑把它们驻留（intern）成 ID，或者使用 "
"`smol_str`、`compact_str` 这类 crate。"

