#: src/foundations/closures-and-iterators.md:3
msgid ""
"Rust code uses closures and iterator chains where C++ uses raw loops, "
"`<algorithm>` and (in C++20) ranges. Engine programmers are rightly "
"suspicious of this style in C++, where it can hide allocations and defeat "
"the optimizer in debug builds. In Rust it is the idiomatic style, and in "
"optimized builds it compiles to the same loop you would write by hand. This "
"chapter shows how closures capture, how iterators work, and how to confirm "
"the cost yourself."
msgstr ""
"在 C++ 使用裸循环、`<algorithm>` 和（C++20 的）ranges 的地方，Rust 代码使用闭包和迭代器链。引擎程序员对 C++ "
"中的这种风格心存疑虑是有道理的，因为它可能隐藏内存分配，并在调试构建中让优化器失效。而在 Rust "
"中，这是惯用的风格，在优化构建中会编译成和你手写的循环一样的代码。本章介绍闭包如何捕获变量、迭代器如何工作，以及如何自己确认它们的开销。"

#: src/foundations/closures-and-iterators.md:10
msgid "Closures"
msgstr "闭包"

#: src/foundations/closures-and-iterators.md:12
msgid ""
"A closure is an anonymous function that can capture variables from its "
"environment, like a C++ lambda:"
msgstr "闭包是一个可以从所在环境中捕获变量的匿名函数，类似 C++ 的 lambda："

#: src/foundations/closures-and-iterators.md:35
msgid "// borrows `scale`\n"
msgstr "// 借用 `scale`\n"

#: src/foundations/closures-and-iterators.md:37
msgid "// mutably borrows `count`\n"
msgstr "// 可变借用 `count`\n"

#: src/foundations/closures-and-iterators.md:40
msgid "// takes ownership of `v`\n"
msgstr "// 获取 `v` 的所有权\n"

#: src/foundations/closures-and-iterators.md:48
msgid ""
"The big difference: **you do not write a capture list**. The compiler looks "
"at what the body does with each variable and captures it the least powerful "
"way that works: by shared reference if it only reads, by mutable reference "
"if it mutates, by value if it moves the variable. The `move` keyword forces "
"capture by value for everything, which you need when the closure outlives "
"the current scope (threads, callbacks stored in structs)."
msgstr ""
"最大的区别是：**你不需要写捕获列表**。编译器会查看函数体如何使用每个变量，并以足够用的最弱方式捕获它：只读就按共享引用捕获，修改就按可变引用捕获，移动就按值捕获。`move`"
" 关键字会强制所有变量按值捕获，当闭包要比当前作用域活得更久时（线程、存储在结构体中的回调），就需要它。"

#: src/foundations/closures-and-iterators.md:55
msgid ""
"Dangling captures, the classic `[&]` bug, are impossible: a closure that "
