"Adapters (`map`, `filter`, `zip`, `enumerate`, `take`, `skip`, `chain`, "
"`flat_map`, `rev`, `step_by`, `windows`…) wrap an iterator in another "
"iterator. They are **lazy**: nothing happens until a consumer (`sum`, "
"`count`, `collect`, `fold`, `for_each`, `min_by`, `any`, `position`…) pulls "
"values through."
msgstr ""
