#: src/foundations/smart-pointers.md:3
msgid ""
"You know `std::unique_ptr` and `std::shared_ptr`. Rust has direct "
"equivalents, `Box` and `Rc`/`Arc`, and they behave the way you expect, with "
"two twists: ownership rules apply to them like to everything else, so many "
"of their C++ footguns disappear, and shared ownership combines with Rust's "
"\"shared XOR mutable\" rule in a way that needs a new tool, **interior "
"mutability**."
msgstr ""
"你熟悉 `std::unique_ptr` 和 `std::shared_ptr`。Rust 有直接的对应物 `Box` 和 "
"`Rc`/`Arc`，它们的行为也符合你的预期，只是有两点不同：所有权规则对它们和对其他一切一样适用，所以它们在 C++ "
"中的许多陷阱都消失了；而共享所有权与 Rust 的“共享与可变互斥”规则结合时，需要一个新工具：**内部可变性**。"

#: src/foundations/smart-pointers.md:11
msgid "`Box<T>` and when you actually need it,"
msgstr "`Box<T>`，以及什么时候真正需要它；"

#: src/foundations/smart-pointers.md:12
