#: src/foundations/smart-pointers.md:94
msgid ""
"Why two types? `shared_ptr` always uses atomic increments, because it cannot"
" know whether it will be shared across threads. Rust can know: `Rc` uses "
"plain, non-atomic counts and the compiler **forbids sending it to another "
"thread** (it does not implement `Send`; see "
"[Concurrency](../systems/concurrency.md)). `Arc` (\"atomically reference "
"counted\") uses atomic counts and can be shared between threads. You get the"
" cheap version by default and the compiler tells you when you need the "
"expensive one."
msgstr ""
"为什么要有两个类型？`shared_ptr` 总是使用原子递增，因为它无法知道自己会不会在线程之间共享。Rust 能知道：`Rc` "
"使用普通的非原子计数，并且编译器**禁止把它发送到另一个线程**（它没有实现 "
"`Send`；参见[并发](../systems/concurrency.md)）。`Arc`（“atomically reference "
"counted”，原子引用计数）使用原子计数，可以在线程之间共享。默认你得到的是便宜的版本，需要昂贵版本时编译器会告诉你。"

#: src/foundations/smart-pointers.md:102
msgid "Two more differences from `shared_ptr`:"
msgstr "与 `shared_ptr` 还有两点不同："

#: src/foundations/smart-pointers.md:104
msgid ""
"The value inside an `Rc` is **immutable** through the `Rc`. `Rc<T>` gives "
"you `&T`, never `&mut T`, because other owners might be reading it. Mutation"
" needs interior mutability, below."
msgstr ""
"通过 `Rc` 访问时，其中的值是**不可变的**。`Rc<T>` 只给你 `&T`，永远不给 `&mut "
"T`，因为其他所有者可能正在读取它。要修改就需要下文介绍的内部可变性。"

#: src/foundations/smart-pointers.md:107
msgid ""
"`Rc::new` allocates the counts and the value together, like "
"`std::make_shared`. There is no separate control block."
msgstr "`Rc::new` 把计数和值分配在一起，类似 `std::make_shared`。没有单独的控制块。"

#: src/foundations/smart-pointers.md:110
msgid "`Weak<T>` and cycles"
msgstr "`Weak<T>` 与循环"

#: src/foundations/smart-pointers.md:112
msgid ""
"Reference counting cannot free cycles: if A owns B and B owns A, both counts"
" stay above zero forever. As with `weak_ptr`, the fix is a non-owning `Weak`"
" pointer for back-edges such as child-to-parent links. `upgrade()` returns "
"an `Option<Rc<T>>`, which is `None` once the value is gone:"
msgstr ""
