#: src/foundations/smart-pointers.md:154
msgid ""
"This works, but look at how much ceremony a parent/child tree takes: `Rc`, "
"`Weak`, `RefCell`, `borrow_mut`, `upgrade`. That is a strong hint. In Rust, "
"graphs of objects that point at each other are usually better stored in an "
"arena with indices or handles; see [Handles and arenas](../engine/handles-"
"and-arenas.md). A scene graph becomes a `Vec<Node>` where `parent: "
"Option<NodeId>`."
msgstr ""
"这样做可行，但看看一棵父子树需要多少仪式性的代码：`Rc`、`Weak`、`RefCell`、`borrow_mut`、`upgrade`。这是一个强烈的暗示。在"
" Rust 中，互相指向的对象图通常更适合存放在 arena 中，用索引或句柄来引用；参见[句柄与 arena](../engine/handles-"
"and-arenas.md)。场景图就变成了一个 `Vec<Node>`，其中 `parent: Option<NodeId>`。"

#: src/foundations/smart-pointers.md:161
msgid "Interior mutability: `Cell` and `RefCell`"
msgstr "内部可变性：`Cell` 与 `RefCell`"

#: src/foundations/smart-pointers.md:163
msgid ""
"The borrow rules say: many `&T` _or_ one `&mut T`. Sometimes you need to "
"mutate something that is reachable only through a shared reference: a cache "
"inside an otherwise immutable object, a counter in an `Rc`, the children "
"list above. C++ has `mutable` for the first case and nothing in particular "
"for the rest."
msgstr ""
"借用规则说：多个 `&T` <em>或</em> 一个 `&mut "
"T`。有时你需要修改某个只能通过共享引用访问到的东西：一个本来不可变的对象内部的缓存、`Rc` 中的一个计数器、上面的子节点列表。C++ 对第一种情况有"
" `mutable`，对其余情况则没有特别的办法。"

#: src/foundations/smart-pointers.md:168
msgid ""
"Rust's answer is types that allow mutation through `&self` while keeping the"
" guarantees, by checking in a different way:"
msgstr "Rust 的答案是一些允许通过 `&self` 进行修改的类型，它们换了一种检查方式来维持保证："

