#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:3
msgid ""
"The [Modules and files](modules.md) chapter covered how modules map to files"
" and how `use` and `pub` work. Now that `impl` blocks and traits are "
"familiar, this chapter covers the questions that come up once a project "
"grows past a few files:"
msgstr ""
"[模块与文件](modules.md)一章讲了模块如何对应到文件，以及 `use` 和 `pub` 如何工作。现在你已经熟悉了 `impl` 块和 "
"trait，本章讨论项目超过几个文件之后会遇到的问题："

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:8
msgid "where methods can be defined, and what callers have to import,"
msgstr "方法可以定义在哪里，调用方需要导入什么；"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:9
msgid "laying out a workspace of crates,"
msgstr "如何布局一个由多个 crate 组成的工作区；"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:10
msgid "how crate boundaries affect compile times."
msgstr "crate 边界如何影响编译时间。"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:12
msgid "Where methods live"
msgstr "方法写在哪里"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:14
msgid ""
"In C++, a member function is visible where its declaration has been "
"`#include`d. Rust has no textual inclusion, so the question becomes: if one "
"file defines a type and another file adds methods to it, what do callers "
"have to import?"
msgstr ""
"在 C++ 中，成员函数在其声明被 `#include` 的地方可见。Rust "
"没有文本包含，所以问题变成了：如果一个文件定义了某个类型，另一个文件给它添加了方法，调用者需要导入什么？"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:19
msgid ""
"**For your own types: nothing extra.** An `impl` block can sit in any module"
" of the crate that defines the type. Its methods belong to the type, not to "
"the file they were written in, so anyone who can reach a value of the type "
"can call them (subject to `pub`). There is nothing to import for the second "
"file:"
msgstr ""
"**对于你自己的类型：什么都不用额外导入。** `impl` 块可以写在定义该类型的 crate "
"中的任何模块里。方法属于类型本身，而不属于编写它的那个文件，所以任何能拿到该类型值的代码都能调用它们（受 `pub` "
"约束）。不需要为第二个文件导入任何东西："

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:29
msgid "// could be src/mesh_ops.rs\n"
msgstr "// 也可以是 src/mesh_ops.rs\n"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:37
msgid "// only the type; no `use crate::mesh_ops`\n"
msgstr "// 只导入了类型；不需要 `use crate::mesh_ops`\n"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:40
msgid "\"{} vertices\""
msgstr ""

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:47
msgid ""
"`use` only creates a short name. You need `use crate::mesh::Mesh` to _write_"
" `Mesh` (to construct one or name it in a signature), not to call methods on"
" a value you already have."
msgstr ""
"`use` 只是创建一个短名字。你需要 `use crate::mesh::Mesh` 是为了<em>写出</em> `Mesh` "
"这个名字（构造它，或者在签名中提到它），而不是为了在已有的值上调用方法。"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:51
msgid ""
"**For other crates' types: an extension trait, which you do import.** You "
"cannot write `impl Vec<f32> { ... }` outside the standard library. Instead "
"you define a trait and implement it for the foreign type. Trait methods are "
"only callable where the trait is in scope, so callers must `use` the trait:"
msgstr ""
"**对于其他 crate 的类型：使用扩展 trait，这时需要导入。** 在标准库之外，你不能写 `impl Vec<f32> { ... "
"}`。取而代之的是定义一个 trait，并为这个外部类型实现它。只有在 trait 处于作用域内时才能调用 trait 方法，所以调用者必须 `use`"
" 这个 trait："

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:62
msgid "\"{} floats\""
msgstr ""

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:67
msgid "// remove this line: \"no method named `describe`\"\n"
msgstr "// 删掉这一行会报错：\"no method named `describe`\"\n"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:73
msgid ""
"This is the one place where Rust resembles \"include it to see it\", and it "
"is deliberate: two crates can add a method with the same name to the same "
"type, and only the traits you import take part in method lookup. The "
"compiler's error message names the trait to import when you forget."
msgstr ""
"这是 Rust 中唯一类似\"包含了才能看见\"的地方，而且是有意为之：两个 crate 可能给同一个类型添加同名方法，只有你导入的 trait "
"才会参与方法查找。如果忘了导入，编译器的错误信息会告诉你该导入哪个 trait。"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:78
msgid "Organizing a larger project"
msgstr "组织较大的项目"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:80
msgid "A pattern that scales well:"
msgstr "一种可以良好扩展的模式："

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:95
msgid "Inside each crate:"
msgstr "在每个 crate 内部："

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:97
msgid ""
"`lib.rs` declares modules and re-exports the public API. Keep it short."
msgstr "`lib.rs` 声明模块并重新导出公开 API。保持它简短。"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:98
msgid ""
"One module per concept (`texture.rs`, `pipeline.rs`), not per type. Rust "
"files are routinely several hundred lines."
msgstr "每个概念一个模块（`texture.rs`、`pipeline.rs`），而不是每个类型一个。Rust 文件动辄几百行是很正常的。"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:100
msgid ""
"Put unit tests at the bottom of each file in a `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` "
"([Testing chapter](../systems/testing-and-tooling.md))."
msgstr ""
"把单元测试放在每个文件末尾的 `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` 中（[测试一章](../systems/testing-and-"
"tooling.md)）。"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:102
msgid ""
"Keep `pub` surfaces small and use `pub(crate)` for helpers shared inside the"
" crate."
msgstr "让 `pub` 的接口保持精简，crate 内部共享的辅助函数用 `pub(crate)`。"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:105
msgid "Compile times and crate boundaries"
msgstr "编译时间与 crate 边界"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:107
msgid "The crate is the unit of compilation:"
msgstr "crate 是编译的单位："

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:109
msgid ""
"**Within a crate**, the compiler splits work into \"codegen units\" for "
"parallel LLVM optimization, but type checking and borrow checking run over "
"the whole crate. A change anywhere in a crate recompiles that crate "
"(incrementally, reusing what it can)."
msgstr ""
"**在一个 crate 内部**，编译器会把工作拆分成多个“代码生成单元”（codegen unit），以便并行进行 LLVM "
"优化，但类型检查和借用检查是在整个 crate 上进行的。crate 中任何地方的修改都会重新编译这个 crate（增量地，尽可能复用已有结果）。"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:113
msgid ""
"**Across crates**, a change to crate A rebuilds every crate that depends on "
"A. Crates that do not depend on each other build in parallel."
msgstr "**在 crate 之间**，对 crate A 的修改会重新构建所有依赖 A 的 crate。互不依赖的 crate 可以并行构建。"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:116
msgid ""
"So the guidance mirrors what you would do with C++ libraries, with the "
"emphasis shifted:"
msgstr "所以指导原则与你对 C++ 库的做法类似，只是侧重点有所不同："

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:119
msgid ""
"Split along stable interfaces. A math crate that rarely changes can be "
"depended on by everything at no cost."
msgstr "沿着稳定的接口拆分。一个很少变化的数学 crate 可以被所有东西依赖而不产生代价。"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:121
msgid ""
"Keep the dependency graph wide, not deep: `render`, `audio` and `physics` "
"depending only on `core` build in parallel."
msgstr "让依赖图宽而不深：只依赖 `core` 的 `render`、`audio` 和 `physics` 可以并行构建。"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:123
msgid ""
"Generic code is compiled in the crate that _uses_ it, like templates. Heavy "
"generic code in a low-level crate makes every dependent crate slower to "
"build. Where possible, have generic functions do minimal work and call a "
"non-generic inner function."
msgstr ""
"泛型代码在<em>使用</em>它的 crate 中编译，就像模板一样。底层 crate 中大量的泛型代码会让每个依赖它的 crate "
"构建得更慢。在可能的情况下，让泛型函数只做最少的工作，再调用一个非泛型的内部函数。"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:127
msgid ""
"Measure with `cargo build --timings`, which produces an HTML report of which"
" crates took how long and what ran in parallel."
msgstr ""
"用 `cargo build --timings` 来测量，它会生成一份 HTML 报告，显示每个 crate 花了多长时间、哪些是并行运行的。"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:134
msgid "Member functions are visible where the class header is included"
msgstr "成员函数在包含了类头文件的地方可见"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:134
msgid "Inherent methods are callable wherever the type is reachable"
msgstr "固有方法在任何能访问到该类型的地方都可以调用"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:135
msgid "Free functions that extend a type, found by ADL"
msgstr "扩展某个类型的自由函数，通过 ADL 查找"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:135
msgid "Extension traits, which callers must `use`"
msgstr "扩展 trait，调用方必须 `use` 它"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:136
msgid "Libraries split along stable interfaces"
msgstr "按稳定接口拆分库"

#: src/foundations/project-organization.md:136
msgid "Crates in a workspace, with a wide dependency graph"
