msgstr ""

#: src/systems/logging.md:77
msgid "// before init: nothing happens\n"
msgstr "// 初始化之前：什么都不会发生\n"

#: src/systems/logging.md:79
msgid "// info is printed, debug is filtered out\n"
msgstr "// info 被打印，debug 被过滤掉\n"

#: src/systems/logging.md:83
msgid ""
"`format_args!` captures the arguments without formatting them, so a filtered"
" message costs a comparison, not a string allocation. `module_path!()` gives"
" every message a **target** such as `my_game::render`, which is what filters"
" match on."
msgstr ""
"`format_args!` 只捕获参数而不格式化它们，所以一条被过滤掉的消息只花费一次比较，而不是一次字符串分配。`module_path!()` "
"给每条消息一个 **target**，比如 `my_game::render`，过滤规则就是根据它来匹配的。"

#: src/systems/logging.md:88
msgid ""
"The rule that follows from this design: **libraries depend only on the "
"facade, and only binaries choose a backend.** A renderer crate calls "
"`log::debug!`; the game, the editor and the test harness each decide where "
"those messages go. In C++ terms, every library logs through the same "
"interface, and the application supplies the sink."
msgstr ""
"由这个设计得出的规则是：**库只依赖门面，只有可执行程序才选择后端。** 渲染器 crate 调用 "
"`log::debug!`；游戏、编辑器和测试框架各自决定这些消息去哪里。用 C++ 的话说，每个库都通过同一个接口记录日志，由应用程序提供输出端。"

#: src/systems/logging.md:94
msgid "`log` and `env_logger`"
msgstr "`log` 与 `env_logger`"

#: src/systems/logging.md:96
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"log = \"0.4\"\n"
"env_logger = \"0.11\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/logging.md:107
msgid "\"{meshes} draw calls this frame\""
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/logging.md:113
msgid "// reads RUST_LOG\n"
msgstr "// 读取 RUST_LOG\n"

#: src/systems/logging.md:114
msgid "\"starting\""
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/logging.md:129
msgid ""
"`RUST_LOG` is a list of `target=level` rules, plus an optional default "
"level. Because targets are module paths, you can turn on `debug` for one "
"subsystem, or silence a chatty dependency (`wgpu_core=warn`), without "
"recompiling. Most crates that log, including wgpu, winit and many others, "
"use `log`, so their messages appear in the same output."
msgstr ""
"`RUST_LOG` 是一组 `target=level` 规则，外加一个可选的默认级别。因为 target "
"就是模块路径，所以无需重新编译，你就可以只为某个子系统打开 "
"`debug`，或者让一个话多的依赖安静下来（`wgpu_core=warn`）。大多数会记录日志的 crate，包括 wgpu、winit 等，都使用"
" `log`，所以它们的消息也会出现在同一个输出里。"

#: src/systems/logging.md:135
msgid "`tracing`: structured fields and spans"
msgstr "`tracing`：结构化字段与 span"

#: src/systems/logging.md:137
msgid ""
"[`tracing`](https://docs.rs/tracing) is the other common facade, and the "
"better fit for a game. It has the same level macros, plus two things `log` "
"lacks:"
msgstr ""
"[`tracing`](https://docs.rs/tracing) 是另一个常用的门面，也更适合游戏。它有同样的级别宏，外加两样 `log` "
"没有的东西："

#: src/systems/logging.md:141
msgid ""
"**Structured fields.** `info!(entity = id, hp, \"took damage\")` records "
"`entity` and `hp` as typed key-value pairs, not just text. A backend can "
"print them, filter on them or send them to a log database."
msgstr ""
"**结构化字段。** `info!(entity = id, hp, \"took damage\")` 会把 `entity` 和 `hp` "
"记录为带类型的键值对，而不只是文本。后端可以打印它们、按它们过滤，或者把它们发送到日志数据库。"

#: src/systems/logging.md:144
msgid ""
"**Spans.** A span is a named period of time with fields, such as one frame, "
"one system or one asset load. Every event inside a span is reported with the"
" span's context, and a profiler backend can show spans on a timeline."
msgstr ""
"**span。** span 是一段带有字段的命名时间段，比如一帧、一个系统的执行或一次资源加载。span 内的每个事件在报告时都带着 span "
"的上下文，性能分析后端还能把 span 显示在时间线上。"

#: src/systems/logging.md:148
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"tracing = \"0.1\"\n"
"tracing-subscriber = { version = \"0.3\", features = [\"env-filter\"] }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/logging.md:159
msgid "// a span per call, with fields\n"
msgstr "// 每次调用一个 span，并带上字段\n"

#: src/systems/logging.md:164
msgid "\"enemy died\""
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/logging.md:166
msgid "\"took damage\""
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/logging.md:173
msgid "// RUST_LOG\n"
msgstr "// RUST_LOG\n"

#: src/systems/logging.md:178
msgid "\"frame\""
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/logging.md:178
msgid "// ends when `_frame` is dropped\n"
msgstr "// `_frame` 被丢弃时结束\n"

#: src/systems/logging.md:181
msgid "\"level not cleared\""
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/logging.md:193
msgid ""
"The output above omits timestamps. Each event carries the chain of spans it "
"happened in, so \"took damage\" is known to belong to frame 1 and to "
"`update_ai`, without passing a context object around. `#[instrument]` is an "
"attribute macro ([Declaring your own "
"attributes](../intro/syntax.md#declaring-your-own-attributes)) that wraps "
"the function in a span named after it."
msgstr ""
"上面的输出省略了时间戳。每个事件都带着它所在的 span 链，所以无需四处传递上下文对象，就能知道 \"took damage\" 属于第 1 帧和 "
"`update_ai`。`#[instrument]` "
"是一个属性宏（[声明自己的属性](../intro/syntax.md#声明自己的属性)），它把函数包进一个以函数名命名的 span 里。"

#: src/systems/logging.md:199
msgid ""
"The backend is called a **subscriber**, and it is built from **layers**: one"
" layer formats to the terminal, another writes a file, another sends spans "
"to a profiler. `tracing-subscriber` also captures messages from crates that "
"use `log`, so `wgpu` and `winit` output appears in the same stream."
msgstr ""
"后端称为 **subscriber**，由多个 **layer** 组成：一个 layer 格式化输出到终端，另一个写文件，还有一个把 span "
"发送给性能分析器。`tracing-subscriber` 还会接收使用 `log` 的 crate 发出的消息，所以 `wgpu` 和 `winit`"
" 的输出也会出现在同一个流里。"

#: src/systems/logging.md:204
msgid ""
"The same spans feed the profiler. Add the `tracing-tracy` layer and every "
"span becomes a zone in [Tracy](https://github.com/wolfpld/tracy), the frame "
"profiler many C++ engines already use ([Memory layout and "
"performance](memory-and-performance.md)). The `frame` span above needs no "
"extra code to appear on the timeline."
msgstr ""
"同样的 span 也能喂给性能分析器。加上 `tracing-tracy` layer，每个 span 就会成为 "
"[Tracy](https://github.com/wolfpld/tracy) 中的一个 zone，而 Tracy 正是许多 C++ "
"引擎已经在用的帧性能分析器（[内存布局与性能](memory-and-performance.md)）。上面的 `frame` span "
"不需要额外代码就能出现在时间线上。"

#: src/systems/logging.md:210
msgid "Engine needs"
msgstr "引擎的需求"

#: src/systems/logging.md:212
msgid "Log files that do not stall a frame"
msgstr "不会卡住帧的日志文件"

#: src/systems/logging.md:214
msgid ""
"Writing to a file from the game thread can block on disk I/O. `tracing-"
"appender` moves the writing to a background thread and rotates the file "
"daily or hourly:"
msgstr "在游戏线程上写文件可能会阻塞在磁盘 I/O 上。`tracing-appender` 把写入移到后台线程，并按天或按小时轮换文件："

#: src/systems/logging.md:218
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"tracing-appender = \"0.2\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/logging.md:227
msgid "\"logs\""
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/logging.md:227
msgid "\"game.log\""
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/logging.md:229
