msgstr "如何判断一个 crate 是否可信，以及有哪些工具可以帮忙；"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:15
msgid "using crates well: features, the lock file, forks and vendoring,"
msgstr "用好 crate：feature、lock 文件、fork 和 vendor；"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:16
msgid "contributing to other people's crates,"
msgstr "为别人的 crate 做贡献；"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:17
msgid "publishing your own crate on crates.io, or only on GitHub."
msgstr "在 crates.io 上发布自己的 crate，或者只发布在 GitHub 上。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:19
msgid "How crates.io is organized"
msgstr "crates.io 是怎样组织的"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:21
msgid ""
"crates.io is the Rust community's package registry, run by the crates.io "
"team under the Rust project. A few rules shape everything else:"
msgstr "crates.io 是 Rust 社区的包注册中心，由 Rust 项目下的 crates.io 团队运营。几条规则决定了其他的一切："

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:24
msgid ""
"**Packages are source code.** A published version is a `.crate` file, a "
"gzipped tarball of the source and its `Cargo.toml`. There are no binaries: "
"Cargo builds every dependency on your machine with your compiler and flags."
msgstr ""
"**包就是源代码。** 发布的每个版本是一个 `.crate` 文件，也就是源代码加上 `Cargo.toml` 的 gzip "
"压缩包。这里没有二进制文件：Cargo 会在你的机器上，用你的编译器和编译选项构建每一个依赖。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:27
msgid ""
"**The namespace is flat.** Names are first come, first served, and there are"
" no organization prefixes like `@company/name`. Related crates use naming "
"conventions instead: `foo`, `foo-sys` (raw FFI bindings to a C library), "
"`foo-derive` or `foo-macros` (procedural macros), `foo-core`."
msgstr ""
"**命名空间是扁平的。** 名字先到先得，没有 `@company/name` 这样的组织前缀。相关的 crate "
"靠命名约定来组织：`foo`、`foo-sys`（C 库的原始 FFI 绑定）、`foo-derive` 或 `foo-"
"macros`（过程宏）、`foo-core`。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:31
msgid ""
"**Versions are immutable.** You cannot change or replace a published "
"version. You can **yank** it: new projects will not select it, but projects "
"whose `Cargo.lock` already uses it keep building. Deleting a crate entirely "
"is only possible under narrow conditions (shortly after publishing, or with "
"few downloads and no dependents), so a build that works today keeps working."
msgstr ""
"**版本不可修改。** 已经发布的版本不能修改，也不能替换。你可以 **yank**（撤回）它：新项目不会再选中这个版本，但 `Cargo.lock` "
"里已经用到它的项目照常构建。只有在很窄的条件下（刚发布不久，或者下载量很少且没有被依赖）才能彻底删除一个 "
"crate，所以今天能构建的项目，以后也能构建。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:36
msgid ""
"**Every crate has owners.** Owners are users or GitHub teams, and only they "
"can publish new versions. Accounts are GitHub logins."
msgstr "**每个 crate 都有所有者。** 所有者可以是用户或 GitHub 团队，只有他们能发布新版本。账号就是 GitHub 登录。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:38
msgid ""
"**Metadata comes from `Cargo.toml`.** Description, license, repository, "
"keywords and categories are shown on the crate page, along with the README, "
"every version, download counts and the list of crates that depend on it."
msgstr ""
"**元数据来自 `Cargo.toml`。** 描述、许可证、代码仓库、关键词和分类都会显示在 crate 页面上，同时显示的还有 "
"README、所有版本、下载量，以及依赖它的 crate 列表。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:42
msgid ""
"Two services sit next to crates.io and work for every crate automatically:"
msgstr "crates.io 旁边还有两项服务，对每个 crate 自动生效："

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:44
msgid ""
"[docs.rs](https://docs.rs) builds the API documentation of every published "
"version. A link like `docs.rs/glam/0.30` is the reference for that version, "
"so you never read docs for the wrong release."
msgstr ""
"[docs.rs](https://docs.rs) 会为每个发布的版本构建 API 文档。像 `docs.rs/glam/0.30` "
"这样的链接就是那个版本的参考文档，所以你永远不会读错版本的文档。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:47
msgid ""
"The **index** is the metadata Cargo downloads to resolve versions. Cargo "
"fetches only the entries it needs (the \"sparse\" protocol), which is why "
"resolving is fast even though the registry has hundreds of thousands of "
"crates."
msgstr ""
"**索引**是 Cargo 解析版本时下载的元数据。Cargo 只获取它需要的条目（即 \"sparse\" 协议），所以即使注册中心有几十万个 "
"crate，解析依然很快。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:52
msgid "Finding crates"
msgstr "寻找 crate"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:54
msgid "Where"
msgstr "在哪里"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:56
msgid "[crates.io](https://crates.io) search, categories and keywords"
msgstr "[crates.io](https://crates.io) 的搜索、分类和关键词"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:56
msgid "The registry itself. Sort by recent downloads, not all-time downloads"
msgstr "注册中心本身。按近期下载量排序，而不是按总下载量"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:57
msgid "[lib.rs](https://lib.rs)"
msgstr "[lib.rs](https://lib.rs)"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:57
msgid ""
"An independent index of the same crates, with better ranking and categories"
msgstr "同样这些 crate 的独立索引，排名和分类做得更好"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:58
msgid "[blessed.rs](https://blessed.rs)"
msgstr "[blessed.rs](https://blessed.rs)"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:58
msgid "A short curated list of the de facto standard crate for each job"
msgstr "一份简短的精选清单，列出每类工作事实上的标准 crate"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:59
msgid "[Are we game yet?](https://arewegameyet.rs)"
msgstr "[Are we game yet?](https://arewegameyet.rs)"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:59
msgid "Game development crates: engines, graphics, audio, physics, networking"
msgstr "游戏开发相关的 crate：引擎、图形、音频、物理、网络"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:60
msgid "A crate page's \"Dependents\" tab"
msgstr "crate 页面上的 \"Dependents\" 标签页"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:60
msgid "Who already relies on it, and how much"
msgstr "已经有谁依赖它，依赖程度如何"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:62
msgid ""
"For common jobs there is usually one crate the community has settled on: "
"serde for serialization, tokio for async I/O, rayon for data parallelism, "
"anyhow and thiserror for errors, clap for command-line parsing, tracing for "
"logging. Start there before you compare alternatives."
msgstr ""
"常见的工作通常都有一个社区公认的 crate：序列化用 serde，异步 I/O 用 tokio，数据并行用 rayon，错误处理用 anyhow 和 "
"thiserror，命令行解析用 clap，日志用 tracing。先从它们开始，再去比较其他选择。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:67
msgid "What Cargo does with a dependency"
msgstr "Cargo 如何处理一个依赖"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:69
msgid ""
"Package management is one of C++'s weak points: there is no standard package"
" format, no standard build description, and no stable ABI, so every library "
"has to be adapted to every build system, compiler and configuration. Rust "
"avoids most of that with a single design: **one tool, one package format, "
"and everything built from source by the same compiler.** This section "
"follows one line of `Cargo.toml` through the whole process."
msgstr ""
"包管理是 C++ 的弱项之一：没有标准的包格式，没有标准的构建描述，也没有稳定的 ABI，所以每个库都要针对每种构建系统、编译器和配置做适配。Rust "
"用一个设计避开了其中的大部分问题：**一个工具，一种包格式，所有代码都由同一个编译器从源代码构建。** 本节跟踪 `Cargo.toml` "
"里的一行，看它经历的完整过程。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:76
msgid "Resolving versions"
msgstr "解析版本"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:78
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"glam = { version = \"0.30\", features = [\"serde\"] }\n"
"serde_json = \"1\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:84
msgid ""
"On the first build, Cargo downloads the index entries for these crates and "
"their dependencies, and picks one exact version for each:"
msgstr "第一次构建时，Cargo 会下载这些 crate 及其依赖的索引条目，并为每个 crate 选出一个确切的版本："

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:87
msgid ""
"A requirement like `\"1\"` or `\"0.30\"` is a caret range: `\"1\"` means "
"`>=1.0.0, <2.0.0`, and `\"0.30\"` means `>=0.30.0, <0.31.0`. Use "
"`\"=1.2.3\"` to pin, or `\">=1.2, <1.5\"` for a custom range, but rarely."
msgstr ""
"`\"1\"` 或 `\"0.30\"` 这样的版本要求是插入符（caret）范围：`\"1\"` 表示 `>=1.0.0, "
"<2.0.0`，`\"0.30\"` 表示 `>=0.30.0, <0.31.0`。用 `\"=1.2.3\"` 可以锁定版本，`\">=1.2, "
"<1.5\"` 可以自定义范围，但很少需要。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:90
msgid ""
"For each crate, Cargo picks the **newest version that satisfies every "
"requirement** on it anywhere in the graph. In edition 2024 it also prefers "
"versions whose declared `rust-version` your compiler supports."
msgstr ""
"对每个 crate，Cargo 会选出**满足依赖图中所有要求的最新版本**。在 edition 2024 中，它还会优先选择声明的 `rust-"
"version` 被你的编译器支持的版本。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:93
msgid ""
"It writes the result to `Cargo.lock`. Later builds use the lock file and do "
"not resolve again until you run `cargo update` or change `Cargo.toml`."
msgstr ""
"结果写入 `Cargo.lock`。之后的构建直接使用 lock 文件，不会重新解析，除非你运行 `cargo update` 或修改 "
"`Cargo.toml`。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:102
msgid ""
"The last line is Cargo telling you that a newer, semver-incompatible glam "
"exists, which you would have to opt into by changing `\"0.30\"`."
msgstr "最后一行是 Cargo 在告诉你：glam 有一个更新的、semver 不兼容的版本，要用它就得自己去改 `\"0.30\"`。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:105
msgid "One version or two"
msgstr "一个版本还是两个版本"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:107
msgid ""
"If `render` asks for `log = \"0.4.17\"` and `audio` asks for `log = "
"\"0.4.20\"`, both requirements are in the same semver range, so Cargo "
"**unifies** them: one copy of `log`, at a version that satisfies both "
"(0.4.20 or newer). This is the diamond dependency, solved automatically."
msgstr ""
"如果 `render` 要求 `log = \"0.4.17\"`，`audio` 要求 `log = \"0.4.20\"`，两个要求在同一个 "
"semver 范围内，Cargo 就会把它们**统一**起来：只有一份 `log`，版本同时满足两者（0.4.20 "
"或更新）。这就是菱形依赖，被自动解决了。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:112
msgid ""
"If the requirements are incompatible (`rand = \"0.8\"` and `rand = "
"\"0.9\"`), Cargo builds **both versions** and links both into the binary. "
"Their symbols are mangled with a hash of the crate's identity, so they do "
"not collide, and their types are different types, so passing a `rand 0.8` "
"value to code that expects `rand 0.9` is a compile error rather than an ODR "
"violation. The cost is build time and binary size, which is why `cargo tree "
"-d` and `cargo deny`'s `multiple-versions` check are worth running."
msgstr ""
"如果要求互不兼容（`rand = \"0.8\"` 和 `rand = \"0.9\"`），Cargo "
"会**同时构建两个版本**，并都链接进二进制文件。它们的符号在改编（mangle）时带有 crate "
"身份的哈希，所以不会冲突；它们的类型也是不同的类型，所以把 `rand 0.8` 的值传给需要 `rand 0.9` 的代码是编译错误，而不是 ODR "
"违规。代价是构建时间和二进制体积，所以值得运行 `cargo tree -d` 和 `cargo deny` 的 `multiple-versions`"
" 检查。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:120
msgid ""
"The exception is native code. A crate that links a C library declares it "
"with `links = \"z\"` in its `Cargo.toml`, and Cargo refuses to put two "
"crates that link the same native library into one graph, because C symbols "
"have no hash to keep them apart. You get an error at resolve time, not a "
"crash at run time."
msgstr ""
"例外是原生代码。链接 C 库的 crate 要在 `Cargo.toml` 里用 `links = \"z\"` 声明，Cargo 不允许依赖图中有两个"
" crate 链接同一个原生库，因为 C 符号没有哈希来区分。你会在解析时得到错误，而不是在运行时崩溃。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:125
msgid "Features are unified"
msgstr "feature 是统一的"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:127
msgid ""
"Features ([Cargo chapter](../foundations/cargo.md#features-conditional-"
"compilation)) are resolved across the whole graph: if any crate enables a "
"feature of a dependency, every user of that dependency gets it. `cargo tree "
"-e features` shows why a feature is on:"
msgstr ""
"feature（[Cargo 一章](../foundations/cargo.md#feature条件编译)）在整个依赖图上统一解析：只要有一个 "
"crate 启用了某个依赖的 feature，这个依赖的所有使用者都会得到它。`cargo tree -e features` 能显示某个 "
"feature 为什么被打开："

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:132
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"$ cargo tree -e features -i serde_core\n"
"serde_core v1.0.229\n"
"├── glam v0.30.10\n"
"│   ├── glam feature \"serde\"\n"
"│   │   └── dep v0.1.0\n"
"...\n"
"└── serde_core feature \"std\"\n"
"    └── serde_json feature \"std\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:143
msgid ""
"Here `glam` asked only for `serde_core`, but `serde_json` enabled its `std` "
"feature, so `glam`'s copy has `std` too: there is only one `serde_core`. "
"This works because features are **additive** by convention: enabling a "
"feature may add API, never remove or change it. When you write a crate, "
"never make a feature that breaks code which does not use it, and never use "
"two features as mutually exclusive switches."
msgstr ""
"这里 `glam` 只要求了 `serde_core`，但 `serde_json` 启用了它的 `std` feature，所以 `glam` "
"用到的那份也带有 `std`：`serde_core` 只有一份。这之所以可行，是因为按照约定 feature 是**可叠加的**：启用一个 "
"feature 可以增加 API，但绝不删除或改变 API。自己写 crate 时，不要让某个 feature 破坏没用到它的代码，也不要把两个 "
"feature 当成互斥的开关。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:150
msgid ""
"Unification has limits that avoid the obvious problems. Dependencies of "
"build scripts and procedural macros (which run on the host) are resolved "
"separately from the code you ship, dev-dependencies only affect test builds,"
" and target-specific dependencies only affect their target."
msgstr ""
"统一也有边界，避免了明显的问题。构建脚本和过程宏（它们运行在宿主机上）的依赖，与你发布的代码分开解析；dev-dependencies "
"只影响测试构建；特定目标平台的依赖只影响对应的目标。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:155
msgid "Where things live"
msgstr "东西放在哪里"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:157
msgid "Location"
msgstr "位置"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:157
msgid "Contents"
msgstr "内容"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:159
msgid "`~/.cargo/registry/index/`"
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:159
msgid "Cached index entries"
msgstr "缓存的索引条目"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:160
msgid "`~/.cargo/registry/cache/`"
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:160
msgid "Downloaded `.crate` files, shared by all your projects"
msgstr "下载的 `.crate` 文件，所有项目共享"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:161
msgid "`~/.cargo/registry/src/`"
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:161
msgid "Unpacked sources; open them to read a dependency's code"
msgstr "解压后的源代码；想读依赖的代码就打开这里"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:162
msgid "`~/.cargo/git/`"
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:162
msgid "Git dependencies"
msgstr "Git 依赖"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:163
msgid "`target/` in each project"
msgstr "每个项目里的 `target/`"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:163
msgid "Compiled artifacts for that project"
msgstr "这个项目的编译产物"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:165
msgid ""
"Each dependency is compiled once per combination of version, features, "
"profile and target, and the artifact's file name includes a hash of that "
"combination. Changing a feature or a flag rebuilds only what it affects, and"
" debug and release builds never mix. To share compiled dependencies between "
"projects, set one `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` for all of them or use `sccache`."
msgstr ""
"每个依赖会按\"版本、feature、profile、目标平台\"的每种组合各编译一次，产物的文件名里带有这个组合的哈希。改动一个 feature "
"或编译选项只会重新构建受影响的部分，调试构建和发布构建也不会混在一起。要在多个项目之间共享编译好的依赖，可以给它们设置同一个 "
"`CARGO_TARGET_DIR`，或者使用 `sccache`。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:171
msgid "Native libraries and `-sys` crates"
msgstr "原生库与 `-sys` crate"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:173
msgid ""
"A crate that wraps a C library is usually split in two: `foo-sys` declares "
"the raw `extern \"C\"` functions and finds or builds the library, and `foo` "
"builds a safe API on top ([FFI with C and C++](ffi.md)). The `-sys` crate's "
"`build.rs` does what `find_package` and `ExternalProject_Add` do in CMake, "
"typically choosing between two strategies with a feature:"
msgstr ""
"封装 C 库的 crate 通常分成两个：`foo-sys` 声明原始的 `extern \"C\"` 函数，并负责找到或构建这个库；`foo` "
"在它之上构建安全的 API（[与 C 和 C++ 的 FFI](ffi.md)）。`-sys` crate 的 `build.rs` 做的事情相当于 "
"CMake 中的 `find_package` 和 `ExternalProject_Add`，通常通过一个 feature 在两种策略之间选择："

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:179
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"# Either use the system's SQLite, found with pkg-config (or vcpkg on Windows):\n"
"rusqlite = \"0.43\"\n"
"# or compile SQLite's C source into your binary with the `cc` crate:\n"
"# rusqlite = { version = \"0.43\", features = [\"bundled\"] }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```toml\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"# 要么使用系统里的 SQLite，通过 pkg-config（Windows 上是 vcpkg）找到：\n"
"rusqlite = \"0.43\"\n"
"# 要么用 `cc` crate 把 SQLite 的 C 源码编译进你的二进制文件：\n"
"# rusqlite = { version = \"0.43\", features = [\"bundled\"] }\n"
"```"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:187
msgid ""
"The `bundled` style is common for game dependencies (SDL, Lua, zstd, "
"mimalloc, PhysX bindings): the C source ships inside the crate, is built "
"with the `cc` or `cmake` crate, and is statically linked, so users need only"
" a C compiler."
msgstr ""
"`bundled` 方式在游戏依赖中很常见（SDL、Lua、zstd、mimalloc、PhysX 绑定）：C 源码随 crate 一起发布，用 "
"`cc` 或 `cmake` crate 构建并静态链接，用户只需要一个 C 编译器。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:191
msgid "What this fixes, compared with C++"
msgstr "和 C++ 相比，它解决了什么"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:193
msgid "C++ problem"
msgstr "C++ 的问题"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:193
msgid "What Cargo does"
msgstr "Cargo 的做法"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:195
msgid "Each library has its own build system to integrate"
msgstr "每个库都有自己的构建系统需要集成"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:195
msgid "Every crate has the same `Cargo.toml` and builds the same way"
msgstr "每个 crate 都有同样的 `Cargo.toml`，构建方式完全一样"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:196
msgid ""
"Prebuilt binaries must match compiler, standard library, "
"`_ITERATOR_DEBUG_LEVEL`, runtime and flags"
msgstr "预编译的二进制必须匹配编译器、标准库、`_ITERATOR_DEBUG_LEVEL`、运行时库和编译选项"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:196
msgid "Everything is built from source with your compiler and your profile"
msgstr "一切都用你的编译器和你的 profile 从源代码构建"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:197
msgid "Transitive dependencies are found and built by hand"
msgstr "传递依赖要手动查找和构建"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:197
msgid "The whole graph is resolved and built from one line"
msgstr "一行就能解析并构建整个依赖图"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:198
msgid "Diamond dependencies with conflicting versions break the ODR"
msgstr "版本冲突的菱形依赖会违反 ODR"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:198
msgid ""
"Compatible versions are unified; incompatible ones coexist as distinct types"
msgstr "兼容的版本被统一；不兼容的版本作为不同的类型共存"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:199
msgid "\"Works on my machine\" because a dependency changed"
msgstr "因为某个依赖变了而出现\"在我机器上能跑\""

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:199
msgid "`Cargo.lock` pins every version"
msgstr "`Cargo.lock` 锁定每一个版本"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:200
msgid "Header-only versus compiled libraries"
msgstr "仅头文件的库和需要编译的库"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:200
msgid "No headers; every crate is compiled the same way"
msgstr "没有头文件；每个 crate 都以同样的方式编译"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:201
msgid "Optional parts of a library through CMake options"
msgstr "通过 CMake 选项启用库的可选部分"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:201
msgid "Features, declared in `Cargo.toml` and visible in `cargo tree`"
msgstr "feature，声明在 `Cargo.toml` 里，用 `cargo tree` 可以看到"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:202
msgid "Cross-compiling dependencies"
msgstr "交叉编译依赖"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:202
msgid "`rustup target add` and `cargo build --target`, for pure-Rust crates"
msgstr "对纯 Rust 的 crate，`rustup target add` 加上 `cargo build --target` 即可"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:204
msgid "What it does not fix"
msgstr "它没有解决什么"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:206
msgid ""
"**Native dependencies are still native.** A `-sys` crate needs a C "
"toolchain, and cross-compiling one needs a cross C toolchain. This is the "
"same problem you have in C++, contained in one crate."
msgstr ""
"**原生依赖仍然是原生的。** `-sys` crate 需要 C 工具链，交叉编译它就需要交叉编译的 C 工具链。这和 C++ "
"里的问题一样，只是被限制在一个 crate 里。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:209
msgid ""
"**No binary distribution.** Building from source means the first build of a "
"large graph takes minutes. `cargo check`, incremental builds, sccache and "
"keeping heavy generic code out of low-level crates ([Project "
"organization](../foundations/project-organization.md#compile-times-and-"
"crate-boundaries)) are the mitigations."
msgstr ""
"**没有二进制分发。** 从源代码构建意味着，大型依赖图的第一次构建需要好几分钟。缓解办法有 `cargo "
"check`、增量构建、sccache，以及不要把繁重的泛型代码放在底层 crate 里（[项目组织](../foundations/project-"
"organization.md#编译时间与-crate-边界)）。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:214
msgid ""
"**No stable ABI between Rust crates.** You cannot ship a closed-source Rust "
"library as a `.rlib` for others to link. Closed-source code is shipped as a "
"C ABI library, a binary, or source in a private registry."
msgstr ""
"**Rust crate 之间没有稳定的 ABI。** 你不能把一个闭源的 Rust 库作为 `.rlib` 发给别人链接。闭源代码要以 C ABI "
"库、可执行文件或私有注册中心中的源代码形式发布。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:217
msgid ""
"**Mixing with an existing C++ build.** Cargo does not build your C++ code. "
"In a CMake project, Corrosion lets CMake drive Cargo ([FFI with C and "
"C++](ffi.md#rust-inside-a-cmake-project))."
msgstr ""
"**与现有的 C++ 构建混用。** Cargo 不会构建你的 C++ 代码。在 CMake 项目中，可以用 Corrosion 让 CMake 来驱动"
" Cargo（[与 C 和 C++ 的 FFI](ffi.md#在-cmake-项目中使用-rust)）。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:221
msgid "Can I trust this crate?"
msgstr "这个 crate 可信吗？"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:223
msgid ""
"crates.io does not review code. Anyone can publish anything, and each "
"dependency brings its own dependencies along. This is the same risk as "
"vendoring a library from GitHub in C++, except that it is so easy to add a "
"crate that you can end up with hundreds of them without noticing. Two facts "
"make it more serious than it first looks:"
msgstr ""
"crates.io 不审查代码。任何人都可以发布任何东西，而每个依赖又会带来它自己的依赖。这和在 C++ 里从 GitHub vendor "
"一个库的风险相同，只是添加 crate 太容易了，你可能在不知不觉中就有了几百个依赖。有两个事实让这件事比初看起来更严重："

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:229
msgid ""
"**Building runs code.** A dependency's `build.rs` and its procedural macros "
"run on your machine during `cargo build`, with your user's permissions, the "
"way a CMake script does. Malicious crates have used this to steal "
"credentials from developer machines."
msgstr ""
"**构建会运行代码。** 依赖的 `build.rs` 和过程宏会在 `cargo build` 时以你的用户权限在你的机器上运行，就像 CMake "
"脚本一样。恶意 crate 曾经利用这一点从开发者的机器上窃取凭据。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:233
msgid ""
"**Published source may differ from the repository.** crates.io stores what "
"the owner uploaded. The GitHub link on the crate page is a claim, not a "
"guarantee. A package published from a git checkout includes a "
"`.cargo_vcs_info.json` file with the commit it was built from, which lets "
"you, or a tool, compare the two."
msgstr ""
"**发布的源代码可能和代码仓库不一致。** crates.io 存储的是所有者上传的内容。crate 页面上的 GitHub "
"链接只是一个声明，而不是保证。从 git 工作区发布的包会包含一个 `.cargo_vcs_info.json` "
"文件，记录了构建它的提交，你或工具可以据此比较两者。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:239
msgid "Signals to check before adding a dependency"
msgstr "添加依赖前要检查的信号"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:241
msgid "Question"
msgstr "问题"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:241
msgid "Where to look"
msgstr "去哪里看"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:243
msgid "Is it widely used?"
msgstr "用的人多吗？"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:243
msgid "Recent downloads and the Dependents tab"
msgstr "近期下载量和 Dependents 标签页"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:244
msgid "Is it maintained?"
msgstr "还在维护吗？"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:244
msgid "Date of the last release, open issues and pull requests, a changelog"
msgstr "最近一次发布的日期、未关闭的 issue 和 pull request、changelog"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:245
msgid "Who maintains it?"
msgstr "谁在维护？"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:245
msgid "Owners on the crate page; one maintainer or a team or organization"
msgstr "crate 页面上的所有者；是一个人，还是一个团队或组织"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:246
msgid "How much does it pull in?"
msgstr "它会引入多少东西？"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:246
msgid ""
"`cargo tree -p <crate>` after adding it, or the dependency list on the crate"
" page"
msgstr "添加之后运行 `cargo tree -p <crate>`，或者看 crate 页面上的依赖列表"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:247
msgid "How much `unsafe` does it use?"
msgstr "它用了多少 `unsafe`？"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:247
msgid "Search the source; `cargo geiger` counts it per dependency"
msgstr "搜索源代码；`cargo geiger` 会按依赖统计"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:248
msgid "Does it run code at build time?"
msgstr "它会在构建时运行代码吗？"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:248
msgid "A `build.rs` file, or a dependency on `proc-macro2` and `syn`"
msgstr "有 `build.rs` 文件，或者依赖了 `proc-macro2` 和 `syn`"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:249
msgid "Is the name right?"
msgstr "名字对吗？"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:249
msgid ""
"Typosquats such as `serde-json` for `serde_json` exist. Copy names from the "
"docs"
msgstr "存在仿冒名字的 crate，比如用 `serde-json` 冒充 `serde_json`。从文档里复制名字"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:250
msgid "Is the license compatible?"
msgstr "许可证兼容吗？"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:250
msgid "The `license` field; most crates are `MIT OR Apache-2.0`"
msgstr "看 `license` 字段；大多数 crate 是 `MIT OR Apache-2.0`"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:252
msgid ""
"A crate at version `0.x` is not necessarily immature. Many foundational "
"crates stayed at `0.x` for years. What matters is how it is maintained and "
"who depends on it."
msgstr ""
"版本号是 `0.x` 的 crate 并不一定不成熟。许多基础 crate 在 `0.x` 停留了很多年。重要的是它的维护情况，以及有谁依赖它。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:256
msgid "Tools that check for you"
msgstr "帮你检查的工具"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:261
msgid "# known vulnerabilities, from the RustSec advisory database\n"
msgstr "# 已知漏洞，来自 RustSec 公告数据库\n"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:262
msgid ""
"# vulnerabilities, licenses, banned crates, duplicate versions, sources\n"
msgstr "# 漏洞、许可证、禁用的 crate、重复版本、来源\n"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:263
msgid "# crates that appear in more than one version\n"
msgstr "# 出现了不止一个版本的 crate\n"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:264
msgid "# who depends on `syn`, and why\n"
msgstr "# 谁依赖了 `syn`，以及为什么\n"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:267
msgid ""
"The [RustSec advisory database](https://rustsec.org) records "
"vulnerabilities, unmaintained crates and yanked versions, and `cargo audit` "
"checks your `Cargo.lock` against it. Run it in CI ([Testing "
"chapter](testing-and-tooling.md#a-ci-setup))."
msgstr ""
"[RustSec 公告数据库](https://rustsec.org)记录了漏洞、无人维护的 crate 和被撤回的版本，`cargo audit` "
"会用它检查你的 `Cargo.lock`。在 CI 中运行它（[测试一章](testing-and-tooling.md#一套-ci-配置)）。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:271
msgid ""
"`cargo deny` is driven by a `deny.toml` in your repository. A small one for "
"a game project:"
msgstr "`cargo deny` 由仓库里的 `deny.toml` 驱动。一个游戏项目的简单配置："

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:274
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[licenses]\n"
"allow = [\"MIT\", \"Apache-2.0\", \"BSD-3-Clause\", \"Zlib\", \"Unicode-3.0\"]\n"
"\n"
"[bans]\n"
"multiple-versions = \"warn\"          # duplicate versions cost build time and binary size\n"
"\n"
"[sources]\n"
"unknown-registry = \"deny\"           # only crates.io unless you list others\n"
"unknown-git = \"deny\"                # no surprise git dependencies\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:286
msgid ""
"For a stricter policy, [cargo-vet](https://mozilla.github.io/cargo-vet/) "
"records which crate versions someone on your team (or an organization you "
"trust, such as Mozilla or Google) has actually reviewed, and fails the build"
" when a new, unreviewed version comes in. [diff.rs](https://diff.rs) shows "
"what changed between two published versions of a crate, which is the code "
"you would be trusting when you run `cargo update`."
msgstr ""
"如果需要更严格的策略，[cargo-vet](https://mozilla.github.io/cargo-vet/) 会记录哪些 crate "
"版本已经被你的团队成员（或者你信任的组织，比如 Mozilla 或 "
"Google）真正审查过，并在引入未经审查的新版本时让构建失败。[diff.rs](https://diff.rs) 可以显示一个 crate "
"两个已发布版本之间的变化，也就是你运行 `cargo update` 时将要信任的代码。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:293
msgid "Using crates well"
msgstr "用好 crate"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:295
msgid ""
"**Turn off what you do not use.** Many crates enable optional features by "
"default. Disabling them reduces build time and the amount of code you trust:"
msgstr "**关掉用不到的部分。** 许多 crate 默认启用可选的 feature。关掉它们可以减少构建时间，也减少你需要信任的代码："

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:298
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"image = { version = \"0.25\", default-features = false, features = [\"png\"] }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:303
msgid ""
"**Commit `Cargo.lock` and update on purpose.** The lock file pins every "
"transitive version, so an update is a diff you can review:"
msgstr "**提交 `Cargo.lock`，有意识地更新。** lock 文件锁定了所有传递依赖的版本，所以每次更新都是一个可以审查的 diff："

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:307
msgid "# what would change\n"
msgstr "# 会发生哪些变化\n"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:308
msgid "# update one crate (and what it needs)\n"
msgstr "# 只更新一个 crate（以及它需要的依赖）\n"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:312
msgid ""
"**Declare the oldest compiler you support** with `rust-version` in "
"`Cargo.toml`. Cargo's resolver then prefers dependency versions that still "
"build with that compiler, and anyone with an older toolchain gets a clear "
"error instead of a confusing one."
msgstr ""
"**声明你支持的最低编译器版本**，即 `Cargo.toml` 里的 `rust-version`。这样 Cargo "
"的解析器会优先选择仍能用这个编译器构建的依赖版本，使用更旧工具链的人也会得到清楚的错误信息，而不是令人困惑的错误。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:317
msgid ""
"**Use a fork while waiting for a fix.** When a dependency has a bug, fix it "
"in a fork and point the whole dependency graph at your fork with `[patch]`, "
"even where the crate is a dependency of a dependency:"
msgstr ""
"**等待修复时使用 fork。** 当某个依赖有 bug 时，在 fork 里修好它，再用 `[patch]` 让整个依赖图都指向你的 "
"fork，即使这个 crate 是依赖的依赖："

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:321
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[patch.crates-io]\n"
"winit = { git = \"https://github.com/you/winit\", branch = \"fix-ime-crash\" }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:326
msgid ""
"When the fix is released upstream, delete the patch. This is the clean "
"version of the \"we carry a local patch to third_party/\" workflow in C++ "
"engines."
msgstr "修复在上游发布后，删掉这个 patch。这是 C++ 引擎里\"我们在 third_party/ 里维护一份本地补丁\"这种做法的干净版本。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:329
msgid ""
"**Vendor for offline or audited builds.** `cargo vendor` copies the source "
"of every dependency into a directory and prints the configuration that makes"
" Cargo build from it, with no network. Console and studio build farms often "
"need this."
msgstr ""
"**为离线或经过审计的构建做 vendor。** `cargo vendor` 会把每个依赖的源代码复制到一个目录中，并打印出让 Cargo "
"从这个目录构建、无需联网的配置。主机平台和工作室的构建农场常常需要这样做。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:334
msgid ""
"**Private registries** are supported for code that cannot be public: list "
"them under `[registries]` in `.cargo/config.toml` and add `registry = "
"\"studio\"` to a dependency. Several commercial and self-hosted registry "
"servers exist."
msgstr ""
"不能公开的代码可以使用**私有注册中心**：在 `.cargo/config.toml` 的 `[registries]` 下列出它，然后给依赖加上 "
"`registry = \"studio\"`。有好几种商业的和自托管的注册中心服务器可选。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:339
msgid "Contributing to other people's crates"
msgstr "为别人的 crate 做贡献"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:341
msgid ""
"Most crates live on GitHub, and the workflow is the usual open-source one:"
msgstr "大多数 crate 托管在 GitHub 上，流程就是常见的开源流程："

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:343
msgid ""
"Read `CONTRIBUTING.md` if it exists, and look for an existing issue. For "
"anything larger than a small fix, open an issue first and agree on the "
"approach."
msgstr ""
"如果有 `CONTRIBUTING.md`，先读一读，并查找是否已有相关 issue。对于比小修复更大的改动，先开一个 issue，就做法达成一致。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:346
msgid ""
"Fork and clone the repository, and check that the tests pass before you "
"change anything: `cargo test`, often `cargo test --all-features` too."
msgstr ""
"fork 并克隆仓库，在修改任何东西之前先确认测试能通过：`cargo test`，通常还有 `cargo test --all-features`。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:348
msgid ""
"Test your change in your own project with `[patch.crates-io]` pointing at "
"your local clone (`path = \"../winit\"`). This is the quickest way to prove "
"that the fix works."
msgstr ""
"在你自己的项目里用 `[patch.crates-io]` 指向本地克隆（`path = "
"\"../winit\"`）来测试你的改动。这是证明修复有效的最快方式。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:351
msgid ""
"Before opening the pull request, run `cargo fmt` and `cargo clippy`. Most "
"projects check both in CI, and Rust reviewers expect formatted code."
msgstr ""
"提交 pull request 之前，运行 `cargo fmt` 和 `cargo clippy`。大多数项目在 CI 中检查这两项，Rust "
"的代码审查者也默认代码是格式化过的。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:353
msgid ""
"Add a test that fails without your fix, and an entry in `CHANGELOG.md` if "
"the project keeps one."
msgstr "添加一个没有你的修复就会失败的测试；如果项目维护 `CHANGELOG.md`，也加上一条记录。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:356
msgid ""
"Contributions that are always welcome and often easier than code: a minimal "
"reproduction for an open bug, a documentation fix, an example, or "
"confirmation that a fix works on your platform. Console and XR platforms in "
"particular are rarely tested by maintainers."
msgstr ""
"有些贡献总是受欢迎，而且往往比写代码更容易：为一个未解决的 bug 提供最小复现、修正文档、添加示例，或者确认某个修复在你的平台上有效。尤其是主机和 "
"XR 平台，维护者很少能测试到。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:361
msgid ""
"crates.io itself is open source too, at [rust-"
"lang/crates.io](https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io). Its issue tracker "
"is the place to report a problem with the registry, and malware or abuse "
"should go to the security contact on the [crates.io policies "
"page](https://crates.io/policies) rather than to a public issue."
msgstr ""
"crates.io 本身也是开源的，地址是 [rust-lang/crates.io](https://github.com/rust-"
"lang/crates.io)。注册中心的问题可以在它的 issue tracker 上报告；恶意软件或滥用行为则应该发给 [crates.io "
"政策页面](https://crates.io/policies)上的安全联系人，而不是公开提 issue。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:367
msgid "Publishing your own crate"
msgstr "发布自己的 crate"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:369
msgid "Prepare the package"
msgstr "准备包"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:371
msgid ""
"crates.io requires a license and a description. Add the rest so people can "
"find the crate and trust it:"
msgstr "crates.io 要求提供许可证和描述。把其余字段也填上，方便别人找到并信任这个 crate："

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:374
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[package]\n"
"name = \"frame-pacer\"\n"
"version = \"0.1.0\"\n"
"edition = \"2024\"\n"
"rust-version = \"1.85\"\n"
"description = \"Frame pacing and fixed-timestep helpers for game loops\"\n"
"license = \"MIT OR Apache-2.0\"\n"
"repository = \"https://github.com/you/frame-pacer\"\n"
"readme = \"README.md\"\n"
"keywords = [\"gamedev\", \"game-loop\", \"timestep\"]   # up to five\n"
"categories = [\"game-development\"]                  # from crates.io's fixed list\n"
"exclude = [\"assets/\", \".github/\"]                  # keep the package small\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:389
msgid ""
"`MIT OR Apache-2.0` is the Rust convention: users may pick either license, "
"and the combination is compatible with almost every project. Add both "
"license files to the repository."
msgstr ""
"`MIT OR Apache-2.0` 是 Rust 的惯例：用户可以任选一种许可证，这个组合几乎与所有项目兼容。把两个许可证文件都放进仓库。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:393
msgid ""
"Document the public API with `///` comments, because docs.rs will publish "
"them the moment the crate is released, and doc examples run as tests "
"([Testing chapter](testing-and-tooling.md#documentation-tests)). Two crate "
"attributes are a good default for a library:"
msgstr ""
"用 `///` 注释为公开 API 写文档，因为 crate 一发布，docs.rs "
"就会公开这些文档，而文档中的示例也会作为测试运行（[测试一章](testing-and-tooling.md#文档测试)）。对一个库来说，下面两个 "
"crate 属性是不错的默认设置："

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:399
msgid "// src/lib.rs\n"
msgstr "// src/lib.rs\n"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:400
msgid "// a promise users can check; drop it if you need unsafe\n"
msgstr "// 一个用户可以验证的承诺；如果需要 unsafe 就去掉它\n"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:401
msgid "// every public item gets documentation\n"
msgstr "// 每个公开条目都要有文档\n"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:404
msgid "Publish"
msgstr "发布"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:407
msgid "# exactly which files will be uploaded\n"
msgstr "# 确切会上传哪些文件\n"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:408
msgid "# builds the package as a user would, without uploading\n"
msgstr "# 像用户那样构建这个包，但不上传\n"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:409
msgid "# once: paste an API token from crates.io settings\n"
msgstr "# 只需一次：粘贴从 crates.io 设置中获得的 API token\n"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:413
msgid ""
"`cargo publish` builds the packaged tarball in isolation, so a file that is "
"missing from the package or a dependency given only by `path` fails here "
"rather than for your users. Path and git dependencies must also have a "
"`version` to be published; crates.io never depends on code outside the "
"registry. In a workspace, `cargo publish --workspace` publishes every member"
" in dependency order."
msgstr ""
"`cargo publish` 会单独构建打包好的压缩包，所以包里缺了文件，或者某个依赖只给了 "
"`path`，都会在这一步失败，而不是在用户那里失败。path 依赖和 git 依赖要能发布，还必须写上 `version`：crates.io 上的 "
"crate 从不依赖注册中心之外的代码。在工作区中，`cargo publish --workspace` 会按依赖顺序发布所有成员。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:420
msgid "Versioning"
msgstr "版本管理"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:422
msgid ""
"Your version number is a promise ([semver](https://semver.org)). Before 1.0,"
" Cargo treats the first non-zero component as the major version, so `0.3.x` "
"to `0.4.0` is a breaking change and `0.3.1` to `0.3.2` is not. Breaking "
"changes in Rust include more than in C++: making a public field private, "
"adding a variant to a public enum (unless it is `#[non_exhaustive]`), adding"
" a required method to a public trait, or removing a trait implementation. "
"[cargo-semver-checks](https://github.com/obi1kenobi/cargo-semver-checks) "
"compares your API with the last published version and reports changes that "
"need a major bump. Run it before each release."
msgstr ""
"版本号是一个承诺（[semver](https://semver.org)）。1.0 之前，Cargo 把第一个非零的部分当作主版本号，所以从 "
"`0.3.x` 到 `0.4.0` 是破坏性变更，从 `0.3.1` 到 `0.3.2` 则不是。Rust 中的破坏性变更比 C++ "
"里更多：把公开字段改为私有、给公开枚举增加变体（除非它标记了 `#[non_exhaustive]`）、给公开 trait "
"增加必须实现的方法，或者移除某个 trait 实现。[cargo-semver-"
"checks](https://github.com/obi1kenobi/cargo-semver-checks) 会把你的 API "
"和上一个已发布的版本进行比较，报告需要升级主版本号的改动。每次发布前运行一下。"

#: src/systems/crates-io.md:432
msgid ""
"If you publish a broken version, publish a fixed one and yank the broken one"
" with `cargo yank --version 0.1.1`."
msgstr "如果发布了一个有问题的版本，就发布一个修复后的版本，再用 `cargo yank --version 0.1.1` 撤回有问题的那个。"

