"Every call returns `io::Result`, so a failed `connect` or a reset connection"
" is a value you handle with `?`, not an `errno` you forget to check. The "
"socket closes when the last handle to it is dropped (`try_clone` is `dup`), "
"and `TcpStream` implements the same `Read` and `Write` traits as files, so "
"`BufReader` and every other I/O adapter work on it."
msgstr ""
"每个调用都返回 `io::Result`，所以 `connect` 失败或连接被重置都是一个用 `?` 处理的值，而不是一个容易忘记检查的 "
"`errno`。最后一个句柄被丢弃时 socket 就会关闭（`try_clone` 相当于 `dup`）。`TcpStream` 实现了和文件相同的 "
"`Read` 和 `Write` trait，所以 `BufReader` 以及其他所有 I/O 适配器都能直接用在它上面。"

