#: src/systems/networking.md:196
msgid ""
"`auto* p = reinterpret_cast<const MovePacket*>(buf);` is fast and common in "
"C++ netcode, and it is undefined behavior if the buffer is misaligned or too"
" short, it depends on the compiler's padding and the machine's byte order, "
"and it trusts every field the sender wrote. In Rust, slicing is bounds-"
"checked and `from_le_bytes` fixes the byte order. If you do want a zero-copy"
" view of a `#[repr(C)]` struct, `bytemuck::try_from_bytes` checks the size "
"and alignment first ([Values, types and layout](../foundations/values-and-"
"types.md)). Either way, validate the values, not just the size: an entity id"
" from the network can still be out of range."
msgstr ""
"`auto* p = reinterpret_cast<const MovePacket*>(buf);` 在 C++ "
"网络代码里又快又常见，但如果缓冲区没有对齐或长度不够，它就是未定义行为；它还依赖编译器的填充方式和机器的字节序，并且完全信任发送方写入的每个字段。在 "
"Rust 里，切片有边界检查，`from_le_bytes` 明确了字节序。如果确实需要零拷贝地查看一个 `#[repr(C)]` "
"结构体，`bytemuck::try_from_bytes` 会先检查大小和对齐（[值、类型与内存布局](../foundations/values-"
"and-types.md)）。无论哪种方式，都要验证值本身，而不只是大小：来自网络的实体 id 仍然可能越界。"

#: src/systems/networking.md:208
