"`write!`（来自 `std::fmt::Write`）来消除这些分配。"

#: src/systems/memory-and-performance.md:269
msgid ""
"Write a loop that sums `data[idx[i]]` for an index array. Look for the "
"bounds check in the assembly. Can you remove it safely?"
msgstr "写一个循环，对索引数组求和 `data[idx[i]]`。在汇编中找到边界检查。你能安全地去掉它吗？"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:3
msgid ""
"Everything so far has been **safe Rust**: code in which the compiler "
"guarantees no undefined behavior. Some code cannot be checked by the "
"compiler: calling C functions, talking to hardware, implementing a new "
"collection on raw memory, using SIMD intrinsics. For those, Rust has the "
"`unsafe` keyword. As a C++ programmer you will find `unsafe` Rust familiar, "
"since it is roughly what you write every day, but the rules are stricter "
"than you might expect, and the way it is used is very different."
msgstr ""
"到目前为止的一切都是**安全的 Rust**（safe Rust）：编译器保证这些代码中没有未定义行为。有些代码是编译器无法检查的：调用 C "
"函数、与硬件交互、在裸内存上实现新的集合、使用 SIMD 内建函数。为此 Rust 提供了 `unsafe` 关键字。作为 C++ 程序员，你会觉得 "
"`unsafe` Rust 很熟悉，因为它大致就是你每天在写的东西，但它的规则比你预想的更严格，使用方式也大不相同。"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:13
msgid "what `unsafe` allows, and what it does not switch off,"
msgstr "`unsafe` 允许做什么，以及它不会关闭什么；"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:14
msgid "raw pointers,"
msgstr "裸指针；"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:15
msgid "what counts as undefined behavior in Rust, especially aliasing,"
msgstr "在 Rust 中什么算未定义行为，尤其是别名规则；"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:16
msgid "building safe abstractions on top of unsafe code,"
msgstr "在 unsafe 代码之上构建安全的抽象；"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:17
msgid "Miri, an interpreter that finds undefined behavior in tests."
msgstr "Miri：一个能在测试中找出未定义行为的解释器。"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:19
msgid "What `unsafe` unlocks"
msgstr "`unsafe` 解锁了什么"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:21
msgid "An `unsafe` block or function lets you do five extra things:"
msgstr "`unsafe` 块或函数允许你额外做五件事："

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:23
msgid "Dereference a raw pointer (`*const T`, `*mut T`)."
msgstr "解引用裸指针（`*const T`、`*mut T`）。"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:24
msgid "Call an `unsafe` function, including all foreign (C) functions."
msgstr "调用 `unsafe` 函数，包括所有外部（C）函数。"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:25
msgid "Access or modify a mutable `static`."
msgstr "访问或修改可变的 `static`。"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:26
msgid "Implement an `unsafe` trait (such as `Send`, `Sync`, `GlobalAlloc`)."
msgstr "实现 `unsafe` trait（例如 `Send`、`Sync`、`GlobalAlloc`）。"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:27
msgid "Access the fields of a `union`."
msgstr "访问 `union` 的字段。"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:29
msgid ""
"That is the whole list. Inside `unsafe`, the borrow checker, type checker "
"and bounds checks still run as usual. `unsafe` does not mean \"turn off the "
"checks\"; it means \"I am doing one of these five things, and **I** promise "
"the invariants the compiler cannot verify\"."
msgstr ""
"完整的清单就是这些。在 `unsafe` 内部，借用检查器、类型检查器和边界检查照常运行。`unsafe` "
"的意思不是“关闭检查”，而是“我正在做这五件事之一，并且由**我**来保证编译器无法验证的那些不变量”。"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:37
msgid "// creating a raw pointer is safe\n"
msgstr "// 创建裸指针是安全的\n"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:40
msgid "// Dereferencing it is not: we promise p+2 is in bounds and valid.\n"
msgstr "// 解引用它则不是：我们保证 p+2 在范围内且有效。\n"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:43
msgid "\"{second}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:45
msgid "\"{values:?}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:49
msgid "Raw pointers"
msgstr "裸指针"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:51
msgid ""
"`*const T` and `*mut T` are C pointers: they can be null, dangling, "
"unaligned, and they alias freely. Creating, copying and comparing them is "
"safe; only reading or writing through them requires `unsafe`. Convert "
"between references and raw pointers explicitly:"
msgstr ""
"`*const T` 和 `*mut T` 就是 C "
"指针：它们可以为空、悬垂、未对齐，并且可以随意重叠。创建、复制和比较它们是安全的；只有通过它们读写才需要 "
"`unsafe`。在引用和裸指针之间要显式转换："

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:60
msgid "// reference -> pointer: safe, implicit coercion\n"
msgstr "// 引用 -> 指针：安全，隐式转换\n"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:61
msgid "// or take the address directly\n"
msgstr "// 或者直接取地址\n"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:62
msgid "// pointer -> reference: unsafe\n"
msgstr "// 指针 -> 引用：unsafe\n"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:65
msgid "// Pointer arithmetic is in elements, like C:\n"
msgstr "// 指针运算以元素为单位，和 C 一样：\n"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:70
msgid "\"{third} {byte_offset}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:74
msgid "Undefined behavior in Rust"
msgstr "Rust 中的未定义行为"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:76
msgid ""
"Rust's list of undefined behavior overlaps with C++'s, with some notable "
"differences. The ones that matter most:"
msgstr "Rust 的未定义行为清单与 C++ 的有重叠，但也有一些明显的区别。最重要的几条："

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:79
msgid "Dereferencing a dangling, null or misaligned pointer."
msgstr "解引用悬垂的、空的或未对齐的指针。"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:80
msgid ""
"Reading uninitialized memory (use `MaybeUninit<T>` for memory that starts "
"uninitialized)."
msgstr "读取未初始化的内存（对一开始未初始化的内存使用 `MaybeUninit<T>`）。"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:82
msgid ""
"Producing an invalid value: a `bool` that is not 0 or 1, an enum with an "
"invalid discriminant, a null reference, a `char` that is not a Unicode "
"scalar value, a `&str` that is not UTF-8. In C++ the bad `bool` is UB only "
"when used; in Rust **creating** it is already UB."
msgstr ""
"产生无效的值：不是 0 或 1 的 `bool`、判别值无效的枚举、空引用、不是 Unicode 标量值的 `char`、不是 UTF-8 的 "
"`&str`。在 C++ 中，坏的 `bool` 只有在使用时才是 UB；在 Rust 中，**创建**它就已经是 UB 了。"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:86
msgid "Data races."
msgstr "数据竞争。"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:87
msgid "**Breaking the aliasing rules of references.**"
msgstr "**违反引用的别名规则。**"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:89
msgid ""
"The last one is the big difference. In C++, the main aliasing rule is "
"_strict aliasing_: pointers to different types are assumed not to alias. "
"Rust has no type-based aliasing rule at all (you may freely cast a `*mut "
"f32` to `*mut u32`), but it has a much stronger rule about references:"
msgstr ""
"最后一条是最大的区别。在 C++ 中，主要的别名规则是<em>严格别名</em>（strict "
"aliasing）：指向不同类型的指针被假定不会重叠。Rust 完全没有基于类型的别名规则（你可以随意把 `*mut f32` 转换成 `*mut "
"u32`），但它对引用有一条强得多的规则："

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:94
msgid ""
"While a `&mut T` is live, no other pointer or reference may access that "
"memory."
msgstr "当一个 `&mut T` 存活时，任何其他指针或引用都不得访问那块内存。"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:96
msgid ""
"While a `&T` is live, the memory must not be written (except inside an "
"`UnsafeCell`, which is what `Cell`, `RefCell` and `Mutex` are built on)."
msgstr ""
"当一个 `&T` 存活时，那块内存不得被写入（`UnsafeCell` 内部除外，`Cell`、`RefCell` 和 `Mutex` "
"都建立在它之上）。"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:99
msgid ""
"These are the same guarantees the borrow checker enforces in safe code, and "
"the optimizer relies on them (it is how `&mut` becomes `noalias`). In unsafe"
" code you can create two `&mut` to the same memory from raw pointers, and if"
" you do, the program is undefined even if it seems to work:"
msgstr ""
"这些正是借用检查器在安全代码中强制执行的保证，优化器也依赖它们（`&mut` 正是因此成为 `noalias`）。在 unsafe "
"代码中，你可以从裸指针创建两个指向同一块内存的 `&mut`；如果你这样做了，即使程序看起来能工作，它的行为也是未定义的："

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:110
msgid "// UB: two live &mut to the same i32\n"
msgstr "// UB：两个指向同一个 i32 的存活的 &mut\n"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:117
msgid ""
"The rule of thumb: **in unsafe code, work with raw pointers, and only create"
" references when you can guarantee the borrow rules for their whole "
"lifetime.**"
msgstr "经验法则：**在 unsafe 代码中使用裸指针，只有当你能在引用的整个生命期内保证借用规则时，才创建引用。**"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:120
msgid "Safe abstractions over unsafe code"
msgstr "在 unsafe 代码之上构建安全抽象"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:122
msgid ""
"The point of `unsafe` in Rust is not to write unsafe programs. It is to "
"write a small, carefully reviewed unsafe core and wrap it in a safe API, so "
"that no caller, however wrong, can cause undefined behavior. The standard "
"library is built this way: `Vec`, `HashMap`, `Rc` and `Mutex` all contain "
"unsafe code, and none of their public safe methods can be misused into UB."
msgstr ""
"Rust 中 `unsafe` 的意义不在于编写不安全的程序，而在于编写一个小的、经过仔细审查的 unsafe 核心，再用安全的 API "
"把它包起来，让任何调用者无论怎么出错都无法造成未定义行为。标准库就是这样构建的：`Vec`、`HashMap`、`Rc` 和 `Mutex` 都包含 "
"unsafe 代码，而它们的公开安全方法都不可能被误用成 UB。"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:128
msgid ""
"Here is a small example: a fixed-capacity, stack-allocated vector (like "
"`boost::static_vector`), built on uninitialized memory."
msgstr "下面是一个小例子：一个建立在未初始化内存之上、容量固定、在栈上分配的 vector（类似 `boost::static_vector`）。"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:136
msgid "// invariant: items[..len] are initialized\n"
msgstr "// 不变量：items[..len] 已初始化\n"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:146
msgid "// full: give the value back\n"
msgstr "// 已满：把值还回去\n"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:158
msgid ""
"// SAFETY: items[len] was initialized (it was below the old len),\n"
"        // and decrementing len first means we never read it again.\n"
msgstr ""
"// SAFETY: items[len] 已初始化（它在旧的 len 之下），\n"
"        // 并且先递减 len 意味着我们再也不会读取它。\n"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:164
msgid ""
"// SAFETY: items[..len] are initialized, and MaybeUninit<T> has the same "
"layout as T.\n"
msgstr "// SAFETY: items[..len] 已初始化，且 MaybeUninit<T> 与 T 的布局相同。\n"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:171
msgid "// drop the initialized elements\n"
msgstr "// 丢弃已初始化的元素\n"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:177
msgid "\"d\""
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:177
msgid "\"e\""
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:179
msgid "\"full, rejected {rejected}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:187
msgid "Notice the pattern:"
msgstr "注意其中的模式："

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:189
msgid ""
"The **invariant** (`items[..len]` are initialized) is written down and "
"maintained by every method."
msgstr "**不变量**（`items[..len]` 已初始化）被明确写了下来，并由每个方法维护。"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:191
msgid ""
"Each `unsafe` block has a `// SAFETY:` comment saying why the invariant "
"makes it sound. This is a strong convention in Rust code reviews, and Clippy"
" can require it (`clippy::undocumented_unsafe_blocks`)."
msgstr ""
"每个 `unsafe` 块都有一条 `// SAFETY:` 注释，说明为什么这个不变量使它是可靠的。这是 Rust 代码审查中很强的惯例，Clippy"
" 也可以强制要求它（`clippy::undocumented_unsafe_blocks`）。"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:194
msgid ""
"The fields are private, so code outside the module cannot break the "
"invariant. Privacy is what makes the abstraction safe."
msgstr "字段是私有的，所以模块之外的代码无法破坏不变量。正是私有性让这个抽象变得安全。"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:196
msgid "The public API is entirely safe. Callers cannot misuse it into UB."
msgstr "公开 API 完全是安全的。调用者无法把它误用成 UB。"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:198
msgid ""
"When reviewing Rust code, you audit the `unsafe` blocks and the module that "
"contains them. Everything else is checked by the compiler. In a C++ code "
"review, every line is potentially unsafe."
msgstr ""
"审查 Rust 代码时，你只需审计 `unsafe` 块以及包含它们的模块。其他一切都由编译器检查。而在 C++ 代码审查中，每一行都可能不安全。"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:202
msgid "Miri: finding UB in tests"
msgstr "Miri：在测试中发现 UB"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:204
msgid ""
"[Miri](https://github.com/rust-lang/miri) is an interpreter for Rust's mid-"
"level IR that checks every memory access against the rules above: use after "
"free, out-of-bounds, uninitialized reads, invalid values, and aliasing "
"violations. It is like running AddressSanitizer, MemorySanitizer and UBSan "
"together, with an aliasing checker none of them have:"
msgstr ""
"[Miri](https://github.com/rust-lang/miri) 是一个 Rust "
"中层中间表示（MIR）的解释器，它会按照上面的规则检查每一次内存访问：释放后使用、越界、读取未初始化内存、无效的值，以及违反别名规则。它就像同时运行 "
"AddressSanitizer、MemorySanitizer 和 UBSan，外加一个它们都没有的别名检查器："

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:215
msgid ""
"Run your test suite under Miri for any crate that contains `unsafe` code. It"
" is slow (100 times or more), so run it on unit tests, not your game. On the"
" Playground, **Tools → Miri** runs it on the current example; try it on the "
"\"two `&mut`\" program above."
msgstr ""
"任何包含 `unsafe` 代码的 crate，都应在 Miri 下运行测试套件。它很慢（慢 100 "
"倍甚至更多），所以在单元测试上运行它，而不是在你的游戏上。在 Playground 中，**Tools → Miri** "
"会对当前示例运行它；试试上面那个“两个 `&mut`”的程序。"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:223
msgid ""
"Real engines written in Rust contain unsafe code in a few well-defined "
"places: FFI to graphics APIs, SIMD intrinsics, custom allocators, lock-free "
"queues, and ECS storage. The rest, usually more than 95% of the code, is "
"safe. Aim for the same: concentrate `unsafe` into small modules with clear "
"invariants and safe interfaces, and keep game code free of it."
msgstr ""
"用 Rust 编写的真实引擎只在少数几个明确的地方包含 unsafe 代码：图形 API 的 FFI、SIMD 内建函数、自定义分配器、无锁队列，以及 "
"ECS 存储。其余部分，通常超过 95% 的代码，都是安全的。你也应以此为目标：把 `unsafe` "
"集中到具有清晰不变量和安全接口的小模块中，让游戏代码完全不含它。"

