#: src/systems/unsafe.md:248
msgid ""
"Add an `fn as_mut_slice(&mut self) -> &mut [T]` and an `fn clear(&mut self)`"
" to `StackVec`, with `SAFETY` comments."
msgstr ""
"给 `StackVec` 添加 `fn as_mut_slice(&mut self) -> &mut [T]` 和 `fn clear(&mut "
"self)`，并附上 `SAFETY` 注释。"

#: src/systems/unsafe.md:250
msgid ""
"`StackVec::pop` decrements `len` _before_ reading. What could go wrong if it"
" read first and the element's `Drop` panicked later? (Hint: think about what"
" `Drop for StackVec` would then do.)"
msgstr ""
"`StackVec::pop` 在读取<em>之前</em>递减 `len`。如果它先读取，而元素的 `Drop` 之后发生了 "
"panic，会出什么问题？（提示：想想 `Drop for StackVec` 那时会做什么。）"

#: src/systems/ffi.md:3
msgid ""
"Your engine already has millions of lines of C and C++, and every graphics "
"API, platform layer and middleware library speaks C. Rust talks to C "
"directly, with no wrapper layer and no overhead: a call from Rust to a C "
"function is the same machine-level call a C program would make. This chapter"
" covers both directions, the tools that generate bindings, and how to bring "
"Rust into an existing CMake project."
msgstr ""
"你的引擎里已经有数百万行 C 和 C++ 代码，而每个图形 API、平台层和中间件库说的都是 C。Rust 可以直接与 C "
"对话，没有包装层，也没有开销：从 Rust 调用 C 函数，与 C 程序发出的调用在机器层面完全相同。本章涵盖两个方向的调用、生成绑定的工具，以及如何把"
" Rust 引入现有的 CMake 项目。"

