#: src/systems/ffi.md:92
msgid ""
"A Rust `enum` must only ever hold one of its declared values; anything else "
"is undefined behavior. C APIs regularly return values that were not in the "
"header you compiled against (a newer driver adds a `VkResult`). So do not "
"declare C enums as Rust enums in FFI signatures. Bindgen's default is to "
"emit them as integer constants for exactly this reason."
msgstr ""
"Rust `enum` 只能持有它声明过的值之一；其他任何值都是未定义行为。而 C API 经常返回你编译时所用头文件中没有的值（新版驱动增加了一个 "
"`VkResult`）。所以不要在 FFI 签名中把 C 枚举声明为 Rust 枚举。bindgen 默认把它们生成为整数常量，正是出于这个原因。"

