#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:3
msgid ""
"Game objects point at each other. A missile tracks its target, a light "
"belongs to a room, a UI widget knows its parent, an animation references a "
"skeleton. In C++ these links are usually raw pointers or "
"`shared_ptr`/`weak_ptr`, and the classic bug is a pointer that outlives its "
"object: the enemy dies, its memory is reused for a bullet, and the missile "
"now steers toward the bullet."
msgstr ""
"游戏对象之间互相指向。导弹追踪目标，灯光属于某个房间，UI 控件知道自己的父控件，动画引用骨骼。在 C++ 中，这些联系通常是裸指针或 "
"`shared_ptr`/`weak_ptr`，而经典的 bug "
"是指针比它指向的对象活得更久：敌人死了，它的内存被一颗子弹重用，于是导弹转而朝那颗子弹飞去。"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:9
msgid ""
"The [borrowing chapter](../foundations/borrowing.md) showed that Rust "
"references are for short-lived access. A `&Enemy` stored inside a `Missile` "
"would freeze the whole enemy list for as long as the missile exists. This "
"chapter introduces the pattern most Rust engines use instead, which many C++"
" engines also use for the same reasons: **objects live in an arena, and "
"other objects refer to them by handle.**"
msgstr ""
"[借用一章](../foundations/borrowing.md)说明了 Rust 的引用是用于短期访问的。存放在 `Missile` 里的 "
"`&Enemy` 会在导弹存在的整个期间冻结整个敌人列表。本章介绍大多数 Rust 引擎采用的替代模式，许多 C++ "
"引擎出于同样的原因也采用了它：**对象存放在 arena 中，其他对象通过句柄引用它们。**"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:16
msgid "You will:"
msgstr "你将会："

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:18
msgid ""
"see why indices alone are not enough, and how a generation counter fixes "
"them,"
msgstr "了解为什么只用索引是不够的，以及分代计数器如何解决这个问题；"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:19
msgid "build a small, typed generational arena (about 80 lines),"
msgstr "构建一个小型的、带类型的分代 arena（大约 80 行）；"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:20
msgid "compare it with `Rc`/`Weak` and with what C++ engines do,"
msgstr "把它与 `Rc`/`Weak` 以及 C++ 引擎的做法进行比较；"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:21
msgid "learn which crates to use in real projects."
msgstr "了解在真实项目中应该使用哪些 crate。"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:23
msgid "Handles in one picture"
msgstr "一张图看懂句柄"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:25
msgid ""
"An **arena** is a `Vec` of slots that owns every object of one type. A "
"**handle** is a small `Copy` value (a slot index plus a generation number) "
"that identifies one object. Every time a slot is freed, its generation goes "
"up, so any handle created before that no longer matches."
msgstr ""
"**arena** 是一个由槽位组成的 `Vec`，它拥有某一种类型的所有对象。**句柄**是一个小小的 `Copy` "
"值（槽位索引加一个代数），用于标识一个对象。每当一个槽位被释放，它的代数就会加一，于是在那之前创建的任何句柄都不再匹配。"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:30
msgid ""
"Play with it. Start in C++ style, spawn two entities, despawn the first, "
"spawn another (it reuses the free slot), then read through the old pointer. "
"Then switch to handles and do the same."
msgstr ""
"动手试试。先用 C++ 风格：生成两个实体，销毁第一个，再生成一个（它会重用空出来的槽位），然后通过旧指针读取。接着切换到句柄，做同样的操作。"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:36
msgid ""
"With plain pointers or indices, reading through a stale reference gives you "
"_a_ valid-looking object, just the wrong one. No sanitizer catches it, "
"because the memory is not freed: it was reused, legitimately. A generation "
"check turns that into an `Option` you are forced to handle."
msgstr ""
"用普通指针或索引时，通过过期引用读取会得到<em>一个</em>看起来有效的对象，只不过是错的那个。没有任何 sanitizer "
"能发现它，因为这块内存并没有被释放：它被合法地重用了。分代检查则把它变成了一个你必须处理的 `Option`。"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:44
msgid ""
"This is the same design as handles in many C++ engines and libraries: Andre "
"Weissflog's \"Handles are the better pointers\" (the Sokol libraries), "
"versioned entity IDs in EnTT, and `VkBuffer` itself, which is a handle and "
"not a pointer. Rust did not invent it. What Rust adds is that the "
"alternative, long-lived raw pointers, simply does not compile, so the whole "
"codebase converges on handles."
msgstr ""
"这与许多 C++ 引擎和库中的句柄设计相同：Andre Weissflog 的“Handles are the better "
"pointers”（Sokol 系列库）、EnTT 中带版本号的实体 ID，以及 `VkBuffer` 本身，它是一个句柄而不是指针。这不是 Rust "
"发明的。Rust 补充的是：另一种做法，也就是长期持有的裸指针，根本无法编译，所以整个代码库自然会收敛到句柄上。"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:53
msgid "Building a generational arena"
msgstr "构建一个分代 arena"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:55
msgid ""
"A handle should be typed, so a `Handle<Texture>` cannot be passed where a "
"`Handle<Mesh>` is expected, even though both are just two integers. "
"`PhantomData` adds the type parameter without storing anything:"
msgstr ""
"句柄应该带有类型，这样 `Handle<Texture>` 就不能传到需要 `Handle<Mesh>` "
"的地方，尽管两者都只是两个整数。`PhantomData` 可以添加类型参数而不存储任何东西："

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:62
msgid "/// A copyable reference to a `T` stored in an `Arena<T>`. 8 bytes.\n"
msgstr "/// 指向存放在 `Arena<T>` 中的某个 `T` 的可复制引用。8 字节。\n"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:67
msgid ""
"// `fn() -> T` instead of `T`: the handle does not own a T, so it stays\n"
"    // Copy, Send and Sync whatever T is.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 用 `fn() -> T` 而不是 `T`：句柄并不拥有 T，所以无论 T 是什么，\n"
"    // 它都保持 Copy、Send 和 Sync。\n"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:71
msgid ""
"// `#[derive(Clone, Copy)]` would require `T: Copy`, so implement them by "
"hand.\n"
msgstr "// `#[derive(Clone, Copy)]` 会要求 `T: Copy`，所以手动实现它们。\n"

