#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:202
msgid ""
"Run it. The missile aimed at the orc reports a lost target instead of "
"hitting the goblin that took the orc's memory."
msgstr "运行它。瞄准兽人的导弹会报告丢失目标，而不是击中占用了兽人内存的哥布林。"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:205
msgid ""
"Notice what the borrow checker is doing here, and what it is not doing:"
msgstr "注意借用检查器在这里做了什么，以及没有做什么："

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:207
msgid ""
"`missiles` holds handles, not references, so `enemies` is never frozen. You "
"can insert and remove enemies while missiles exist."
msgstr "`missiles` 持有的是句柄而不是引用，所以 `enemies` 永远不会被冻结。在导弹存在期间，你可以插入和移除敌人。"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:209
msgid ""
"`get_mut` returns a short-lived `&mut Enemy`. _That_ reference is checked as"
" usual: you cannot keep it across a call to `enemies.insert`, which might "
"reallocate the `Vec`. The borrow checker still protects you from the C++ "
"invalidation bug, at the moment of access."
msgstr ""
"`get_mut` 返回一个短期的 `&mut Enemy`。<em>这个</em>引用照常受到检查：你不能在调用 `enemies.insert` "
"期间一直持有它，因为那可能会重新分配 `Vec`。在访问的那一刻，借用检查器依然保护你免受 C++ 失效 bug 的困扰。"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:213
msgid ""
"The arena is the single owner of every enemy. Dropping the arena drops them "
"all, in one place."
msgstr "arena 是每个敌人唯一的所有者。丢弃 arena 就会在同一个地方丢弃所有敌人。"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:219
msgid ""
"A `Handle<T>` is 8 bytes and `Copy`. Compared with a 64-bit pointer it is "
"the same size, survives reallocation, and can be serialized, saved to disk, "
"or sent over the network, because it contains no address."
msgstr ""
"`Handle<T>` 有 8 字节，并且是 `Copy` 的。与 64 "
"位指针相比，它大小相同，能在重新分配后继续有效，还可以被序列化、保存到磁盘或通过网络发送，因为它不包含地址。"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:222
msgid ""
"Access costs one bounds check, one compare, and one load, all on the same "
"cache line as the value. `Rc<RefCell<T>>` costs a separate heap allocation "
"per object plus a runtime borrow flag."
msgstr ""
"一次访问的开销是一次边界检查、一次比较和一次加载，都与值位于同一条缓存行上。而 `Rc<RefCell<T>>` "
"的开销是每个对象一次单独的堆分配，外加一个运行时借用标志。"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:225
msgid ""
"All enemies sit in one contiguous `Vec`, which is what you want for "
"iteration in a system update."
msgstr "所有敌人都位于一个连续的 `Vec` 中，这正是系统更新时进行迭代所需要的。"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:227
msgid ""
"`Option<Handle<T>>` is 12 bytes here. If the generation starts at 1 and is "
"stored as `NonZeroU32`, the compiler uses 0 as the `None` niche and "
"`Option<Handle<T>>` becomes 8 bytes too. (That is exercise 2.)"
msgstr ""
"这里 `Option<Handle<T>>` 是 12 字节。如果代数从 1 开始并存储为 `NonZeroU32`，编译器就会把 0 用作 "
"`None` 的 niche，`Option<Handle<T>>` 也会变成 8 字节。（这是练习 2。）"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:233
msgid "Comparing the options"
msgstr "各种方案的比较"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:237
msgid "Temporary access during a call"
msgstr "在一次调用期间临时访问"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:237
msgid "`T&`, `T*`"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:238
msgid "Single owner, heap allocated"
msgstr "单一所有者，在堆上分配"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:239
msgid "Shared ownership, object lives while anyone holds it"
msgstr "共享所有权，只要有人持有对象就存活"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:239 src/appendix/cheat-sheet.md:45
msgid "`std::shared_ptr<T>`"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:239
msgid "`Rc<T>` / `Arc<T>`"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:240
msgid "Observe without keeping alive"
msgstr "观察但不让它保持存活"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:240 src/appendix/cheat-sheet.md:46
msgid "`std::weak_ptr<T>`"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:240
msgid "`rc::Weak<T>`"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:241
msgid ""
"Many objects of one type, referenced from many places, lifetime decided by "
"game logic"
msgstr "同一类型的许多对象，被许多地方引用，生命期由游戏逻辑决定"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:241
msgid "object pool + handles, or raw pointers and care"
msgstr "对象池 + 句柄，或者裸指针加上小心翼翼"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:241
msgid "`Arena<T>` + `Handle<T>`"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:243
msgid ""
"`Rc`/`Weak` work, and are the right answer for some structures (a shared "
"immutable asset, a UI tree). But for game objects whose lifetime is decided "
"by the game (\"the enemy dies when its HP hits zero\"), shared ownership is "
"the wrong model: nobody holding a reference should keep a dead enemy alive. "
"The arena makes the owner explicit, and handles make \"it might be gone\" "
"explicit."
msgstr ""
"`Rc`/`Weak` 是可行的，对某些结构来说也是正确的答案（共享的不可变资源、UI 树）。但对于生命期由游戏决定的游戏对象（“敌人的 HP "
"降到零时死亡”），共享所有权是错误的模型：任何持有引用的人都不应该让一个死去的敌人继续存活。arena "
"让所有者变得明确，句柄让“它可能已经不在了”变得明确。"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:249
msgid "Arenas of a different kind: bump allocation"
msgstr "另一种 arena：bump 分配"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:251
msgid ""
"\"Arena\" also names a second pattern you may know from C++ frame "
"allocators: allocate many small objects from one big block, then free the "
"whole block at once. In Rust this is the `bumpalo` crate. It hands out real "
"references whose lifetime is tied to the arena, so the borrow checker proves"
" nothing outlives the frame:"
msgstr ""
"“arena”还指另一种你可能在 C++ 帧分配器中见过的模式：从一大块内存中分配许多小对象，然后一次性释放整块内存。在 Rust 中，这就是 "
"`bumpalo` crate。它交出的是真正的引用，其生命周期与 arena 绑定，所以借用检查器可以证明没有任何东西活过这一帧："

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:266
msgid ""
"// Both allocations live in the arena. The references cannot escape it:\n"
"    // their lifetime is tied to `frame_alloc`.\n"
msgstr ""
"// 两次分配都位于 arena 中。引用无法逃出它：\n"
"    // 它们的生命周期与 `frame_alloc` 绑定。\n"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:277
msgid "// free everything from this frame, O(1)\n"
msgstr "// 以 O(1) 释放这一帧的所有内容\n"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:283
msgid ""
"Generational arenas are for long-lived objects with individual lifetimes. "
"Bump arenas are for short-lived scratch data with a shared lifetime. Engines"
" use both."
msgstr "分代 arena 用于有各自生命期的长期对象。bump arena 用于共享同一生命期的短期临时数据。引擎会同时使用两者。"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:287
msgid "Crates for real projects"
msgstr "用于真实项目的 crate"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:289
msgid ""
"Writing your own arena is a good exercise and fine for small projects. For "
"production, use a maintained crate:"
msgstr "自己编写 arena 是很好的练习，对小项目也够用了。在生产环境中，请使用有人维护的 crate："

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:292
msgid ""
"[`slotmap`](https://docs.rs/slotmap): the most widely used. `SlotMap` is the"
" design above; `DenseSlotMap` keeps values packed for faster iteration; "
"`SecondaryMap` attaches extra per-object data to existing keys, which is a "
"small step toward ECS components."
msgstr ""
"[`slotmap`](https://docs.rs/slotmap)：使用最广泛。`SlotMap` 就是上面的设计；`DenseSlotMap` "
"让值保持紧凑以加快迭代；`SecondaryMap` 可以为已有的键附加额外的逐对象数据，这已经是向 ECS 组件迈出的一小步。"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:296
msgid ""
"[`thunderdome`](https://docs.rs/thunderdome): a compact generational arena "
"with 8-byte `Option<Index>`."
msgstr ""
"[`thunderdome`](https://docs.rs/thunderdome)：一个紧凑的分代 arena，`Option<Index>` "
"只有 8 字节。"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:298
msgid "[`bumpalo`](https://docs.rs/bumpalo): bump allocation, as above."
msgstr "[`bumpalo`](https://docs.rs/bumpalo)：bump 分配，如上所述。"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:300
msgid ""
"The next step from \"an arena per object type, plus handles\" is an entity-"
"component system, where the handle is the entity and each component type has"
" its own storage. That is the [next chapter](ecs.md)."
msgstr ""
"从“每种对象类型一个 "
"arena，再加上句柄”再往前一步，就是实体组件系统（ECS）：句柄就是实体，每种组件类型都有自己的存储。这是[下一章](ecs.md)的内容。"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:306
msgid ""
"Add `fn get2_mut(&mut self, a: Handle<T>, b: Handle<T>) -> Option<(&mut T, "
"&mut T)>` that returns two distinct objects mutably (for a collision "
"response, say). Hint: `split_at_mut` or `get_disjoint_mut` from the "
"[borrowing chapter](../foundations/borrowing.md), and decide what to do when"
" `a == b`."
msgstr ""
"添加 `fn get2_mut(&mut self, a: Handle<T>, b: Handle<T>) -> Option<(&mut T, "
"&mut "
"T)>`，以可变方式返回两个不同的对象（比如用于碰撞响应）。提示：使用[借用一章](../foundations/borrowing.md)中的 "
"`split_at_mut` 或 `get_disjoint_mut`，并决定当 `a == b` 时该怎么办。"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:310
msgid ""
"Change `generation` to `NonZeroU32` starting at 1 and confirm with "
"`std::mem::size_of::<Option<Handle<Enemy>>>()` that it shrinks to 8 bytes."
msgstr ""
"把 `generation` 改成从 1 开始的 `NonZeroU32`，并用 "
"`std::mem::size_of::<Option<Handle<Enemy>>>()` 确认它缩小到了 8 字节。"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:312
msgid ""
"`remove` uses `wrapping_add`. After 2³² reuses of one slot, a very old "
"handle could match again. Make a slot retire permanently (never return to "
"the free list) when its generation would wrap. What does that cost?"
msgstr ""
"`remove` 使用了 `wrapping_add`。当一个槽位被重用 2³² "
"次之后，一个非常旧的句柄可能会再次匹配。让一个槽位在其代数即将回绕时永久退役（再也不放回空闲列表）。这样做的代价是什么？"

#: src/engine/handles-and-arenas.md:315
msgid ""
"Make `Arena::iter_mut` that yields `(Handle<T>, &mut T)`. Why can't it be "
"written by calling `get_mut` in a loop?"
msgstr ""
"编写 `Arena::iter_mut`，产生 `(Handle<T>, &mut T)`。为什么不能通过在循环中调用 `get_mut` 来实现它？"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:3
msgid ""
"The classic object-oriented engine has a `GameObject` base class, a scene "
"graph of parents and children pointing at each other, and components that "
"hold pointers to their owner and to sibling components. Translate that "
"literally into Rust and you hit the borrow checker on the first day: every "
"object is reachable from several places, and any of those places might want "
"to mutate it."
msgstr ""
"经典的面向对象引擎有一个 `GameObject` 基类，一个父子节点互相指向的场景图，以及持有指向所有者和兄弟组件的指针的组件。把它照字面翻译成 "
"Rust，你第一天就会撞上借用检查器：每个对象都能从好几个地方访问到，而其中任何一个地方都可能想修改它。"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:10
msgid ""
"The entity-component-system pattern (ECS) that many C++ engines adopted for "
"performance happens to be the shape that the borrow checker likes best. This"
" chapter explains why, builds a tiny ECS in about a hundred lines, and then "
"shows the crates real projects use."
msgstr ""
"许多 C++ 引擎出于性能考虑采用的实体组件系统（ECS）模式，恰好是借用检查器最喜欢的形态。本章解释其中的原因，用大约一百行代码构建一个微型 "
"ECS，然后介绍真实项目所用的 crate。"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:17
msgid "why a graph of mutually pointing objects fights the borrow checker,"
msgstr "为什么互相指向的对象图会和借用检查器冲突；"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:18
msgid "the struct-of-arrays world and split borrows,"
msgstr "数组结构体形式的 world 与拆分借用；"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:19
msgid "a tiny generic ECS with runtime-checked column borrows,"
msgstr "一个在运行时检查列借用的微型泛型 ECS；"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:20
msgid "archetypes, and the hecs and bevy_ecs crates,"
msgstr "原型（archetype），以及 hecs 和 bevy_ecs 这两个 crate；"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:21
msgid "running systems in parallel safely."
msgstr "安全地并行运行系统。"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:23
msgid "Why object graphs hurt"
msgstr "为什么对象图会带来麻烦"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:25
msgid "Here is a typical C++ scene node:"
msgstr "下面是一个典型的 C++ 场景节点："

#: src/engine/ecs.md:32
msgid "// each Component has Node* owner\n"
msgstr "// 每个 Component 都有一个 Node* owner\n"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:36
msgid ""
"Every pointer here is a second path to the same object. In C++ nothing stops"
" you from updating a child through `children[i]` while another function "
"holds a `Node&` to that same child. In Rust, a `&mut Node` must be the only "
"path to that node for as long as it lives. A literal translation therefore "
"ends up as `Rc<RefCell<Node>>` everywhere, with `Weak` for the parent link:"
msgstr ""
"这里的每个指针都是通往同一对象的第二条路径。在 C++ 中，当另一个函数持有某个子节点的 `Node&` 时，没有什么能阻止你通过 "
"`children[i]` 更新同一个子节点。在 Rust 中，`&mut Node` "
"在其整个生命期内必须是通往该节点的唯一路径。因此字面翻译的结果就是到处都是 `Rc<RefCell<Node>>`，父节点链接则用 `Weak`："

#: src/engine/ecs.md:76
msgid "\"{} world y = {}, parent = {}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/ecs.md:80
msgid ""
"It works, but look at the cost. Every node is a separate heap allocation "
"with a reference count, every field access goes through a runtime borrow "
"flag, a mistake becomes a `BorrowMutError` panic instead of a compile error,"
" and the data is scattered across the heap, which is the cache behavior ECS "
"was invented to avoid. This is a sign that the design is fighting the "
"language, not that Rust cannot express it."
msgstr ""
"它能工作，但看看代价。每个节点都是一次单独的、带引用计数的堆分配，每次字段访问都要经过一个运行时借用标志，错误会变成 `BorrowMutError` "
"panic 而不是编译错误，而且数据散落在堆上各处，这正是 ECS 被发明出来要避免的缓存行为。这说明设计在和语言作对，而不是 Rust 表达不了它。"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:90
msgid ""
"If you find yourself writing `Rc<RefCell<...>>` for most of your game "
"objects, stop and restructure. Put objects in arenas or component storage, "
"refer to them by [handle](handles-and-arenas.md), and pass the storage (not "
"the object) to the code that needs it."
msgstr ""
"如果你发现自己为大多数游戏对象都写上了 `Rc<RefCell<...>>`，请停下来重新组织结构。把对象放进 arena "
"或组件存储中，通过[句柄](handles-and-arenas.md)引用它们，并把存储（而不是对象）传给需要它的代码。"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:97
msgid "Step 1: a world of columns"
msgstr "第 1 步：由列组成的 world"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:99
msgid ""
"The simplest ECS is a struct of arrays. An entity is an index; each "
"component type is a column; a missing component is `None`:"
msgstr "最简单的 ECS 就是一个数组结构体。实体是一个索引；每种组件类型是一列；缺少的组件为 `None`："

#: src/engine/ecs.md:125
msgid "// A system is a function that borrows exactly the columns it needs.\n"
msgstr "// 系统就是一个只借用它所需列的函数。\n"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:147
msgid ""
"// Split borrows: &mut to one field and & to another at the same time is "
"fine.\n"
msgstr "// 拆分借用：同时对一个字段取 &mut、对另一个字段取 & 是没问题的。\n"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:151
msgid "\"player {:?} {:?}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/ecs.md:152
msgid "\"rock   {:?}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/ecs.md:156
msgid "Two things make this pleasant in Rust:"
msgstr "有两点让这在 Rust 中很顺手："

#: src/engine/ecs.md:158
msgid ""
"**Split borrows.** `&mut world.positions` and `&world.velocities` borrow "
"different fields, so the compiler allows both at once. This is the same rule"
" that lets the particle loop in [Memory and performance](../systems/memory-"
"and-performance.md) vectorize: the compiler knows the slices do not alias."
msgstr ""
"**拆分借用。** `&mut world.positions` 和 `&world.velocities` "
"借用的是不同的字段，所以编译器允许两者同时存在。正是同一条规则让[内存布局与性能](../systems/memory-and-"
"performance.md)中的粒子循环得以向量化：编译器知道这些切片互不重叠。"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:163
msgid ""
"**Systems declare their access in their signature.** `movement` cannot touch"
" health; `poison` cannot touch positions. You can read a system's data "
"dependencies from its parameter list."
msgstr ""
"**系统在签名中声明它们的访问。** `movement` 无法访问 health；`poison` 无法访问 "
"positions。从一个系统的参数列表就能读出它的数据依赖。"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:167
msgid ""
"What this version lacks is extensibility: every component type is a field of"
" `World`, and despawning leaves holes. Despawning is solved with "
"generations, exactly as in the [arena chapter](handles-and-arenas.md). "
"Extensibility needs type erasure."
msgstr ""
"这个版本缺少的是可扩展性：每种组件类型都是 `World` 的一个字段，而且销毁实体会留下空洞。销毁的问题用代数来解决，和 [arena "
"一章](handles-and-arenas.md)完全一样。可扩展性则需要类型擦除。"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:172
msgid "Step 2: a generic world"
msgstr "第 2 步：泛型的 world"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:174
msgid ""
"A reusable ECS cannot know the component types in advance. It stores one "
"column per type in a map keyed by `TypeId`, with the column type-erased as "
"`Box<dyn Any>`. Each column sits inside a `RefCell`, so that a query can "
"borrow the `Position` column mutably and the `Velocity` column immutably at "
"the same time, through a shared `&World`:"
msgstr ""
"一个可复用的 ECS 无法预先知道组件类型。它在一个以 `TypeId` 为键的映射中为每种类型存放一列，列的类型被擦除为 `Box<dyn "
"Any>`。每一列都放在一个 `RefCell` 中，这样一次查询就可以通过共享的 `&World`，同时可变地借用 `Position` "
"列、不可变地借用 `Velocity` 列："

#: src/engine/ecs.md:190
msgid "// each value is a RefCell<Vec<Option<T>>>\n"
msgstr "// 每个值都是一个 RefCell<Vec<Option<T>>>\n"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:205
msgid "\"column type matches its TypeId\""
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/ecs.md:206
msgid "// &mut World: no runtime check needed\n"
msgstr "// &mut World：不需要运行时检查\n"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:217
msgid "\"no such component type\""
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/ecs.md:251
msgid "\"{:>6} at {:?}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/ecs.md:259
msgid "\"ship\""
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/ecs.md:263
msgid "\"buoy\""
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/ecs.md:271
msgid ""
"This is the trade most ECS libraries make internally. The compiler cannot "
"see which columns a query will touch, because the types are chosen at run "
"time through a map, so the borrow rules move to run time: a system that asks"
" for `write::<Position>()` twice panics with \"already borrowed\" instead of"
" creating two aliasing `&mut`. The guarantee is the same as the compiler's "
"(never two mutable paths to the same column), only checked later. Real "
"libraries check these conflicts once, when a query or system is created, "
"rather than on every access."
msgstr ""
"这是大多数 ECS 库在内部做出的取舍。编译器看不出一次查询会访问哪些列，因为类型是在运行时通过映射选出来的，所以借用规则被挪到了运行时：一个两次请求 "
"`write::<Position>()` 的系统会以“already borrowed”panic，而不是产生两个互相重叠的 "
"`&mut`。保证与编译器提供的相同（同一列永远不会有两条可变路径），只是检查得更晚。真正的库会在创建查询或系统时检查一次这些冲突，而不是在每次访问时检查。"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:283
msgid ""
"`Box<dyn Any>` plus `downcast_ref` is Rust's checked equivalent of storing a"
" `void*` next to a type ID and `static_cast`ing it back. `downcast_ref` "
"compares `TypeId`s and returns `None` on mismatch, so a bug gives you a "
"clean panic instead of reinterpreting memory."
msgstr ""
"`Box<dyn Any>` 加上 `downcast_ref`，是 Rust 中“在类型 ID 旁边存一个 `void*`，再用 "
"`static_cast` 转回来”的带检查版本。`downcast_ref` 会比较 `TypeId`，不匹配时返回 `None`，所以 bug "
"只会导致一次干净的 panic，而不是把内存当成错误的类型来解释。"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:290
msgid "Archetypes"
msgstr "原型（Archetype）"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:292
msgid ""
"Columns of `Option<T>` indexed by entity waste memory when components are "
"sparse, and a query over two components still walks every entity. Production"
" ECS libraries (Unity DOTS, flecs, bevy_ecs, hecs) use **archetypes** "
"instead: all entities with exactly the same set of component types are "
"stored together, in one table with a dense column per type."
msgstr ""
"当组件很稀疏时，按实体索引的 `Option<T>` 列会浪费内存，而对两个组件的查询仍然要遍历每个实体。生产级的 ECS 库（Unity "
"DOTS、flecs、bevy_ecs、hecs）改用**原型**：组件类型集合完全相同的所有实体存放在一起，位于一张表中，每种类型一列密集存储。"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:298
msgid "Archetype"
msgstr "原型"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:298
msgid "Columns (dense, same length)"
msgstr "列（密集，长度相同）"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:298
msgid "Entities"
msgstr "实体"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:300
msgid "{Position, Velocity}"
msgstr "{Position, Velocity}"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:300
msgid "`Vec<Position>`, `Vec<Velocity>`"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/ecs.md:300
msgid "ship, bullet 1, bullet 2"
msgstr "飞船、子弹 1、子弹 2"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:301
msgid "{Position, Name}"
msgstr "{Position, Name}"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:301
msgid "`Vec<Position>`, `Vec<Name>`"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/ecs.md:301
msgid "buoy"
msgstr "浮标"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:302
msgid "{Position, Velocity, Health}"
msgstr "{Position, Velocity, Health}"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:302
msgid "three columns"
msgstr "三列"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:302
msgid "player"
msgstr "玩家"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:304
msgid ""
"A query for `(&mut Position, &Velocity)` visits only the tables whose "
"archetype contains both types, and inside each table zips two dense slices: "
"the same tight loop as the struct-of-arrays version, with no `Option` "
"checks. Adding or removing a component moves the entity to a different "
"table, which is the cost of the design. An entity ID maps to (table, row) "
"through a small lookup array with generations, like the arena in the "
"previous chapter."
msgstr ""
"对 `(&mut Position, &Velocity)` 的查询只访问那些原型同时包含这两种类型的表，并在每张表内部把两个密集切片 zip "
"起来：与数组结构体版本同样紧凑的循环，而且没有 `Option` 检查。添加或移除组件会把实体移到另一张表中，这是这种设计的代价。实体 ID "
"通过一个带代数的小型查找数组映射到（表，行），就像上一章的 arena。"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:311
msgid ""
"Rust does not change how archetypes work. What it changes is that a query "
"hands out `&mut Position` and `&Velocity` references, and the library must "
"prove they never alias. Libraries do that with the same runtime check we "
"used, done once per query, plus a little `unsafe` inside to hand out the "
"slices."
msgstr ""
"Rust 并没有改变原型的工作方式。它改变的是：查询会交出 `&mut Position` 和 `&Velocity` "
"引用，而库必须证明它们永远不会重叠。库用的是和我们一样的运行时检查（每次查询做一次），再在内部用一点 `unsafe` 交出切片。"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:316
msgid "Using hecs"
msgstr "使用 hecs"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:318
msgid ""
"[hecs](https://docs.rs/hecs) is a small, library-style archetype ECS: a "
"`World` and queries, no scheduler and no framework. It is the closest thing "
"to EnTT in spirit:"
msgstr ""
"[hecs](https://docs.rs/hecs) 是一个小巧的、库风格的原型 ECS：一个 `World` "
"加上查询，没有调度器，也不是框架。从理念上说，它是最接近 EnTT 的："

#: src/engine/ecs.md:332
msgid "// Iterate entities that have Position and Velocity, but not Frozen.\n"
msgstr "// 遍历具有 Position 和 Velocity、但没有 Frozen 的实体。\n"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:342
msgid "// moves the entity to another archetype\n"
msgstr "// 把实体移到另一个原型\n"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:343
msgid "// the old Entity is now stale: get() returns Err\n"
msgstr "// 旧的 Entity 现在已经过期：get() 返回 Err\n"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:346
msgid ""
"`query_mut` takes `&mut World`, so the compiler alone proves exclusivity. "
"The shared version, `world.query::<...>()` on `&World`, checks column "
"borrows at run time, like our `RefCell`s."
msgstr ""
"`query_mut` 接收 `&mut World`，所以仅靠编译器就能证明独占性。共享版本，即对 `&World` 调用的 "
"`world.query::<...>()`，会在运行时检查列借用，就像我们的 `RefCell` 一样。"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:350
msgid "Using bevy_ecs"
msgstr "使用 bevy_ecs"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:352
msgid ""
"[bevy_ecs](https://docs.rs/bevy_ecs) is the ECS of the Bevy engine, and "
"works as a standalone crate. Systems are ordinary functions whose "
"**parameter types describe their data access**. The scheduler reads those "
"types and runs systems whose access does not conflict on different threads:"
msgstr ""
"[bevy_ecs](https://docs.rs/bevy_ecs) 是 Bevy 引擎的 ECS，也可以作为独立的 crate "
"使用。系统是普通的函数，它们的**参数类型描述了它们的数据访问**。调度器读取这些类型，并把访问不冲突的系统放到不同的线程上运行："

#: src/engine/ecs.md:383
msgid "// disjoint access: may run in parallel\n"
msgstr "// 访问互不相交：可以并行运行\n"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:387
msgid ""
"`movement` writes `Position` and reads `Velocity` and `Time`; `regenerate` "
"writes `Health`. No overlap, so the scheduler may run them at the same time."
" If two systems both wrote `Position`, it would run them one after the "
"other. A single system that asks for `Query<&mut Position>` twice is "
"rejected when the schedule is built."
msgstr ""
"`movement` 写入 `Position`，读取 `Velocity` 和 `Time`；`regenerate` 写入 "
"`Health`。没有重叠，所以调度器可以同时运行它们。如果两个系统都写入 `Position`，调度器就会让它们先后运行。一个两次请求 "
"`Query<&mut Position>` 的系统会在构建调度时被拒绝。"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:393
msgid ""
"`Res<Time>` is a **resource**: a singleton stored in the world. This is how "
"ECS code handles global state without `static mut`, a topic the [game "
"loop](game-loop.md) chapter returns to."
msgstr ""
"`Res<Time>` 是一个**资源**（resource）：存放在 world 中的单例。这就是 ECS 代码在没有 `static mut` "
"的情况下处理全局状态的方式，[游戏循环](game-loop.md)一章会再次讨论这个话题。"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:397
msgid "Parallel systems, by hand"
msgstr "手动并行运行系统"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:399
msgid ""
"The scheduler is not magic. Split borrows plus scoped threads give you the "
"same thing for the struct-of-arrays world, and the compiler checks it:"
msgstr "调度器并不神奇。对于数组结构体形式的 world，拆分借用加上作用域线程也能做到同样的事，而且由编译器检查："

#: src/engine/ecs.md:417
msgid ""
"// Destructure into disjoint borrows, then hand them to different threads.\n"
msgstr "// 解构成互不相交的借用，再把它们交给不同的线程。\n"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:436
msgid ""
"If both threads tried to write `pos`, the program would not compile. In C++,"
" the same mistake compiles and becomes a data race you look for in a frame "
"capture. Here the scheduler's job, deciding what can run together, is done "
"by the type checker."
msgstr ""
"如果两个线程都试图写入 `pos`，程序就无法编译。在 C++ "
"中，同样的错误能够编译，并变成一个你要在帧捕获中寻找的数据竞争。在这里，调度器的工作，也就是决定哪些可以一起运行，是由类型检查器完成的。"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:441
msgid "Hierarchies in an ECS"
msgstr "ECS 中的层次结构"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:443
msgid ""
"Scene graphs do not disappear; they become data. Parent links are components"
" holding entity IDs, and the world transform is computed by a system:"
msgstr "场景图并没有消失，而是变成了数据。父节点链接是持有实体 ID 的组件，世界变换由一个系统计算："

#: src/engine/ecs.md:451
msgid ""
"// Assumes parents come before children (sort once when the hierarchy "
"changes).\n"
msgstr "// 假设父节点排在子节点之前（层次结构改变时排序一次）。\n"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:461
msgid "// root, arm, hand\n"
msgstr "// 根、手臂、手\n"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:465
msgid "\"{world:?}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/ecs.md:469
msgid ""
"No `Rc`, no `RefCell`, no `Weak`: the parent link is an index, the borrows "
"are three plain slices, and the update is a linear pass over contiguous "
"memory. Compare it with the `Rc<RefCell<Node>>` version at the top of the "
"chapter."
msgstr ""
"没有 `Rc`，没有 `RefCell`，没有 "
"`Weak`：父节点链接是一个索引，借用是三个普通的切片，更新是对连续内存的一次线性遍历。把它和本章开头的 `Rc<RefCell<Node>>` "
"版本比较一下。"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:477
msgid "`GameObject*` graph, components with owner pointers"
msgstr "`GameObject*` 图，组件带有指向所有者的指针"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:477
msgid "Entities as IDs, components in columns or archetype tables"
msgstr "实体是 ID，组件存放在列或原型表中"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:478
msgid "`std::shared_ptr` + `weak_ptr` scene graph"
msgstr "`std::shared_ptr` + `weak_ptr` 场景图"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:478
msgid "`Parent(Entity)` component and a propagation system"
msgstr "`Parent(Entity)` 组件加一个传播系统"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:479 src/appendix/cheat-sheet.md:164
msgid "EnTT, flecs"
msgstr "EnTT、flecs"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:479
msgid "hecs (library), bevy_ecs (with scheduler)"
msgstr "hecs（库）、bevy_ecs（带调度器）"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:480
msgid "Hand-written job graph with read/write declarations"
msgstr "手写的、带读写声明的任务图"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:480
msgid "System parameter types (`Query<&mut T>`, `Res<T>`)"
msgstr "系统参数类型（`Query<&mut T>`、`Res<T>`）"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:481
msgid "Data races found in captures"
msgstr "在捕获中发现数据竞争"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:481
msgid "Conflicting access rejected by the compiler or at schedule build"
msgstr "冲突的访问被编译器拒绝，或在构建调度时被拒绝"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:482
msgid "`void*` + type ID"
msgstr "`void*` + 类型 ID"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:482
msgid "`Box<dyn Any>` + `downcast_ref`"
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/ecs.md:486
msgid ""
"Add generational entity IDs and a `despawn` to the generic `World`, reusing "
"the `Handle` idea from [Handles and arenas](handles-and-arenas.md). What "
"should `insert` do with a stale entity?"
msgstr ""
"借鉴[句柄与 arena](handles-and-arenas.md) 中的 `Handle` 思路，给泛型的 `World` 添加分代实体 ID 和"
" `despawn`。对于过期的实体，`insert` 应该怎么做？"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:489
msgid ""
"In the generic `World`, write a system that calls "
"`world.write::<Position>()` twice in the same scope. Run it. Which error do "
"you get, and when would the compiler have caught it instead?"
msgstr ""
"在泛型的 `World` 中，编写一个在同一作用域内两次调用 `world.write::<Position>()` "
"的系统。运行它。你会得到什么错误？编译器在什么情况下本可以发现它？"

#: src/engine/ecs.md:492
msgid ""
"Add a third thread to the parallel example that reads `pos` while the first "
"writes it. Read the compiler error, then fix it by running the reader after "
"the scope ends."
msgstr "在并行示例中添加第三个线程，在第一个线程写入 `pos` 的同时读取它。阅读编译错误，然后通过在作用域结束后再运行读取者来修复它。"

#: src/engine/math-and-simd.md:1
msgid "Math libraries and SIMD"
msgstr "数学库与 SIMD"

#: src/engine/math-and-simd.md:3
msgid ""
"Every engine has a vector math library, and in C++ it is usually GLM, "
"DirectXMath, Eigen or something written in-house. Rust has a few mature "
"ones, and they look familiar: small `Copy` structs with overloaded "
"operators. This chapter shows how to use them, how to lay out math types for"
" the GPU, and how to go from auto-vectorized loops down to explicit SIMD "
"intrinsics."
msgstr ""
"每个引擎都有一个向量数学库，在 C++ 中通常是 GLM、DirectXMath、Eigen 或者自研的库。Rust "
"有几个成熟的数学库，它们看起来很眼熟：带有重载运算符的小型 `Copy` 结构体。本章介绍如何使用它们、如何为 GPU "
"安排数学类型的布局，以及如何从自动向量化的循环一路深入到显式的 SIMD 内建函数。"

#: src/engine/math-and-simd.md:11
msgid "glam and nalgebra, and how they compare with GLM and Eigen,"
msgstr "glam 和 nalgebra，以及它们与 GLM 和 Eigen 的对比；"

#: src/engine/math-and-simd.md:12
msgid "`#[repr(C)]` math types and `bytemuck` for GPU uploads,"
msgstr "`#[repr(C)]` 数学类型，以及用 `bytemuck` 上传到 GPU；"

#: src/engine/math-and-simd.md:13
msgid "checking auto-vectorization,"
msgstr "检查自动向量化；"

#: src/engine/math-and-simd.md:14
msgid "`core::arch` intrinsics and runtime CPU feature detection,"
