#: src/engine/opengl.md:27
msgid ""
"The **`gl`** crate is a generated binding with exactly the C names: you call"
" `gl::GenBuffers(1, &mut id)` inside `unsafe`, and porting C++ code is "
"mostly mechanical. **`glow`** (\"GL on whatever\") wraps the same calls in "
"slightly more Rust-like signatures (returning the new object, taking slices "
"instead of pointer + length) and runs on desktop GL, GLES and WebGL2 in the "
"browser. Both leave every call `unsafe`, because the driver can do anything "
"with a bad argument. This chapter uses glow."
msgstr ""
"**`gl`** crate 是自动生成的绑定，名字与 C 完全一致：你在 `unsafe` 中调用 `gl::GenBuffers(1, &mut "
"id)`，移植 C++ 代码基本是机械操作。**`glow`**（\"GL on whatever\"）把同样的调用包装成稍微更像 Rust "
"的签名（返回新对象、接收切片而非指针加长度），可以运行在桌面 GL、GLES 以及浏览器中的 WebGL2 上。两者都让每个调用保持 "
"`unsafe`，因为参数错误时驱动可能做出任何事。本章使用 glow。"

