#: src/engine/vulkan.md:3
msgid ""
"Vulkan was designed to be explicit: you create every object, you synchronize"
" every access, and you destroy everything in the right order. That makes it "
"a natural fit for Rust's ownership model, and also the place where you feel "
"most clearly what Rust can check and what it cannot. This chapter uses "
"[ash](https://docs.rs/ash), the most widely used Vulkan binding, which is a "
"thin, `unsafe`, one-to-one mapping of the C API."
msgstr ""
"Vulkan 的设计宗旨是显式：每个对象都由你创建，每次访问都由你同步，所有东西都由你按正确顺序销毁。这使它与 Rust "
"的所有权模型天然契合，也是你最能清楚感受到 Rust 能检查什么、不能检查什么的地方。本章使用 "
"[ash](https://docs.rs/ash)，这是使用最广泛的 Vulkan 绑定，它是对 C API 的一对一、`unsafe` 的薄映射。"

