#: src/engine/vulkan.md:241
msgid "// ...it is destroyed after the last buffer\n"
msgstr "// ……它在最后一个缓冲区之后才被销毁\n"

#: src/engine/vulkan.md:245
msgid ""
"The order of destruction is now a property of the data structure, not of the"
" order of lines in a shutdown function. `Arc` costs an atomic increment per "
"created object, which is nothing compared with `vkCreateBuffer`."
msgstr ""
"销毁顺序现在是数据结构的属性，而不是关闭函数中代码行顺序的属性。`Arc` 每创建一个对象只需一次原子自增，与 `vkCreateBuffer` "
"相比微不足道。"

#: src/engine/vulkan.md:249
msgid "Frames in flight"
msgstr "多帧并行"

#: src/engine/vulkan.md:251
msgid ""
"The hardest lifetime in Vulkan is not a CPU lifetime at all. When you drop a"
" `Buffer` on the CPU, the GPU may still be executing a command buffer, "
"recorded one or two frames ago, that reads it. Destroying it immediately is "
"a use-after-free on the GPU, and `Drop` alone cannot know."
msgstr ""
"Vulkan 中最难的生命周期根本不是 CPU 上的生命周期。当你在 CPU 上丢弃一个 `Buffer` 时，GPU "
"可能仍在执行一两帧前录制的、读取它的命令缓冲区。立即销毁它就是 GPU 上的释放后使用，而单靠 `Drop` 无从得知。"

#: src/engine/vulkan.md:256
msgid ""
"The standard solution, in C++ and in Rust, is a **deletion queue**: dropping"
" a resource defers its destruction until the frame that last used it has "
"finished on the GPU (its fence has signaled). With `N` frames in flight, a "
"resource dropped during frame `f` is safe to destroy when frame `f` "
"completes, which you know when you wait on that frame's fence at the start "
"of frame `f + N`:"
msgstr ""
"无论在 C++ 还是 Rust 中，标准解法都是**删除队列**：丢弃资源时，把它的销毁推迟到最后使用它的那一帧在 GPU 上完成（其 fence "
"已发出信号）之后。在有 `N` 帧并行时，在第 `f` 帧丢弃的资源，在第 `f` 帧完成后即可安全销毁，而你在第 `f + N` 帧开始等待该帧的 "
"fence 时就能知道这一点："

#: src/engine/vulkan.md:270
msgid "// the ids are only printed\n"
msgstr "// 这些 id 只用于打印\n"

#: src/engine/vulkan.md:275
msgid "// (frame in which it was dropped, object)\n"
msgstr "// （丢弃时所在的帧，对象）\n"

#: src/engine/vulkan.md:279
msgid "/// Call after waiting on the fence of `completed_frame`.\n"
msgstr "/// 在等待 `completed_frame` 的 fence 之后调用。\n"

#: src/engine/vulkan.md:283
msgid "\"  destroy {obj:?} (dropped in frame {frame})\""
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/vulkan.md:305
msgid "// Not destroyed now: the GPU may still be reading it.\n"
msgstr "// 现在不销毁：GPU 可能仍在读取它。\n"

#: src/engine/vulkan.md:313
msgid "\"frame {}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/vulkan.md:315
msgid "// Here a real renderer waits on the fence of frame (frame - N).\n"
msgstr "// 真正的渲染器会在这里等待第 (frame - N) 帧的 fence。\n"

#: src/engine/vulkan.md:330
msgid "// dropped in frame 1\n"
msgstr "// 在第 1 帧丢弃\n"

#: src/engine/vulkan.md:332
msgid "// destroyed at the start of frame 3\n"
msgstr "// 在第 3 帧开始时销毁\n"

#: src/engine/vulkan.md:337
msgid ""
"The simplification here is that a buffer records the frame in which it was "
"_created_; a real renderer records the last frame in which it was _used_, "
"usually by bumping a counter when a command buffer references it. Some "
"engines use a reference count instead: command buffers hold an `Arc` to "
"every resource they use and drop those references when their fence signals, "
"so the resource's `Drop` runs at the right time automatically. wgpu does "
"exactly this internally."
msgstr ""
"这里的简化在于，缓冲区记录的是它被<em>创建</em>的帧；真正的渲染器记录的是它最后被<em>使用</em>的帧，通常在命令缓冲区引用它时递增一个计数器。有些引擎改用引用计数：命令缓冲区对它使用的每个资源持有一个"
" `Arc`，并在其 fence 发出信号时丢弃这些引用，这样资源的 `Drop` 就会自动在正确的时间运行。wgpu 内部正是这样做的。"

#: src/engine/vulkan.md:348
msgid ""
"Command pools and command buffers are \"externally synchronized\" in Vulkan:"
" only one thread may use them at a time. Map that to `&mut`: if recording "
"requires `&mut CommandBuffer`, the compiler guarantees one recorder at a "
"time, and you give each worker thread its own pool. Queues likewise: "
"`queue_submit` taking `&mut Queue` (or a `Mutex<Queue>`) turns a spec rule "
"into a type rule."
msgstr ""
"在 Vulkan 中，命令池和命令缓冲区是\"外部同步\"的：同一时间只能有一个线程使用它们。把这映射为 `&mut`：如果录制需要 `&mut "
"CommandBuffer`，编译器就保证同一时间只有一个录制者，而你给每个工作线程分配自己的池。队列也一样：让 `queue_submit` 接收 "
"`&mut Queue`（或 `Mutex<Queue>`），就把规范规则变成了类型规则。"

#: src/engine/vulkan.md:356
msgid "Memory allocation"
msgstr "内存分配"

#: src/engine/vulkan.md:358
msgid ""
"Allocating a `VkDeviceMemory` per buffer does not scale, so C++ engines use "
"VulkanMemoryAllocator. In Rust the common choices are the [gpu-"
"allocator](https://docs.rs/gpu-allocator) crate (pure Rust, used by many "
"projects, also supports D3D12) and [vk-mem](https://docs.rs/vk-mem) "
"(bindings to VMA itself). Both return allocations that you free explicitly, "
"and both fit the owning-wrapper pattern above: the allocation lives in the "
"`Buffer` wrapper and is freed in its `Drop` (or its deletion-queue entry)."
msgstr ""
"为每个缓冲区分配一个 `VkDeviceMemory` 无法扩展，所以 C++ 引擎使用 VulkanMemoryAllocator。在 Rust "
"中，常见的选择是 [gpu-allocator](https://docs.rs/gpu-allocator) crate（纯 "
"Rust，被许多项目使用，也支持 D3D12）和 [vk-mem](https://docs.rs/vk-mem)（VMA "
"本身的绑定）。两者返回的分配都需要显式释放，也都适合上面的拥有型封装模式：分配存放在 `Buffer` 封装中，并在其 "
"`Drop`（或其删除队列条目）中释放。"

