#: src/engine/openxr.md:98
msgid "Connecting to Vulkan"
msgstr "连接到 Vulkan"

#: src/engine/openxr.md:100
msgid ""
"The Vulkan instance and device must be created **through OpenXR** (with "
"`XR_KHR_vulkan_enable2`), because the runtime needs to add its own "
"extensions and pick the physical device the headset is attached to. The "
"`openxr` crate wraps the calls and leaves the Vulkan objects as raw handles,"
" which you then hand to ash:"
msgstr ""
"Vulkan 实例和设备必须**通过 OpenXR** 创建（借助 "
"`XR_KHR_vulkan_enable2`），因为运行时需要添加自己的扩展，并选择连接头显的物理设备。`openxr` crate "
"封装了这些调用，并把 Vulkan 对象作为原始句柄留给你，然后你再把它们交给 ash："

#: src/engine/openxr.md:108
msgid "// The runtime tells us which Vulkan versions it can work with.\n"
msgstr "// 运行时告诉我们它能配合哪些 Vulkan 版本。\n"

#: src/engine/openxr.md:115
msgid ""
"// OpenXR calls vkCreateInstance for us, adding the extensions it needs.\n"
msgstr "// OpenXR 替我们调用 vkCreateInstance，并添加它需要的扩展。\n"

#: src/engine/openxr.md:123
msgid "// OpenXR error\n"
msgstr "// OpenXR 错误\n"

#: src/engine/openxr.md:124
msgid "// Vulkan error\n"
msgstr "// Vulkan 错误\n"

#: src/engine/openxr.md:129
msgid "// The physical device that drives the headset.\n"
msgstr "// 驱动头显的物理设备。\n"

#: src/engine/openxr.md:133
msgid ""
"// ... create the logical device the same way, with create_vulkan_device "
"...\n"
msgstr "// ……用同样的方式，通过 create_vulkan_device 创建逻辑设备……\n"

#: src/engine/openxr.md:150
msgid ""
"This is the most `unsafe` part of an OpenXR program, and it is unsafe for a "
"real reason: OpenXR and ash each have their own copy of the Vulkan handle "
"types, and the code converts between them through raw integers "
"(`as_raw`/`from_raw`). The compiler cannot check that the `VkDevice` you "
"pass really came from that `VkInstance`. Wrap this setup in one function "
"that returns your renderer's safe types, and the rest of the program never "
"sees it."
msgstr ""
"这是 OpenXR 程序中最 `unsafe` 的部分，而且有真实的原因：OpenXR 和 ash 各有一份 Vulkan "
"句柄类型，代码通过原始整数（`as_raw`/`from_raw`）在两者之间转换。编译器无法检查你传入的 `VkDevice` 是否真的来自那个 "
"`VkInstance`。把这段初始化封装在一个返回渲染器安全类型的函数中，程序的其余部分就永远看不到它。"

#: src/engine/openxr.md:157
msgid ""
"The `G` parameter of `Session<G>` is the payoff: a `Session<xr::Vulkan>` "
"only produces swapchains whose images are `VkImage`s, and only accepts a "
"Vulkan `SessionCreateInfo`. Mixing graphics APIs is a type error, not a "
"runtime crash."
msgstr ""
"`Session<G>` 的 `G` 参数就是回报：`Session<xr::Vulkan>` 只会产生图像为 `VkImage` 的交换链，也只接受 "
"Vulkan 的 `SessionCreateInfo`。混用图形 API 是类型错误，而不是运行时崩溃。"

#: src/engine/openxr.md:161
msgid "The session state machine"
msgstr "会话状态机"

#: src/engine/openxr.md:163
msgid ""
"An OpenXR session moves through states the runtime controls: the user puts "
"the headset on or takes it off, opens the system menu, or another app takes "
"focus. You learn about it from events, and you must respond: begin the "
"session when it is `READY`, end it when it is `STOPPING`, exit on `EXITING` "
"or `LOSS_PENDING`. Here is the logic as plain Rust, with a stand-in for the "
"runtime's events:"
msgstr ""
"OpenXR "
"会话在运行时控制的各个状态之间切换：用户戴上或摘下头显、打开系统菜单，或者另一个应用获得焦点。你通过事件得知这些变化，并且必须作出响应：状态为 "
"`READY` 时开始会话，`STOPPING` 时结束会话，`EXITING` 或 `LOSS_PENDING` 时退出。下面用普通 Rust "
"表达这段逻辑，并用一个替身模拟运行时的事件："

#: src/engine/openxr.md:180
msgid "\"  -> session.begin()\""
msgstr ""

#: src/engine/openxr.md:181
msgid "\"  -> session.end()\""
msgstr ""

