#: src/engine/openxr.md:431
msgid ""
"With glam, the same projection is a "
"`Mat4::from_cols_array_2d(&projection(...))` and the view is "
"`Mat4::from_rotation_translation(q, p).inverse()`; the hand-written version "
"is shown so you can see exactly what OpenXR's numbers mean. Two pitfalls "
"that are not Rust-specific but cost everyone a day:"
msgstr ""
"使用 glam 时，同样的投影是 `Mat4::from_cols_array_2d(&projection(...))`，视图是 "
"`Mat4::from_rotation_translation(q, p).inverse()`；这里展示手写版本，是为了让你确切看到 OpenXR "
"的数字意味着什么。有两个陷阱并非 Rust 特有，却会让每个人都浪费一天："

#: src/engine/openxr.md:436
msgid ""
"OpenXR's FOV is **not symmetric**. A symmetric `perspective(fovy, aspect)` "
"looks almost right and makes users feel sick."
msgstr ""
"OpenXR 的 FOV **不是对称的**。对称的 `perspective(fovy, aspect)` 看起来几乎正确，却会让用户感到不适；"

#: src/engine/openxr.md:438
msgid ""
"`angle_down` and `angle_left` are negative. Clip-space y is down in Vulkan "
"and up in OpenGL; use the GL variant of the formula (`h = u - d`, depth "
"\\-1..1) for OpenGL."
msgstr ""
"`angle_down` 和 `angle_left` 是负数。裁剪空间的 y 在 Vulkan 中朝下，在 OpenGL 中朝上；对 OpenGL "
"请使用公式的 GL 版本（`h = u - d`，深度 \\-1..1）。"

