#: src/engine/ui.md:29
msgid ""
"The lambda holds `this` for as long as the button exists, and mutates "
"`light` whenever a click arrives. Nothing stops two callbacks from changing "
"the same state, or a callback from running after `this` is destroyed. The "
"direct Rust translation does not compile, because a closure stored inside "
"`editor` cannot also hold a mutable borrow of `editor`:"
msgstr ""
"只要按钮还存在，这个 lambda 就一直持有 `this`，并在每次点击时修改 "
"`light`。没有任何机制阻止两个回调修改同一份状态，也没有任何机制阻止回调在 `this` 被销毁之后运行。直接翻译成 Rust "
"是无法编译的，因为存放在 `editor` 内部的闭包不能同时持有 `editor` 的可变借用："

#: src/engine/ui.md:42
msgid "// error[E0506], error[E0597]\n"
msgstr "// error[E0506], error[E0597]\n"

#: src/engine/ui.md:49
msgid ""
"You can make it work with shared ownership, `Rc<RefCell<State>>` captured by"
" every callback ([Smart pointers](../foundations/smart-pointers.md)), and "
"bindings to C and C++ toolkits (GTK, Qt) do exactly that. But it moves the "
"borrow checking to run time and spreads `borrow_mut()` across the UI. Rust "
"UI libraries instead pick one of three designs that avoid long-lived "
"callbacks holding mutable state:"
msgstr ""
"你可以用共享所有权让它工作：每个回调都捕获一个 "
"`Rc<RefCell<State>>`（[智能指针与内部可变性](../foundations/smart-pointers.md)），而 C 和 "
"C++ 工具包（GTK、Qt）的绑定正是这样做的。但这会把借用检查推迟到运行时，并让 `borrow_mut()` 散布在整个 UI 中。Rust 的 "
"UI 库则从三种设计中选择一种，以避免长期存活的回调持有可变状态："

