#: src/engine/hot-reload-and-plugins.md:3
msgid ""
"C++ engines reload game code by building it as a DLL, unloading the old one "
"and loading the new one while the process keeps running (Handmade Hero, "
"Live++, Unreal's Live Coding). Plugins work the same way, with a C or C++ "
"interface that both sides agree on. Rust can do all of this, but there is "
"one fact to understand first: **Rust has no stable ABI**. This chapter "
"explains what that means, then shows the practical ways to reload code, load"
" plugins and embed a scripting language."
msgstr ""
"C++ 引擎重载游戏代码的方式是：把它构建为 DLL，在进程持续运行的同时卸载旧的、加载新的（Handmade Hero、Live++、Unreal 的"
" Live Coding）。插件的工作方式相同，使用双方约定的 C 或 C++ 接口。Rust 可以做到所有这些，但有一个事实需要先理解：**Rust "
"没有稳定的 ABI**。本章解释这意味着什么，然后展示重载代码、加载插件和嵌入脚本语言的实用方法。"

#: src/engine/hot-reload-and-plugins.md:13
msgid "what \"no stable ABI\" means, and the C ABI escape hatch,"
msgstr "\"没有稳定 ABI\"意味着什么，以及 C ABI 这个逃生舱；"

#: src/engine/hot-reload-and-plugins.md:14
msgid "loading dynamic libraries with `libloading`,"
msgstr "用 `libloading` 加载动态库；"

#: src/engine/hot-reload-and-plugins.md:15
msgid "hot reloading game code, and keeping state across reloads,"
msgstr "热重载游戏代码，以及在重载之间保持状态；"

#: src/engine/hot-reload-and-plugins.md:16
msgid "the hot-reload tools available today,"
msgstr "目前可用的热重载工具；"

#: src/engine/hot-reload-and-plugins.md:17
msgid "scripting with Lua, Rhai and WebAssembly."
msgstr "用 Lua、Rhai 和 WebAssembly 编写脚本。"

#: src/engine/hot-reload-and-plugins.md:19
msgid "No stable ABI"
msgstr "没有稳定的 ABI"

#: src/engine/hot-reload-and-plugins.md:21
msgid ""
"The layout of a default Rust struct, the calling convention of a Rust "
"function, the layout of `Vec`, `String` and trait objects, and the mangling "
"of symbol names can all change between compiler versions, and even between "
"two builds with different flags. Rust makes no promise, and in practice "
"field reordering means it really does change. C++ is in a similar position "
"in theory (the ABI belongs to the compiler, not the standard) but in "
"practice compilers keep it stable for years."
msgstr ""
"默认 Rust 结构体的布局、Rust 函数的调用约定、`Vec`、`String` 和 trait "
"对象的布局，以及符号名的修饰方式，都可能在编译器版本之间改变，甚至在使用不同标志的两次构建之间改变。Rust "
"不做任何承诺，而且由于字段重排，它在实践中确实会变。C++ 在理论上处境类似（ABI 属于编译器而不是标准），但实践中编译器会让它保持多年稳定。"

#: src/engine/hot-reload-and-plugins.md:29
msgid "The consequences:"
msgstr "其后果是："

#: src/engine/hot-reload-and-plugins.md:31
msgid ""
"A Rust dynamic library and the program that loads it must be built **by the "
"same compiler, with the same flags, from the same dependency versions** if "
"they exchange Rust types. For hot reloading during development, that holds "
"automatically: you are rebuilding the same workspace."
msgstr ""
"如果 Rust 动态库和加载它的程序之间交换 Rust "
"类型，它们必须**由同一个编译器、用相同的标志、基于相同的依赖版本**构建。对于开发期间的热重载，这一点自动成立：你重新构建的是同一个工作空间；"

#: src/engine/hot-reload-and-plugins.md:35
msgid ""
"For **plugins built separately** (by users, by other teams, months later), "
"the interface must use the C ABI: `extern \"C\"` functions and `#[repr(C)]` "
"types, exactly as in the [FFI chapter](../systems/ffi.md). Crates such as "
"[abi_stable](https://docs.rs/abi_stable) and "
"[stabby](https://docs.rs/stabby) generate stable-ABI versions of `Vec`, "
"`String`, trait objects and more, so a plugin interface does not have to be "
"written in raw C types."
msgstr ""
"对于**单独构建的插件**（由用户、其他团队或几个月后构建），接口必须使用 C ABI：`extern \"C\"` 函数和 `#[repr(C)]` "
"类型，与 [FFI "
"一章](../systems/ffi.md)完全相同。[abi_stable](https://docs.rs/abi_stable) 和 "
"[stabby](https://docs.rs/stabby) 等 crate 生成 `Vec`、`String`、trait 对象等的稳定 ABI "
"版本，因此插件接口不必用原始 C 类型编写。"

#: src/engine/hot-reload-and-plugins.md:43
msgid "Rust has two library crate types for this:"
msgstr "Rust 为此提供了两种库 crate 类型："

